-- ============================================================
-- mlr1: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (United Kingdom), regulations 8 to 32 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a business that is a relevant person under the Regulations (a bank, an accountancy or legal firm, an estate agent, a money service business and so on) and its
-- compliance officer.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask: do the Regulations apply to
-- me, when must I apply customer due diligence measures, what measures must I apply, what must I have in place and keep, and by when.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as the person would be asked.  A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot
-- answer without it answers NOTHING.  A business of several kinds asks once for each kind (the kind is asked as one choice).  A list of several items (for example the
-- activities in Schedule 2) is asked one item at a time.  Money is in pounds sterling.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulations themselves give; NOTHING means the Regulations do not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md,
-- "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (mlr1)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THERE IS NO SEAT FOR AN OFFICIAL.  Regulations 16, 16A, 17 and 25 address the Treasury, the Home Office and the supervisory authorities; they are in layer 1 and reach the
-- business only through the questions below.
--
-- Wiring (not questions): the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.

DECLARE `mlr1 my answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `mlr1 my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

§ `Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 -- my questions`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Do the Regulations apply to me? (regulations 8 to 15)`
-- Situation: asked by a business, or its compliance officer, before it knows which Parts of the Regulations bind it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 8, am I a relevant person to whom the Regulations apply?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `I act in the course of business carried on by me in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act in the course of a business that you carry on in the United Kingdom?
      `I come within the exclusions in regulation 15` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Do you come within the exclusions in regulation 15?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 8, am I a relevant person` IS
    `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) `I act in the course of business carried on by me in the United Kingdom` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I come within the exclusions in regulation 15`)

@export Under regulation 8(3), am I a relevant person for the purposes of this particular regulation?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `I act in the course of business carried on by me in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you act in the course of a business that you carry on in the United Kingdom?
      `I come within the exclusions in regulation 15` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Do you come within the exclusions in regulation 15?
      `the number of the regulation I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which regulation are you asking about? Give its number, for example 19.
      `the letter after the number, if any` IS A STRING @desc Is there a letter after the number, for example A in 19A? Give it, or "" if there is none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 8(3), am I a relevant person for the purposes of this particular regulation` IS
    `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) `I act in the course of business carried on by me in the United Kingdom` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I come within the exclusions in regulation 15`) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF `the number of the regulation I ask about`, `the letter after the number, if any`)

@export Under regulation 9, am I regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `A would otherwise be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: A would otherwise be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office? (true or false)
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom? (true or false)
      `A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling? (true or false)
      `at least one piece of remote gambling equipment is situated in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: at least one piece of remote gambling equipment is situated in Great Britain? (true or false)
      `no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 9, am I regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS
    `reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` `A would otherwise be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` (`reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom`) (`reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` `A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling` `at least one piece of remote gambling equipment is situated in Great Britain` `no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there`)

@export Under regulation 10(1), am I a credit institution?
GIVEN `the person is a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation? (true or false)
      `the person is a branch located in the United Kingdom of such an institution, or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a branch located in the United Kingdom of such an institution, or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country? (true or false)
      `it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public? (true or false)
      `it grants credits for its own account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it grants credits for its own account? (true or false)
      `it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 10(1), am I a credit institution` IS
    `reg 10(1) the person is a credit institution` `the person is a credit institution as defined in Article 4.1(1) of the capital requirements regulation` `the person is a branch located in the United Kingdom of such an institution, or of an equivalent institution whose head office is in a third country` `it accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` `it grants credits for its own account` `it bids directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients`

@export Under regulation 10(2)(a), am I a financial institution because I am an undertaking that carries out a listed activity?
GIVEN `the person is an undertaking, including a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is an undertaking, including a money service business? (true or false)
      `regulation 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `one of the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2` IS A `Listed activity` @desc Which one of the activities in Schedule 2 do you carry out? (ask again for each)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 10(2)(a), am I a financial institution because I am an undertaking that carries out a listed activity` IS
    `reg 10(2)(a) the person falls within regulation 10(2)(a)` `the person is an undertaking, including a money service business` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 10(3) the undertaking is an institution referred to in paragraph (3)`) (LIST `one of the activities the undertaking carries out among those of Schedule 2`)

@export Under regulation 10(2)(b), am I a financial institution because I am an insurance undertaking?
GIVEN `the person is an authorised person with permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is an authorised person with permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance? (true or false)
      `it is carrying out or effecting a contract of long-term insurance that is not a reinsurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is carrying out or effecting a contract of long-term insurance that is not a reinsurance contract? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 10(2)(b), am I a financial institution because I am an insurance undertaking` IS
    `reg 10(2)(b) the person is a financial institution as an insurance undertaking` `the person is an authorised person with permission under Part 4A of FSMA to carry out or effect contracts of insurance` `it is carrying out or effecting a contract of long-term insurance that is not a reinsurance contract`

@export Under regulation 10(2)(c), am I a financial institution because I am an investment firm?
GIVEN `its regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: its regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis? (true or false)
      `the person falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of investment firm in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of investment firm in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order? (true or false)
      `it is providing investment services or performing investment activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing investment services or performing investment activities? (true or false)
      `it is bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 10(2)(c), am I a financial institution because I am an investment firm` IS
    `reg 10(2)(c) the person is a financial institution as an investment firm` `its regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis` `the person falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of investment firm in article 3(1) of the Regulated Activities Order` `it is providing investment services or performing investment activities` `it is bidding directly in auctions in accordance with the emission allowance auctioning regulation or the UK auctioning regulations on behalf of its clients`

@export Under regulation 11(a), am I an auditor?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or individual? (true or false)
      `the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006? (true or false)
      `it is carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act? (true or false)
      `the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014? (true or false)
      `it is carrying out an audit required by that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is carrying out an audit required by that Act? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 11(a), am I an auditor` IS
    `reg 11(a) the person is an auditor` `the person is a firm or individual` `the person is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of the Companies Act 2006` `it is carrying out statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of that Act` `the person is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` `it is carrying out an audit required by that Act`

@export Under regulation 11(b), am I an insolvency practitioner?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or individual? (true or false)
      `it acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 11(b), am I an insolvency practitioner` IS
    `reg 11(b) the person is an insolvency practitioner` `the person is a firm or individual` `it acts as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`

@export Under regulation 11(c), am I an external accountant?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons? (true or false)
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing such services? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 11(c), am I an external accountant` IS
    `reg 11(c) the person is an external accountant` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it by way of business provides accountancy services to other persons` `it is providing such services`

@export Under regulation 11(d), am I a tax adviser?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party? (true or false)
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing such services? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 11(d), am I a tax adviser` IS
    `reg 11(d) the person is a tax adviser` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it by way of business provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons, whether provided directly or through a third party` `it is providing such services`

@export Under regulation 12(1), am I an independent legal professional?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons? (true or false)
      `it assists in the planning or execution of the transaction, or otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it assists in the planning or execution of the transaction, or otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction? (true or false)
      `what the financial or real property transaction concerns` IS A `reg 12(1) what the transaction concerns` @desc Which applies: what the financial or real property transaction concerns?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 12(1), am I an independent legal professional` IS
    `reg 12(1) the person is an independent legal professional` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons` `it assists in the planning or execution of the transaction, or otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction` `what the financial or real property transaction concerns`

@export Under regulation 12(2), am I a trust or company service provider?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `one of the services it provides by way of business to other persons` IS A `reg 12(2) service` @desc Which applies: one of the services it provides by way of business to other persons?
      `where it acts as a nominee shareholder, the person it acts for is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: where it acts as a nominee shareholder, the person it acts for is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market? (true or false)
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing such services? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 12(2), am I a trust or company service provider` IS
    `reg 12(2) the person is a trust or company service provider` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` (LIST `one of the services it provides by way of business to other persons`) `where it acts as a nominee shareholder, the person it acts for is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` `it is providing such services`

@export Under regulation 13(1), am I an estate agent?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it, or its employees, carry out estate agency work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it, or its employees, carry out estate agency work? (true or false)
      `the work is being carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the work is being carried out? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 13(1), am I an estate agent` IS
    `reg 13(1) the person is an estate agent` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it, or its employees, carry out estate agency work` `the work is being carried out`

@export Under regulation 13(3), am I a letting agent?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it, or its employees, carry out letting agency work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it, or its employees, carry out letting agency work? (true or false)
      `it is carrying out such work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is carrying out such work? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 13(3), am I a letting agent` IS
    `reg 13(3) the person is a letting agent` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it, or its employees, carry out letting agency work` `it is carrying out such work`

@export Under regulation 14(1)(a), am I a high value dealer?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole trader` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole trader? (true or false)
      `it by way of business trades in goods, including as an auctioneer dealing in goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it by way of business trades in goods, including as an auctioneer dealing in goods? (true or false)
      `the total of the payments in cash it makes or receives in respect of the transaction, in single or linked operations, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the total of the payments in cash it makes or receives in respect of the transaction, in single or linked operations, in pounds sterling? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 14(1)(a), am I a high value dealer` IS
    `reg 14(1)(a) the person is a high value dealer` `the person is a firm or sole trader` `it by way of business trades in goods, including as an auctioneer dealing in goods` `the total of the payments in cash it makes or receives in respect of the transaction, in single or linked operations, in pounds sterling`

@export Under regulation 14(1)(b), am I a casino?
GIVEN `the person holds a casino operating licence, that is a licence within section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person holds a casino operating licence, that is a licence within section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 14(1)(b), am I a casino` IS
    `reg 14(1)(b) the person is a casino` `the person holds a casino operating licence, that is a licence within section 65(2)(a) of the Gambling Act 2005`

@export Under regulation 14(1)(d)(i), am I an art market participant because I trade in works of art or act as an intermediary?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `it by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art? (true or false)
      `the value of the transaction, or of a series of linked transactions, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the value of the transaction, or of a series of linked transactions, in pounds sterling? (a number)
      `regulation 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 14(1)(d)(i), am I an art market participant because I trade in works of art or act as an intermediary` IS
    `reg 14(1)(d)(i) the person is an art market participant as a trader or intermediary` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` `it by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art` `the value of the transaction, or of a series of linked transactions, in pounds sterling` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 14(3) the firm or sole practitioner is an art market participant in relation to the sale`)

@export Under regulation 14A(1), am I a cryptoasset exchange provider?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `one of the services it provides by way of business` IS A `reg 14A(1) service` @desc Which applies: one of the services it provides by way of business?
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing such services? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 14A(1), am I a cryptoasset exchange provider` IS
    `reg 14A(1) the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` (LIST `one of the services it provides by way of business`) `it is providing such services`

@export Under regulation 14A(2), am I a custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is a firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `one of the things it provides services by way of business to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer` IS A `reg 14A(2) what is safeguarded` @desc Which applies: one of the things it provides services by way of business to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer?
      `it is providing such services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is providing such services? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 14A(2), am I a custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 14A(2) the person is a custodian wallet provider` `the person is a firm or sole practitioner` (LIST `one of the things it provides services by way of business to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer`) `it is providing such services`

@export Under regulation 15(3), do I engage in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis?
GIVEN `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds sterling? (a number)
      `the largest number of transactions exceeding the transaction size that the financial activity involves for any one customer` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the largest number of transactions exceeding the transaction size that the financial activity involves for any one customer? (a number)
      `the person's annual turnover from the financial activity, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the person's annual turnover from the financial activity, in pounds sterling? (a number)
      `the person's total annual turnover, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the person's total annual turnover, in pounds sterling? (a number)
      `the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity? (true or false)
      `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money, or any representation of monetary value, by any means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money, or any representation of monetary value, by any means? (true or false)
      `the kind of my main activity` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business is your main activity?
      `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person? (true or false)
      `the financial activity is offered to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the financial activity is offered to the public? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 15(3), do I engage in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` IS
    `reg 15(3) the person engages in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` (LIST (`reg 15(3)(a) the turnover in respect of the financial activity is within the limit` `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds sterling`), (`reg 15(3)(b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding 1000 pounds sterling` `the largest number of transactions exceeding the transaction size that the financial activity involves for any one customer`), (`reg 15(3)(c) the financial activity does not exceed 5 per cent of the person's total annual turnover` `the person's annual turnover from the financial activity, in pounds sterling` `the person's total annual turnover, in pounds sterling`), (`reg 15(3)(d) the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity` `the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity`), (`reg 15(3)(e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money` `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money, or any representation of monetary value, by any means`), (`reg 15(3)(f) the person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)` (LIST `the kind of my main activity`)), (`reg 15(3)(g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity and is not offered to the public` `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person` `the financial activity is offered to the public`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `My risk assessment, policies, controls and records (regulations 18 to 24)`
-- Situation: asked by a business that is a relevant person, about what it must have in place and what it must keep.  There is no question for a supervisory authority: regulations 16, 16A, 17 and 25 address it, and are in layer 1 only.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 18(1), have I taken the steps that the risk assessment requires?
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject? (true or false)
      `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 18(1), have I taken the steps that the risk assessment requires` IS
    `reg 18(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject` `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks`

@export Under regulation 18(4), have I kept the written record of my risk assessment that regulation 18(4) requires?
GIVEN `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)? (true or false)
      `the record is up to date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the record is up to date? (true or false)
      `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 18(4), have I kept the written record of my risk assessment that regulation 18(4) requires` IS
    `reg 18(4) the relevant person has kept the record paragraph (4) requires` `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` `the record is up to date` `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required`

@export Under regulation 18A(1), have I taken the steps that the proliferation financing risk assessment requires?
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject? (true or false)
      `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 18A(1), have I taken the steps that the proliferation financing risk assessment requires` IS
    `reg 18A(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject` `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks`

@export Under regulation 18A(4), have I kept the written record of my proliferation financing risk assessment that regulation 18A(4) requires?
GIVEN `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)? (true or false)
      `the record is up to date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the record is up to date? (true or false)
      `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 18A(4), have I kept the written record of my proliferation financing risk assessment that regulation 18A(4) requires` IS
    `reg 18A(4) the relevant person has kept the record paragraph (4) requires` `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` `the record is up to date` `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required`

@export Under regulation 19(1), have I established, kept under review and recorded my policies, controls and procedures?
GIVEN `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)? (true or false)
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 19(1), have I established, kept under review and recorded my policies, controls and procedures` IS
    `reg 19(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business`

@export Under regulation 19A(1), have I established, kept under review and recorded my policies, controls and procedures on proliferation financing?
GIVEN `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)? (true or false)
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 19A(1), have I established, kept under review and recorded my policies, controls and procedures on proliferation financing` IS
    `reg 19A(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business`

@export Under regulation 20(1), as a parent undertaking, have I applied my group policies, controls and procedures to my subsidiaries and branches?
GIVEN `it has ensured that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings, including those located outside the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has ensured that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings, including those located outside the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations? (true or false)
      `it has ensured that those policies, controls and procedures apply to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom which carry out such an activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has ensured that those policies, controls and procedures apply to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom which carry out such an activity? (true or false)
      `it has established and maintains throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has established and maintains throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group? (true or false)
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established, of any changes made as a result of the review and update, and of the steps taken to communicate them to its subsidiary undertakings and branches` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established, of any changes made as a result of the review and update, and of the steps taken to communicate them to its subsidiary undertakings and branches? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 20(1), as a parent undertaking, have I applied my group policies, controls and procedures to my subsidiaries and branches` IS
    `reg 20(1) the relevant parent undertaking has done what paragraph (1) requires` `it has ensured that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings, including those located outside the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations` `it has ensured that those policies, controls and procedures apply to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom which carry out such an activity` `it has established and maintains throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group` `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)` `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established, of any changes made as a result of the review and update, and of the steps taken to communicate them to its subsidiary undertakings and branches`

@export Under regulation 21(1), have I put in place the compliance officer, screening and independent audit that regulation 21(1) requires?
GIVEN `it has appointed one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has appointed one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations? (true or false)
      `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it before the appointment is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it before the appointment is made? (true or false)
      `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it during the course of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it during the course of the appointment? (true or false)
      `it has established an independent audit function with the responsibility to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has established an independent audit function with the responsibility to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures? (true or false)
      `the independent audit function has the responsibility to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the independent audit function has the responsibility to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures? (true or false)
      `the independent audit function has the responsibility to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the independent audit function has the responsibility to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations? (true or false)
      `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person? (true or false)
      `it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 21(1), have I put in place the compliance officer, screening and independent audit that regulation 21(1) requires` IS
    `reg 21(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` `it has appointed one individual who is a member of the board of directors (or if there is no board, of its equivalent management body) or of its senior management as the officer responsible for the relevant person's compliance with these Regulations` `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it before the appointment is made` `it carries out screening of relevant employees appointed by it during the course of the appointment` `it has established an independent audit function with the responsibility to examine and evaluate the adequacy and effectiveness of its policies, controls and procedures` `the independent audit function has the responsibility to make recommendations in relation to those policies, controls and procedures` `the independent audit function has the responsibility to monitor the relevant person's compliance with those recommendations` `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (1): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` `it is appropriate with regard to the size and nature of its business`

@export Under regulation 21(3), have I appointed a nominated officer?
GIVEN `an individual in the relevant person's firm has been appointed as a nominated officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: an individual in the relevant person's firm has been appointed as a nominated officer? (true or false)
      `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 21(3), have I appointed a nominated officer` IS
    `reg 21(3) the relevant person has appointed a nominated officer` `an individual in the relevant person's firm has been appointed as a nominated officer` `paragraph (6) disapplies paragraph (3): the relevant person is an individual who neither employs nor acts in association with any other person`

@export Under regulation 21(4), did I tell my supervisory authority of the nominated officer within 14 days of the appointment?
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date of the appointment?
      `the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 21(4), did I tell my supervisory authority of the nominated officer within 14 days of the appointment` IS
    `reg 21(4) the relevant person informed its supervisory authority within 14 days of the appointment` `the date of the appointment` `the date on which the relevant person informed its supervisory authority`

@export Under regulation 23(1), did I tell the FCA within 28 days that I had begun to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider?
GIVEN `the date on which the authorised person began to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the authorised person began to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider?
      `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 23(1), did I tell the FCA within 28 days that I had begun to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS
    `reg 23(1) the authorised person informed the FCA in time` `the date on which the authorised person began to act as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA`

@export Under regulation 23(3), did I tell the FCA within 28 days that I had ceased to act?
GIVEN `the date on which the authorised person ceased to act` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the authorised person ceased to act?
      `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 23(3), did I tell the FCA within 28 days that I had ceased to act` IS
    `reg 23(3) the authorised person informed the FCA of ceasing to act within 28 days` `the date on which the authorised person ceased to act` `the date on which the authorised person informed the FCA`

@export Under regulation 23(3A), did I give the FCA the details of a change or the correction of an inaccuracy within 30 days?
GIVEN `the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy?
      `the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 23(3A), did I give the FCA the details of a change or the correction of an inaccuracy within 30 days` IS
    `reg 23(3A) A provided the FCA with the details or correction within 30 days beginning with the date` `the date of the occurrence of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy` `the date on which A provided the FCA with the details or correction`

@export Under regulation 24(1), have I made my employees aware of the law and trained them, and kept a record of the training?
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations? (true or false)
      `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing? (true or false)
      `it maintains a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular of the training given to its relevant employees and to any such agents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it maintains a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular of the training given to its relevant employees and to any such agents? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 24(1), have I made my employees aware of the law and trained them, and kept a record of the training` IS
    `reg 24(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are made aware of the law relating to money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing, and to the requirements of data protection, which are relevant to the implementation of these Regulations` `it has taken appropriate measures to ensure that its relevant employees, and any agents it uses whose work is of a kind mentioned in paragraph (2), are regularly given training in how to recognise and deal with transactions and other activities or situations which may be related to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing` `it maintains a record in writing of the measures taken under sub-paragraph (a), and in particular of the training given to its relevant employees and to any such agents`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Approval of beneficial owners, officers and managers (regulation 26)`
-- Situation: asked by a firm or sole practitioner of a kind named in regulation 26(2), about the people who own or run it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 26(1), may this person be a beneficial owner, officer or manager of my firm, or act as a sole practitioner?
GIVEN `the person is the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm, or a sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person is the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm, or a sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `the kind of firm or sole practitioner` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business is the firm or sole practitioner?
      `the person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
      `regulation 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 26(1), may this person be a beneficial owner, officer or manager of my firm, or act as a sole practitioner` IS
    `reg 26(1) the person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of the relevant firm, or the relevant sole practitioner` `the person is the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm, or a sole practitioner` (`reg 26(2) the kind of firm or sole practitioner is within this paragraph` `the kind of firm or sole practitioner`) `the person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)`) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)`)

@export Under regulation 26(4), may this person be appointed, or continue to act, as an officer or manager of my firm?
GIVEN `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid? (true or false)
      `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 26(4), may this person be appointed, or continue to act, as an officer or manager of my firm` IS
    `reg 26(4) the person may be appointed, or continue to act, as an officer or manager of the relevant firm` `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined`

@export Under regulation 26(10)(a), did I tell my supervisory authority of my conviction within 30 days?
GIVEN `regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the date on which P was convicted` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which P was convicted?
      `the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 26(10)(a), did I tell my supervisory authority of my conviction within 30 days` IS
    `reg 26(10)(a) P informed the supervisory authority within 30 days of the conviction` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation`) `the date on which P was convicted` `the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P`

@export Under regulation 26(10)(b), did my firm tell its supervisory authority of the conviction within 30 days of becoming aware of it?
GIVEN `regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction?
      `the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 26(10)(b), did my firm tell its supervisory authority of the conviction within 30 days of becoming aware of it` IS
    `reg 26(10)(b) the relevant firm informed its supervisory authority within 30 days of becoming aware of the conviction` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation`) `the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction` `the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `When must I apply customer due diligence? (regulation 27)`
-- Situation: asked by a relevant person about one customer, or one transaction, at the moment of dealing.  Money is in pounds sterling.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 27(1), must I apply customer due diligence measures because I am establishing a business relationship, carrying out an occasional transfer of funds over 800 pounds, suspect money laundering or terrorist financing, or doubt earlier identification documents?
GIVEN `regulation 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is there a business relationship with the customer, as regulation 4 describes? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the relevant person establishes that business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you establishing that business relationship now?
      `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds sterling, taking linked operations together?
      `the transaction is paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction paid in cash?
      `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction carried out as part of a business relationship?
      `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction a transfer of funds within Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation?
      `I suspect money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suspect money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `I doubt the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: I doubt the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(1), must I apply customer due diligence measures on the general occasions` IS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST (`reg 27(1)(a) the relevant person establishes a business relationship` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`) `the relevant person establishes that business relationship`), (`reg 27(1)(b) the relevant person carries out an occasional transaction that is a transfer of funds exceeding 800 pounds` (Transaction OF `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling`, `the transaction is paid in cash`, `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship`, `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation`)), (`reg 27(1)(c) the relevant person suspects money laundering or terrorist financing` `I suspect money laundering or terrorist financing`), (`reg 27(1)(d) the relevant person doubts the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained` `I doubt the veracity or adequacy of documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification`))

@export Under regulation 27(2), must I apply customer due diligence measures because of an occasional transaction of 12,000 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds sterling, taking linked operations together?
      `the transaction is paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction paid in cash?
      `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction carried out as part of a business relationship?
      `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction a transfer of funds within Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(2), must I apply customer due diligence measures to an occasional transaction of 12000 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(2) the relevant person carries out an occasional transaction of 12000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (Transaction OF `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling`, `the transaction is paid in cash`, `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship`, `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation`)

@export Under regulation 27(3) and (4), must I, as a high value dealer, apply customer due diligence measures because of an occasional transaction in cash of 10,000 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds sterling, taking linked operations together?
      `the transaction is paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction paid in cash?
      `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction carried out as part of a business relationship?
      `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction a transfer of funds within Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation?
      `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party? (true or false)
      `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction into a bank account for the benefit of the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction into a bank account for the benefit of the other party? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(3), must I, as a high value dealer, apply customer due diligence measures to an occasional transaction in cash of 10000 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(3) the high value dealer carries out an occasional transaction in cash of 10000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (Transaction OF `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling`, `the transaction is paid in cash`, `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship`, `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation`) (`reg 27(4) the transaction is a transaction in cash for the purposes of paragraph (3)` `the transaction is paid in cash` `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction to a person other than the other party for the benefit of the other party` `cash is paid by or on behalf of a party to the transaction into a bank account for the benefit of the other party`)

@export Under regulation 27(5) to (7), must I, as a casino, apply customer due diligence measures to this transaction of 2,000 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds sterling, taking linked operations together?
      `the kind of casino transaction` IS A `reg 27(6) kind of transaction` @desc What kind of transaction is it: a wager, a purchase of tokens, a payment for a gaming machine, a deposit for remote gambling, a collection of winnings, or another?
      `the winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected but are being re-used in the transaction, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected but are being re-used in the transaction, in pounds sterling? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(5), must I, as a casino, apply customer due diligence measures to a transaction of 2000 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(5) the casino carries out a transaction within paragraph (6) of 2000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (`reg 27(6) the transaction is within this paragraph` `the kind of casino transaction`) (`reg 27(7) the amount of the transaction for the purposes of paragraph (5)` `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` `the winnings from a previous transaction which had not been collected but are being re-used in the transaction, in pounds sterling`)

@export Under regulation 27(7A), must I, as a letting agent, apply customer due diligence measures because of this letting?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction carried out as part of a business relationship?
      `the transaction consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the transaction consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land? (true or false)
      `the term of the letting, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the term of the letting, in months? (a number)
      `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(7A), must I, as a letting agent, apply customer due diligence measures to this letting` IS
    `reg 27(7A) the letting agent concludes an agreement for the letting of land for a month or more at a monthly rent of 10000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (Transaction OF 0, FALSE, `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship`, FALSE) `the transaction consists of the conclusion of an agreement for the letting of land` `the term of the letting, in months` `the highest monthly rent, or its monthly equivalent, during any part of the term, in pounds sterling`

@export Under regulation 27(7C)(a), must I, as an art market participant, apply customer due diligence measures because of a trade in a work of art of 10,000 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transaction, in pounds sterling, taking linked operations together?
      `the transaction is paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction paid in cash?
      `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction carried out as part of a business relationship?
      `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction a transfer of funds within Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation?
      `the transaction is a trade in a work of art, carried out or acted in respect of by the firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the transaction is a trade in a work of art, carried out or acted in respect of by the firm or sole practitioner? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(7C)(a), must I, as an art market participant, apply customer due diligence measures to a trade in a work of art of 10000 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(7C)(a) the art market participant carries out or acts in respect of an occasional transaction in a work of art of 10000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (Transaction OF `the value of the transaction, linked operations taken together, in pounds sterling`, `the transaction is paid in cash`, `the transaction is carried out as part of a business relationship`, `the transaction is a transfer of funds under the funds transfer regulation`) `the transaction is a trade in a work of art, carried out or acted in respect of by the firm or sole practitioner`

@export Under regulation 27(7C)(b), must I, as an art market participant operating a freeport, apply customer due diligence measures because of works of art stored for a person worth 10,000 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the art market participant is the operator of a freeport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the art market participant is the operator of a freeport? (true or false)
      `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, in pounds sterling? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(7C)(b), must I, as an art market participant operating a freeport, apply customer due diligence measures to storage of works of art worth 10000 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(7C)(b) the art market participant is the operator of a freeport storing works of art of 10000 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) `the art market participant is the operator of a freeport` `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or series of linked persons, in pounds sterling`

@export Under regulation 27(7D), must I, as a cryptoasset exchange provider, apply customer due diligence measures to a transaction carried out using my machine?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the person operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the person operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets? (true or false)
      `the transaction is carried out using that machine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the transaction is carried out using that machine? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(7D), must I, as a cryptoasset exchange provider, apply customer due diligence measures to a transaction carried out using my machine` IS
    `reg 27(7D) the cryptoasset exchange provider carries out a transaction using its machine` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) `the person operates a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money, or money for cryptoassets` `the transaction is carried out using that machine`

@export Under regulation 27(7E), must I, as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, apply customer due diligence measures to a cryptoasset transfer of 800 pounds or more?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the kind of cryptoasset transfer` IS A `Kind of cryptoasset transfer` @desc What kind of cryptoasset transfer is it: an inter-cryptoasset business transfer, or an unhosted wallet transfer?
      `the value of the cryptoasset transfer, linked transfers taken together, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for: the value of the cryptoasset transfer, linked transfers taken together, in pounds sterling? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(7E), must I, as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, apply customer due diligence measures to a cryptoasset transfer of 800 pounds or more` IS
    `reg 27(7E) the cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider carries out a cryptoasset transfer of 800 pounds or more` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) (`Cryptoasset transfer` OF `the kind of cryptoasset transfer`, `the value of the cryptoasset transfer, linked transfers taken together, in pounds sterling`)

@export Under regulation 27(8), must I apply customer due diligence measures to an existing customer now?
GIVEN `the relevant person has a legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing information that is relevant to the risk assessment for that customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person has a legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing information that is relevant to the risk assessment for that customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer? (true or false)
      `the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015? (true or false)
      `it is appropriate, on a risk based approach, to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers at this time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is appropriate, on a risk based approach, to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers at this time? (true or false)
      `the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 27(8), must I apply customer due diligence measures to an existing customer now` IS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST (`reg 27(8)(za) the relevant person has a legal duty to contact an existing customer to review beneficial ownership information` `the relevant person has a legal duty in the course of the calendar year to contact an existing customer for the purpose of reviewing information that is relevant to the risk assessment for that customer and relates to the beneficial ownership of the customer`), (`reg 27(8)(zb) the relevant person has to contact an existing customer to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015` `the relevant person has to contact an existing customer in order to fulfil a duty under the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015`), (`reg 27(8)(a) it is an appropriate time to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers` `it is appropriate, on a risk based approach, to apply customer due diligence measures to existing customers at this time`), (`reg 27(8)(b) the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer have changed` `the relevant person becomes aware that the circumstances of an existing customer relevant to its risk assessment for that customer have changed`))

