-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What customer due diligence measures must I apply? (regulation 28)`
-- Situation: asked once regulation 27 requires measures.  Each question first asks whether regulation 27 requires them (Yes, No or I am not sure) and builds the answer regulation 28(1) needs from it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 28(2)(a), must I identify the customer?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(2)(a), must I identify the customer` IS
    `reg 28(2)(a) the relevant person must identify the customer` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) `the identity of that customer is known to, and has been verified by, the relevant person`

@export Under regulation 28(2)(b), must I verify the customer's identity?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(2)(b), must I verify the customer's identity` IS
    `reg 28(2)(b) the relevant person must verify the customer's identity` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) `the customer's identity has already been verified by the relevant person`

@export Under regulation 28(2)(c), must I assess the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(2)(c), must I assess the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction` IS
    `reg 28(2)(c) the relevant person must assess the purpose and intended nature of the business relationship or occasional transaction` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`))

@export Under regulation 28(3)(a), must I obtain and verify the name, registration number and addresses of a customer that is a body corporate?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 3(1) the entity is a body corporate` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is the customer a body corporate? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(3)(a), must I obtain and verify the name, registration number and addresses of a customer that is a body corporate` IS
    `reg 28(3)(a) the relevant person must obtain and verify the particulars of the body corporate` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 3(1) the entity is a body corporate`)

@export Under regulation 28(3)(a), what particulars of a body corporate must I obtain and verify?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(3)(a), what particulars of a body corporate must I obtain and verify` IS
    `reg 28(3)(a) the particulars the relevant person must obtain and verify`

@export Under regulation 28(3)(b), must I take reasonable measures to determine and verify the law, constitution and management of a customer that is a body corporate?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 3(1) the entity is a body corporate` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is the customer a body corporate? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(3)(b), must I take reasonable measures to determine and verify the law, constitution and management of a customer that is a body corporate` IS
    `reg 28(3)(b) the relevant person must take reasonable measures to determine and verify the law, constitution and management of the body corporate` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 3(1) the entity is a body corporate`) `paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market`

@export Under regulation 28(4), must I identify the beneficial owner and take reasonable measures to verify their identity?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `the customer is beneficially owned by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the customer is beneficially owned by another person? (true or false)
      `paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(4), must I identify the beneficial owner and take reasonable measures to verify their identity` IS
    `reg 28(4) the relevant person must identify the beneficial owner and take reasonable measures to verify the beneficial owner's identity` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) `the customer is beneficially owned by another person` `paragraph (5) applies: the customer is a company which is listed on a regulated market`

@export Under regulation 28(10), must I verify that a person acting for the customer is authorised, identify them and verify their identity?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(10), must I verify that a person acting for the customer is authorised, identify them and verify their identity` IS
    `reg 28(10) the relevant person must verify A's authority, identify A and verify A's identity` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) `a person (“A”) purports to act on behalf of the customer`

@export Under regulation 28(11), must I conduct ongoing monitoring of the business relationship?
GIVEN `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Does regulation 27 require you to apply customer due diligence measures on this occasion? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(11), must I conduct ongoing monitoring of the business relationship` IS
    `reg 28(11) the relevant person must conduct ongoing monitoring of a business relationship` (`reg 28(1) this regulation applies` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `I am required by regulation 27 to apply customer due diligence measures`)) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`)

@export Under regulation 28(14), am I still required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures after a disclosure that would make continuing a tipping-off offence?
GIVEN `a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer? (true or false)
      `the relevant person makes a disclosure required by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person makes a disclosure required by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002? (true or false)
      `continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 or section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 or section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(14), am I still required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures after a disclosure that would make continuing a tipping-off offence` IS
    `reg 28(14) the relevant person is required to continue to apply customer due diligence measures under paragraph (2) or (10)` (`reg 28(15) this paragraph applies` `a relevant person has taken customer due diligence measures in relation to a customer` `the relevant person makes a disclosure required by Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` `continuing to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to that customer would result in the commission of an offence by the relevant person under section 21D of the Terrorism Act 2000 or section 333A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`)

@export Under regulation 28(16), am I able to demonstrate to my supervisory authority that the extent of my measures is appropriate to the risks?
GIVEN `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1)? (true or false)
      `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47? (true or false)
      `paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(16), am I able to demonstrate to my supervisory authority that the extent of my measures is appropriate to the risks` IS
    `reg 28(16) the relevant person is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures is appropriate` `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by the risk assessment carried out under regulation 18(1)` `it is able to demonstrate to its supervisory authority that the extent of the measures it has taken is appropriate in view of the risks identified by its supervisory authority and in information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47` `paragraph (17) disapplies paragraph (16): the relevant person is the National Savings Bank or the Director of Savings`

@export Under regulation 28(18)(a), is the identity verified on the basis of documents or information from a reliable source independent of the person?
GIVEN `the documents or information are obtained from a reliable source` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the documents or information are obtained from a reliable source? (true or false)
      `that source is independent of the person whose identity is being verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: that source is independent of the person whose identity is being verified? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 28(18)(a), is the identity verified on the basis of documents or information from a reliable source independent of the person` IS
    `reg 28(18)(a) the identity is verified` `the documents or information are obtained from a reliable source` `that source is independent of the person whose identity is being verified`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Additional measures for credit institutions and financial institutions (regulation 29)`
-- Situation: asked by a credit institution or financial institution, which regulation 29 adds to regulation 28.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 29(1), does regulation 29 apply to me in addition to regulation 28?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 29(1), does regulation 29 apply to me in addition to regulation 28` IS
    `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`)

@export Under regulation 29(6), may I set up an anonymous account, passbook or safe-deposit box?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 29(6), may I set up an anonymous account, passbook or safe-deposit box` IS
    `reg 29(6) the relevant person may set up an anonymous account, an anonymous passbook or an anonymous safe-deposit box for a new or existing customer` (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`))

@export Under regulation 29(8) and (9), may I issue shares evidenced by a share certificate?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of business do you carry on?
      `the relevant person is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001? (true or false)
      `the date on which the relevant person is authorised` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the relevant person is authorised?
      `the date on which the application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made?
      `the date on which that application was determined` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which that application was determined?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 29(8), may I issue shares evidenced by a share certificate` IS
    `reg 29(8) the relevant person may issue shares evidenced by a share certificate or other documentary evidence of entitlement` (`reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`)) `the relevant person is an open-ended investment company within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001` `the date on which the relevant person is authorised` (`reg 29(9) paragraph (8) does not apply to the open-ended investment company` `the date on which the application for an authorisation order under regulation 12 of the Open-ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 was made` `the date on which that application was determined`)

@export Under regulation 29(15), did my customer keep the records of a pooled-account payment for the whole five years?
GIVEN `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete?
      `the last day on which the customer maintained the records of that payment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the last day on which the customer maintained the records of that payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 29(15), did my customer keep the records of a pooled-account payment for the whole five years` IS
    `reg 29(15) the customer maintained the records of the payment for the whole period of five years` `the date on which the customer knows, or has reasonable grounds to believe, that the payment is complete` `the last day on which the customer maintained the records of that payment`

