§§ `Timing of verification, insolvent bank customers, register discrepancies, ceasing transactions and trustees of debt issues (regulations 30 to 32)`
-- Situation: asked by a relevant person that is verifying a customer, reporting a discrepancy in a register, or unable to complete the measures.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


@export Under regulation 30(3), may I complete the verification during the establishment of the business relationship?
GIVEN `the verification is completed as soon as practicable after contact is first established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the verification is completed as soon as practicable after contact is first established? (true or false)
      `this is necessary not to interrupt the normal conduct of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: this is necessary not to interrupt the normal conduct of business? (true or false)
      `there is little risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: there is little risk of money laundering and terrorist financing? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 30(3), may I complete the verification during the establishment of the business relationship` IS
    `reg 30(3) verification may be completed during the establishment of a business relationship` `the verification is completed as soon as practicable after contact is first established` `this is necessary not to interrupt the normal conduct of business` `there is little risk of money laundering and terrorist financing`

@export Under regulation 30(4), may a credit institution or financial institution verify the identity of a customer opening an account after the account has been opened?
GIVEN `the kind of business I carry on` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which applies: the kind of business I carry on?
      `the verification is of the identity of a customer opening an account, any person purporting to act on behalf of the customer and any beneficial owner of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the verification is of the identity of a customer opening an account, any person purporting to act on behalf of the customer and any beneficial owner of the customer? (true or false)
      `there are adequate safeguards in place to ensure that no transactions are carried out by or on behalf of the customer before verification has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: there are adequate safeguards in place to ensure that no transactions are carried out by or on behalf of the customer before verification has been completed? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 30(4), may a credit institution or financial institution verify the identity of a customer opening an account after the account has been opened` IS
    `reg 30(4) verification may take place after the account has been opened` (LIST `the kind of business I carry on`) `the verification is of the identity of a customer opening an account, any person purporting to act on behalf of the customer and any beneficial owner of the customer` `there are adequate safeguards in place to ensure that no transactions are carried out by or on behalf of the customer before verification has been completed`

@export Under regulation 30ZA(5), is this customer an insolvent bank customer?
GIVEN `the credit institution is reasonably satisfied that the customer was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the credit institution is reasonably satisfied that the customer was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank? (true or false)
      `the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer?
      `the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank` IS A DATE @desc What is the date for: the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 30ZA(5), is this customer an insolvent bank customer` IS
    `reg 30ZA(5) the customer is an insolvent bank customer` `the credit institution is reasonably satisfied that the customer was a customer of an insolvent bank at the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank` `the date on which the credit institution begins to establish a business relationship with the customer` `the insolvency date in respect of that insolvent bank`

@export Under regulation 30A(3), to whom must I report a material discrepancy?
GIVEN `the type of customer the discrepancy relates to` IS A `reg 30A(1) type of customer` @desc Which applies: the type of customer the discrepancy relates to?
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 30A(3) person to whom a material discrepancy is reported`
DECIDE `Under regulation 30A(3), to whom must I report a material discrepancy` IS
    `reg 30A(3) the person to whom the material discrepancy must be reported` `the type of customer the discrepancy relates to`

@export Under regulation 31(1)(a), may I carry out a transaction through a bank account with a customer whose due diligence I cannot complete?
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28? (true or false)
      `regulation 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 31(1)(a), may I carry out a transaction through a bank account with a customer whose due diligence I cannot complete` IS
    `reg 31(1)(a) the relevant person may carry out a transaction through a bank account with the customer or on behalf of the customer` `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 31(2) paragraph (1)(a) does not prevent the repayment of the money deposited`) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply`) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply`)

@export Under regulation 31(1)(b), may I establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with a customer, otherwise than through a bank account, whose due diligence I cannot complete?
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28? (true or false)
      `regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
      `regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 31(1)(b), may I establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with a customer, otherwise than through a bank account, whose due diligence I cannot complete` IS
    `reg 31(1)(b) the relevant person may establish a business relationship or carry out a transaction with the customer otherwise than through a bank account` `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 31(3) paragraph (1) does not apply`) (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 31(5) paragraph (1)(a) to (c) does not apply`)

@export Under regulation 31(1)(c), must I terminate an existing business relationship with a customer whose due diligence I cannot complete?
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28? (true or false)
      `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 31(1)(c), must I terminate an existing business relationship with a customer whose due diligence I cannot complete` IS
    `reg 31(1)(c) the relevant person must terminate any existing business relationship with the customer` `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) or (5) takes the case out of paragraph (1)`

@export Under regulation 31(1)(d), must I consider whether I am required to make a disclosure?
GIVEN `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28? (true or false)
      `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) takes the case out of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) takes the case out of paragraph (1)? (true or false)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 31(1)(d), must I consider whether I am required to make a disclosure` IS
    `reg 31(1)(d) the relevant person must consider whether it is required to make a disclosure` `the relevant person is unable to apply customer due diligence measures as required by regulation 28` `paragraph (1) does not apply: paragraph (3) takes the case out of paragraph (1)`

@export Under regulation 32(1), am I required to apply the measure in regulation 28(3) and (4) to the holders of debt instruments of which I am trustee?
GIVEN `the relevant person is appointed by the issuer of the instruments or securities as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person is appointed by the issuer of the instruments or securities as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities? (true or false)
      `the relevant person's customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the relevant person's customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities? (true or false)
      `regulation 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities` IS A `mlr1 my answer` @desc Is this so: regulation 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities? Answer Yes, No or I am not sure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 32(1), am I required to apply the measure in regulation 28(3) and (4) to the holders of debt instruments of which I am trustee` IS
    `reg 32(1) the relevant person is required to apply the customer due diligence measure referred to in regulation 28(3) and (4) in respect of the holders of the instruments or securities` `the relevant person is appointed by the issuer of the instruments or securities as trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` `the relevant person's customer is a trustee of an issue of such instruments or securities` (`mlr1 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 32(2) the instruments or securities are specified instruments or securities`)

-- ============================================================
-- mlr2: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692),
-- United Kingdom, regulations 33 to 45ZB -- THE SEAT LAYER.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script;
-- it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a business that is a relevant person under the Regulations (a bank, an accountancy or legal firm, an estate agent, a money
-- service business and so on) and its compliance officer, asking on facts they can state whether the Regulations apply, what customer
-- due diligence is required for a given customer or transaction, what to record and keep, and by when.  This layer phrases the rules
-- already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- THE BUSINESS IS A RELEVANT PERSON.  Every question assumes the business is a relevant person under regulation 8 (that is the seat);
-- regulation 8 itself is another part's.  Where a rule is addressed to "a relevant person", the question passes `JUST TRUE` for regulation 8's answer.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The records and MAYBE inputs the modules expect are
-- built inside each question, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--   * An answer that another regulation gives (whether a transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27, whether
--     there is a business relationship under regulation 4, whether a person is a beneficial owner under regulations 5 and 6,
--     whether a trust is listed in Schedule 3A) is asked as a yes/no fact.
--   * A day that has not come (a payment not yet made, a notice not yet given) is asked as "has it happened?" and a date.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulations themselves give; NOTHING means the Regulations do not
-- answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Regulations 36(1) and (2) (the Treasury and the FCA), 43(5) to (8) and 44(5) to (8) (information to a
-- law enforcement authority), 45(1), (10J) and (11) to (13) and 45ZB(2), (3), (4)(b) and (c), (5) to (7) and (11) (what the Commissioners
-- must or may do) address officials or authorities, or the trustees; they are in layer 1 for what they decide.  The trustees' own filing
-- duties (regulations 45(2) to (10I) and 45ZA(3) to (7)) are likewise in layer 1 only: the seat is the business as a relevant person, and
-- the seat asks no question on them (stated in NOTES.md, Seams).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The business is a relevant person (regulation 8, another part): the seat.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` MEANS JUST TRUE -- input mapping

-- A yes/no fact as the MAYBE BOOLEAN that a module expects.
GIVEN fact IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    IF fact THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- input mapping

-- A day that may not have come: "has it happened?" and the date.
GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A figure that the person may not have: 0 means none.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`mlr2 seat the amount if there is one` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `The Money Laundering Regulations 2017, regulations 33 to 45ZB -- my questions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Enhanced customer due diligence (regulation 33)`

-- reg 33(1) with 33(3).  The duty arises in any of the listed cases.  "A FATF call for action country" and "established in" are
-- asked as the facts they come to: the business relationship is with a person established in such a country, or a party to a
-- transaction that needs customer due diligence under regulation 27 is.
@export Under regulation 33(1), must my business apply enhanced customer due diligence measures?
GIVEN `my risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identified the case as one with a high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business's own risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identify this case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `information made available to me under regulations 17(9) and 47 identified the case as one with a high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did information made available to your business under regulations 17(9) and 47 identify this case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `there is a business relationship with the customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a business relationship between your business and the customer (regulation 4)?
      `the customer is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your business has the relationship with established in a country named on the Financial Action Task Force list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action?
      `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a transaction for which your business must apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27?
      `a party to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is either party to that transaction established in a country named on the Financial Action Task Force list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action?
      `it is a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution?
      `I have determined that the customer is a PEP or a relative or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business determined that the customer or potential customer is a politically exposed person, or a family member or known close associate of one?
      `I discovered false or stolen identification and propose to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business discovered that the customer provided false or stolen identification documentation or information, and does it propose to continue to deal with the customer?
      `a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a transaction unusually complex or unusually large, given the nature of the transaction?
      `there is an unusual pattern of transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an unusual pattern of transactions?
      `the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose?
      `the case by its nature can present a higher risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a case which by its nature can present a higher risk of money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(1), must my business apply enhanced customer due diligence measures` IS
    `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the case`
    WHERE
        `the case` MEANS `reg 33(1) the case` WITH
            `the relevant person's risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS `my risk assessment under regulation 18(1) identified the case as one with a high risk` -- input mapping
            `information made available under regulations 17(9) and 47 identified the case as one where there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS `information made available to me under regulations 17(9) and 47 identified the case as one with a high risk` -- input mapping
            `reg 33(1)(b) the business relationship or transaction is connected with a FATF call for action country` IS
                `reg 33(1)(b) the business relationship or transaction is connected with a FATF call for action country`
                    (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship with the customer`)
                    (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the customer is established in a FATF call for action country`)
                    (`reg 33(3)(b) the transaction is a relevant transaction` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27`))
                    (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `a party to the transaction is established in a FATF call for action country`)
            `the case is a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution` IS `it is a correspondent relationship with a credit institution or a financial institution` -- input mapping
            `the relevant person has determined that the customer or potential customer is a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP` IS `I have determined that the customer is a PEP or a relative or close associate of one` -- input mapping
            `the relevant person has discovered that the customer has provided false or stolen identification documentation or information, and proposes to continue to deal with that customer` IS `I discovered false or stolen identification and propose to continue` -- input mapping
            `a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, in each case given the nature of the transaction` IS `a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large` -- input mapping
            `there is an unusual pattern of transactions` IS `there is an unusual pattern of transactions` -- input mapping
            `the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` IS `the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` -- input mapping
            `the case by its nature can present a higher risk of money laundering or terrorist financing` IS `the case by its nature can present a higher risk` -- input mapping

-- reg 33(2).
@export Under regulation 33(2), does the FATF-country limb not apply because my customer is a branch or subsidiary of an entity established in a third country?
GIVEN `the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity established in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the customer a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity which is established in a third country?
      `the entity is subject to equivalent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity?
      `the entity is supervised equivalently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive?
      `the branch or subsidiary complies with the group policies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the branch or subsidiary comply fully with procedures and policies established for the group under requirements equivalent to Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive?
      `I do not consider enhanced measures necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business, applying a risk-based approach, not consider that it is necessary to apply enhanced customer due diligence measures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(2), does the FATF-country limb not apply` IS
    `reg 33(2) paragraph (1)(b) does not apply` `the customer is a branch or majority owned subsidiary undertaking of an entity established in a third country` `the entity is subject to equivalent requirements` `the entity is supervised equivalently` `the branch or subsidiary complies with the group policies` `I do not consider enhanced measures necessary`

-- reg 33(3A) and (4).
@export Under regulation 33(3A), have the enhanced measures I took for the FATF-country limb included every measure the paragraph requires?
GIVEN `the measures are taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the enhanced measures taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(b) (the FATF call for action country limb)?
      `I obtained additional information on the customer and the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business obtain additional information on the customer and on the customer's beneficial owner?
      `I obtained additional information on the intended nature of the relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business obtain additional information on the intended nature of the business relationship?
      `I obtained information on the source of funds and source of wealth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business obtain information on the source of funds and source of wealth of the customer and of the customer's beneficial owner?
      `I obtained information on the reasons for the transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business obtain information on the reasons for the transactions?
      `I obtained the approval of senior management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business obtain the approval of senior management for establishing or continuing the business relationship?
      `I conducted enhanced monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business conduct enhanced monitoring of the business relationship by increasing the number and timing of controls applied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(3A), have my enhanced measures included every measure required` IS
    `reg 33(3A) the enhanced measures taken include every measure that the paragraph requires` `the measures are taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(b)` `the measures I took`
    WHERE
        `the measures I took` MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (IF `I obtained additional information on the customer and the beneficial owner` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(a) obtaining additional information on the customer and on the customer's` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I obtained additional information on the intended nature of the relationship` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(b) obtaining additional information on the intended nature of the business` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I obtained information on the source of funds and source of wealth` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(c) obtaining information on the source of funds and source of wealth` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I obtained information on the reasons for the transactions` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(d) obtaining information on the reasons for the transactions` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I obtained the approval of senior management` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(e) obtaining the approval of senior management for establishing` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I conducted enhanced monitoring` THEN LIST `reg 33(3A)(f) conducting enhanced monitoring of the business relationship` ELSE EMPTY))

@export Under regulation 33(4), have the enhanced measures I took for a case of unusual transactions included every measure the paragraph requires?
GIVEN `the measures are taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the enhanced measures taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(f) (unusually complex or large transactions, unusual patterns, no apparent purpose)?
      `I examined the background and purpose of the transaction as far as reasonably possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business, as far as reasonably possible, examine the background and purpose of the transaction?
      `I increased the degree and nature of monitoring of the business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business increase the degree and nature of monitoring of the business relationship in which the transaction is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(4), have my enhanced measures included every measure required` IS
    `reg 33(4) the enhanced measures taken include every measure that the paragraph requires` `the measures are taken for the purpose of regulation 33(1)(f)` `the measures I took`
    WHERE
        `the measures I took` MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (IF `I examined the background and purpose of the transaction as far as reasonably possible` THEN LIST `reg 33(4)(a) as far as reasonably possible, examining the background and purpose` ELSE EMPTY),
                (IF `I increased the degree and nature of monitoring of the business relationship` THEN LIST `reg 33(4)(b) increasing the degree and nature of monitoring of the business` ELSE EMPTY))

-- reg 33(4A) and (4B).
@export Under regulation 33(4A), must my business consider the nature and identity of the beneficiary of a life insurance policy it provides?
GIVEN `my business provides a life insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business provide a life insurance policy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(4A), must my business consider the beneficiary of the policy` IS
    `reg 33(4A) the relevant person must consider the nature and identity of the beneficiary of the policy` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `my business provides a life insurance policy`

@export Under regulation 33(4B), must my business take reasonable measures to identify and verify the beneficial owner of the beneficiary of a life insurance policy?
GIVEN `the beneficiary is a legal person or a legal arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the beneficiary of the life insurance policy your business provides a legal person or a legal arrangement?
      `the beneficiary presents a high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the beneficiary present a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(4B), must my business identify and verify the beneficial owner of the beneficiary` IS
    `reg 33(4B) the relevant person must take reasonable measures to identify and verify the identity of the beneficial owner of the beneficiary` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the beneficiary is a legal person or a legal arrangement` `the beneficiary presents a high risk`

@export Under regulation 33(4B), did my business take those measures before any payment was made under the policy?
GIVEN `the measures have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the measures to identify and verify the beneficial owner of the beneficiary been taken?
      `the date the measures were taken` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the measures taken? (any date if they have not been taken)
      `a payment has been made under the policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any payment been made under the policy?
      `the date of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the (first) payment made under the policy? (any date if none has been made)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 33(4B), were the measures taken before any payment was made` IS
    `reg 33(4B) the measures were taken before any payment was made under the policy` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the measures have been taken` `the date the measures were taken`) (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `a payment has been made under the policy` `the date of the payment`)

§§ `Credit institutions and financial institutions (regulation 34)`

@export Under regulation 34(1), must my institution take the additional measures for a correspondent relationship with a respondent?
GIVEN `the kind of my business` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc What kind of relevant person is your business?
      `I have or propose a correspondent relationship involving payments with another institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your institution have, or propose to have, a correspondent relationship involving the execution of payments with another credit institution or financial institution (the respondent)?
      `the respondent is from a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the respondent from a third country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 34(1), must my institution take the additional measures for the respondent` IS
    `reg 34(1) the correspondent must take the measures that the paragraph lists` `the kind of my business` `I have or propose a correspondent relationship involving payments with another institution` `the respondent is from a third country`

-- reg 34(1)(d): senior-management approval "before establishing a new correspondent relationship".
@export Under regulation 34(1)(d), did my institution obtain senior-management approval before establishing the new correspondent relationship?
GIVEN `I obtained approval from senior management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your institution obtain approval from senior management for the new correspondent relationship?
      `the date I obtained approval` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your institution obtain that approval? (any date if you did not)
      `the date I established the new correspondent relationship` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your institution establish the new correspondent relationship?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 34(1)(d), was senior-management approval obtained before the relationship was established` IS
    `reg 34(1)(d) approval was obtained before the new correspondent relationship was established` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `I obtained approval from senior management` `the date I obtained approval`) `the date I established the new correspondent relationship`

@export Under regulation 34(2), may my institution enter into or continue a correspondent relationship with the other party?
GIVEN `the kind of my business` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc What kind of relevant person is your business?
      `the other party is a shell bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other party a shell bank?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 34(2), may my institution have a correspondent relationship with the other party` IS
    `reg 34(2) the institution may enter into or continue a correspondent relationship with the other party` `the kind of my business` `the other party is a shell bank`

@export Under regulation 34(3), must my institution take appropriate enhanced measures to ensure it does not have a relationship with an institution that allows shell bank accounts?
GIVEN `the kind of my business` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc What kind of relevant person is your business?
      `the other institution is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other credit institution or financial institution known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 34(3), must my institution take appropriate enhanced measures` IS
    `reg 34(3) the institution must take appropriate enhanced measures to ensure it does not enter into or continue the relationship` `the kind of my business` `the other institution is known to allow its accounts to be used by a shell bank`

@export Under regulation 34(4), is the other institution a shell bank?
GIVEN `it is a credit institution, a financial institution or an institution engaged in equivalent activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the institution a credit institution or a financial institution, or an institution engaged in activities equivalent to those of a credit institution or financial institution?
      `it is incorporated where it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it incorporated in a jurisdiction in which it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management?
      `it is part of a financial conglomerate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it part of a financial conglomerate or a third-country financial conglomerate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 34(4), is the other institution a shell bank` IS
    `reg 34(4)(b) the institution is a shell bank` `it is a credit institution, a financial institution or an institution engaged in equivalent activities` `it is incorporated where it has no physical presence involving meaningful decision-making and management` `it is part of a financial conglomerate`

§§ `Politically exposed persons (regulation 35)`

@export Under regulation 35(3), must my business assess the level of risk and the extent of the enhanced due diligence measures for a PEP?
GIVEN `I have determined that the customer is a PEP or a relative or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business determined that the customer or potential customer is a politically exposed person, or a family member or known close associate of one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(3), must my business assess the level of risk and the extent of the measures` IS
    `reg 35(3) the relevant person must assess the level of risk and the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `I have determined that the customer is a PEP or a relative or close associate of one`

@export Under regulation 35(3A), does the assessment of a domestic PEP start from a lower level of risk, and may the extent of the measures be less than for a non-domestic PEP?
GIVEN `the customer is a domestic PEP or a relative or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the customer or potential customer a domestic PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a domestic PEP?
      `no enhanced risk factors are present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are no enhanced risk factors present (that is, no risk factors other than the customer's position as a domestic PEP or as a relative or associate of one)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(3A), may the extent of my measures be less than for a non-domestic PEP` IS
    `reg 35(3A)(b) the extent of the enhanced customer due diligence measures is less than the extent for a non-domestic PEP` `the customer is a domestic PEP or a relative or close associate of one` `no enhanced risk factors are present`

@export Under regulation 35(5), must my business meet this requirement when it proposes to have or continue a business relationship with a PEP?
GIVEN `there is a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business relationship entered into (regulation 4)?
      `I propose to have or continue a business relationship with a PEP or a relative or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business propose to have, or to continue, a business relationship with a PEP, or a family member or a known close associate of a PEP?
      requirement IS A `reg 35(5) requirement` @desc Which requirement are you asking about: approval from senior management, adequate measures on source of wealth and funds, or enhanced ongoing monitoring?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(5), must my business meet the requirement` IS
    `reg 35(5) the relevant person must meet the requirement, in addition to the measures required by regulation 33` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship`) `I propose to have or continue a business relationship with a PEP or a relative or close associate of one` requirement

@export Under regulation 35(7), did my business take the measures on the beneficiaries of a long-term insurance policy before any payment or assignment?
GIVEN `the measures have been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the measures to determine whether the beneficiaries or their beneficial owners are PEPs been taken?
      `the date the measures were taken` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the measures taken? (any date if they have not been taken)
      `a payment has been made under the policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any payment been made under the insurance policy?
      `the date of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the payment made? (any date if none has been made)
      `the benefit has been assigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the benefit of the insurance policy been assigned?
      `the date of the assignment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the benefit assigned? (any date if it has not been assigned)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(7), were my measures taken before any payment or assignment` IS
    `reg 35(7) the measures required by paragraph (6) were taken before any payment was made or the benefit was assigned` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the measures have been taken` `the date the measures were taken`) (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `a payment has been made under the policy` `the date of the payment`) (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the benefit has been assigned` `the date of the assignment`)

@export Under regulation 35(8)(a), must my business ensure that senior management is informed before it pays out under a policy whose beneficiary is a PEP?
GIVEN `the beneficiary is a PEP or a relative or close associate within regulation 35(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the beneficiary of the insurance policy a PEP, or a family member or known close associate of a PEP who comes within regulation 35(6)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(8)(a), must my business ensure that senior management is informed before pay-out` IS
    `reg 35(8)(a) the relevant person must ensure that its senior management is informed before it pays out any sums under the insurance policy` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the beneficiary is a PEP or a relative or close associate within regulation 35(6)(b)`

@export Under regulation 35(9), read with 35(10), must my business keep applying the PEP requirements on the date I am asking about?
GIVEN `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person a PEP who is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function?
      `the date the person ceased to be entrusted` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person cease to be entrusted with that public function?
      `I consider a longer period appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business consider a period longer than 12 months appropriate?
      `the day the longer period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what date does that longer period end? (any date if you do not consider a longer period appropriate)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether the requirements still apply?
      `the person was a PEP under the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person a politically exposed person within the meaning of regulation 14(5) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, when those Regulations were in force? (Regulation 35(10) takes out of regulation 35(9) a person who was not, and who ceased to be entrusted before these Regulations came into force on 26 June 2017.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(9), must my business keep applying the requirements` IS
    `reg 35(9) read with reg 35(10) the relevant person must continue to apply the requirements in paragraphs (5) and (8) on the date asked` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the person was a PEP and is no longer entrusted with a prominent public function` `the date the person ceased to be entrusted` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `I consider a longer period appropriate` `the day the longer period ends`) `the date I am asking about` `the person was a PEP under the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`

-- reg 35(12)(b): "family member of a politically exposed person includes" the relatives listed; a relative not listed is left open.
@export Under regulation 35(12)(b), is this relative a family member of the politically exposed person?
GIVEN relative IS A `reg 35(12)(b) relative` @desc Which relative is it: the spouse or civil partner of the PEP; the children of the PEP and the spouses or civil partners of the PEP's children; the parents of the PEP; or another relative (a brother or sister, for example)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 35(12)(b), is the relative a family member of the politically exposed person` IS
    `reg 35(12)(b) the relative is a family member of the politically exposed person` relative

§§ `Simplified customer due diligence and electronic money (regulations 37 and 38)`

@export Under regulation 37(1), may my business apply simplified customer due diligence measures?
GIVEN `I have determined that the relationship or transaction presents a low degree of risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business determined that the business relationship or transaction presents a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing?
      `I took into account my risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business take into account the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)?
      `I took into account the information made available to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business take into account relevant information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47?
      `I took into account the risk factors in regulation 37(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business take into account the risk factors referred to in regulation 37(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 37(1), may my business apply simplified customer due diligence measures` IS
    `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person`
        (IF `I have determined that the relationship or transaction presents a low degree of risk` THEN `low risk` ELSE `neither high nor low risk`)
        `I took into account my risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` `I took into account the information made available to me` `I took into account the risk factors in regulation 37(3)`

@export Under regulation 37(2), must my business keep monitoring the relationships it applies simplified measures to?
GIVEN `I apply simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business apply simplified customer due diligence measures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 37(2), must my business carry out sufficient monitoring` IS
    `reg 37(2)(b) the relevant person must carry out sufficient monitoring of the business relationships or transactions subject to those measures` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `I apply simplified customer due diligence measures`

@export Under regulation 37(5), may my business apply simplified measures to a pooled account?
GIVEN `the customer is a relevant person or a third-country person within regulation 37(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the customer a relevant person under regulation 8, or a person carrying on business in a third country that is subject to equivalent requirements and supervised equivalently?
      `the product is an account into which monies are pooled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the product an account into which monies are pooled?
      `the relationship with the holder presents a low degree of risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the business relationship with the holder of the pooled account present a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing?
      `information on the persons whose monies are held is available on request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account available, on request to your business, where the pooled account is held?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 37(5), may my business apply simplified measures to the pooled account` IS
    `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the customer is a relevant person or a third-country person within regulation 37(6)`) `the product is an account into which monies are pooled` `the relationship with the holder presents a low degree of risk` `information on the persons whose monies are held is available on request`

@export Under regulation 37(8), may my business continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures?
GIVEN `I doubt the veracity or accuracy of documents or information obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business doubt the veracity or accuracy of any documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification?
      `my risk assessment has changed and I no longer consider the risk low` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your risk assessment changed so that you no longer consider that there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing?
      `I suspect money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business suspect money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `a condition in regulation 33(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of the conditions in regulation 33(1) apply (a case that requires enhanced customer due diligence)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 37(8), may my business continue to apply simplified measures` IS
    `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `I doubt the veracity or accuracy of documents or information obtained` `my risk assessment has changed and I no longer consider the risk low` `I suspect money laundering or terrorist financing` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `a condition in regulation 33(1) applies`)

@export Under regulation 38(1), am I not required to apply customer due diligence measures to this electronic money?
GIVEN `the maximum amount which can be stored electronically, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount, in pounds, that can be stored electronically?
      `the payment instrument is not reloadable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment instrument used in connection with the electronic money not reloadable?
      `the monthly payment limit, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If the instrument is reloadable: what is the maximum limit on monthly payment transactions, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
      `the instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the payment instrument only be used in the United Kingdom?
      `the instrument is used exclusively to purchase goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment instrument used exclusively to purchase goods or services?
      `anonymous electronic money cannot fund the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that anonymous electronic money cannot be used to fund the payment instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 38(1), am I not required to apply customer due diligence measures to the electronic money` IS
    `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the maximum amount which can be stored electronically, in pounds` `the payment instrument is not reloadable` (`mlr2 seat the amount if there is one` `the monthly payment limit, in pounds`) `the instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom` `the instrument is used exclusively to purchase goods or services` `anonymous electronic money cannot fund the instrument`

@export Under regulation 38(2), does the exemption not apply to this cash redemption or withdrawal?
GIVEN `it is a redemption in cash or a cash withdrawal of the monetary value of the electronic money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transaction consist of the redemption in cash, or a cash withdrawal, of the monetary value of the electronic money?
      `the amount redeemed, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, was redeemed?
      `it is a remote payment transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a remote payment transaction?
      `the amount redeemed per transaction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc For a remote payment transaction: what amount, in pounds, was redeemed per transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 38(2), does the exemption not apply to the transaction` IS
    `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` `it is a redemption in cash or a cash withdrawal of the monetary value of the electronic money` `the amount redeemed, in pounds` `it is a remote payment transaction` `the amount redeemed per transaction, in pounds`

@export Under regulation 38(4A), may my institution accept payment using this anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country?
GIVEN `the kind of my business` IS A `Kind of relevant person` @desc What kind of relevant person is your business?
      `I am acting as an acquirer for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your institution acting as an acquirer for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country?
      `the card is subject to equivalent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the card subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in regulation 38?
      `the card satisfies those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the card satisfy those requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 38(4A), may my institution accept payment using the card` IS
    `reg 38(4A) the institution may accept payment using the anonymous prepaid card` `the kind of my business` `I am acting as an acquirer for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country` `the card is subject to equivalent requirements` `the card satisfies those requirements`

§§ `Reliance on others, record-keeping and personal data (regulations 39 to 41)`

-- reg 39(1) with 39(3).  The third party is a relevant person (regulation 8, another part's answer, asked as a fact), or one of the other kinds in paragraph (3).
@export Under regulation 39(1), may my business rely on this third party to apply a customer due diligence measure?
GIVEN `the third party is a relevant person under regulation 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party a relevant person under regulation 8?
      `the third party carries on business in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the third party carry on business in a third country?
      `the third party is subject to equivalent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party subject to requirements on customer due diligence and record keeping equivalent to those of the fourth money laundering directive?
      `the third party is supervised equivalently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of that directive?
      `the third party is an organisation of such persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party an organisation whose members consist of persons of the kinds just described?
      `the measure is one that regulation 39 covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure one required by regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10), or by regulation 30A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 39(1), may my business rely on the third party` IS
    `reg 39(1) the relevant person may rely on the third party` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person`
        (`reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the third party is a relevant person under regulation 8`) `the third party carries on business in a third country` `the third party is subject to equivalent requirements` `the third party is supervised equivalently` `the third party is an organisation of such persons`)
        `the measure is one that regulation 39 covers`

@export Under regulation 39(1), do I remain liable for a failure to apply the measure when I rely on a third party?
GIVEN `I rely on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business rely on the third party to apply the measure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 39(1), do I remain liable for the third party's failure` IS
    `reg 39(1) the relevant person remains liable for any failure to apply such measures` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `I rely on the third party`

@export Under regulation 39(2), must my business obtain the information and enter into the arrangements before relying on a third party?
GIVEN `I rely on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business rely on the third party to apply the measure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 39(2), must my business obtain the information and enter into the arrangements` IS
    `reg 39(2) the relevant person must obtain the information and enter into the arrangements` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `I rely on the third party`

@export Under regulation 39(2), have I met those requirements?
GIVEN `I rely on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business rely on the third party to apply the measure?
      `I immediately obtained the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business immediately obtain from the third party all the information needed to satisfy the requirements of regulation 28(2) to (6) and (10) and regulation 30A?
      `I entered into arrangements to obtain copies on request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business enter into arrangements which enable it to obtain from the third party, immediately on request, copies of any identification and verification data and other relevant documentation?
      `the arrangements require the third party to retain copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those arrangements require the third party to retain copies of the data and documents for the period referred to in regulation 40?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 39(2), have I met the requirements` IS
    `reg 39(2) the relevant person has met the requirements` `I rely on the third party` `I immediately obtained the information` `I entered into arrangements to obtain copies on request` `the arrangements require the third party to retain copies`

-- reg 39(4) with 39(5).
@export Under regulation 39(4), may my business rely on a third party established in a FATF call for action country?
GIVEN `the third party is established in a FATF call for action country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party established in a country named on the Financial Action Task Force list of High-Risk Jurisdictions subject to a Call for Action?
      `the third party is a branch or majority owned subsidiary of an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the third party a branch or majority owned subsidiary of an entity?
      `the entity is a relevant person under these Regulations and supervised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity a relevant person within regulation 8, supervised for compliance with these Regulations?
      `the entity is subject to equivalent requirements and supervised equivalently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity subject to requirements in national legislation equivalent to the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity, and supervised for compliance in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of that directive?
      `the branch or subsidiary complies with the group policies under regulation 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the branch or subsidiary comply fully with procedures and policies established for the group under regulation 20?
      `the branch or subsidiary complies with the equivalent group policies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the branch or subsidiary comply fully with group procedures and policies under national requirements equivalent to Article 45 of the fourth money laundering directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 39(4), may my business rely on a third party in a FATF call for action country` IS
    `reg 39(4) the relevant person may rely on the third party established in a FATF call for action country` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the third party is established in a FATF call for action country`
        (`reg 39(5) paragraph (4) does not apply to the third party` `the third party is a branch or majority owned subsidiary of an entity` `the entity is a relevant person under these Regulations and supervised` `the entity is subject to equivalent requirements and supervised equivalently` `the branch or subsidiary complies with the group policies under regulation 20` `the branch or subsidiary complies with the equivalent group policies`)

-- reg 40(1) with 40(3).
@export Under regulation 40(1), must my business still keep the records on the date I am asking about?
GIVEN `the transaction is complete or the relationship has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or have you reasonable grounds to believe, that the transaction is complete or that the business relationship has come to an end?
      `the date it became complete or ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you know, or have reasonable grounds to believe, that the transaction was complete or the business relationship had ended? (any date if it has not)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether you must still keep the records?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 40(1), must my business still keep the records` IS
    `reg 40(1) the relevant person must still keep the records on the date asked` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the transaction is complete or the relationship has ended` `the date it became complete or ended`) `the date I am asking about`

@export Under regulation 40(3), on what date does the period of five years end?
GIVEN `the date the period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period begin (the date on which the occasional transaction is completed, or the business relationship ends)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 40(3), on what date does the five-year period end` IS
    `reg 40(3) the last day of the period of five years` `the date the period begins`

@export Under regulation 40(5), must my business delete the personal data?
GIVEN `the five-year period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period of five years referred to in regulation 40(3) expired?
      `I must retain it by or under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business required to retain records containing the personal data by or under any enactment?
      `I must retain it for court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business required to retain records containing the personal data for the purposes of any court proceedings?
      `the data subject has consented to the retention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the data subject given consent to the retention of that data?
      `I have reasonable grounds to retain it for legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 40(5), must my business delete the personal data` IS
    `reg 40(5) the relevant person must delete the personal data obtained for the purposes of these Regulations` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the five-year period has expired` `I must retain it by or under an enactment` `I must retain it for court proceedings` `the data subject has consented to the retention` `I have reasonable grounds to retain it for legal proceedings`

@export Under regulation 40(7), must my business, as the person relied on, make the information available and forward copies?
GIVEN `a relevant person relies on my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a relevant person rely on your business to apply customer due diligence measures?
      `the relevant person has asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the relevant person asked for the information and documents?
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the relevant person ask for the information and documents? (any date if it has not)
      `the last day of the retention period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period referred to in regulation 40(3) or, if applicable, regulation 40(4)?
      `the relevant person applies measures by means of an agent or outsourcing service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the relevant person apply customer due diligence measures by means of an agent or an outsourcing service provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 40(7), must my business make the information available` IS
    `reg 40(7) the person relied on must make the information available and forward copies of the data and documents to the relevant person` (`reg 39(3) the person falls within paragraph (3)` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `a relevant person relies on my business` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the relevant person has asked` `the date of the request`) `the last day of the retention period` `the relevant person applies measures by means of an agent or outsourcing service provider`

@export Under regulation 41(6), have I provided the customer with the statement before establishing the relationship or entering into the transaction?
GIVEN `the customer is a new customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the customer a new customer?
      `the statement says what regulation 41(6) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement say that personal data received from the customer will be processed only for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing, or as permitted under regulation 41(3)?
      `I have provided the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided the statement to the customer?
      `the date the statement was provided` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement provided? (any date if it has not been)
      `the date the relationship was established or the transaction entered into` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the business relationship established or the occasional transaction entered into?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 41(6), have I provided the statement in time` IS
    `reg 41(6) the relevant person has provided the customer with the statement before establishing the business relationship or entering into the occasional transaction` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `the customer is a new customer` `the statement says what regulation 41(6) requires` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `I have provided the statement` `the date the statement was provided`) `the date the relationship was established or the transaction entered into`

§§ `Beneficial ownership information (regulations 42 to 45ZB)`

-- reg 42(2)(a).
@export Under regulation 42(2)(a), is the body a UK body corporate?
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom?
      `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an eligible Scottish partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 42(2)(a), is the body a UK body corporate` IS
    `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` `the body is a body corporate incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of it` `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership`

-- reg 43(1): the business asks a UK body corporate for information about its ownership.
@export Under regulation 43(1), must the UK body corporate provide me with this information on request?
GIVEN `the body is incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a body corporate incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of it?
      `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an eligible Scottish partnership?
      `the body is listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate listed on a regulated market?
      `the body enters into a transaction with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body corporate enter into a transaction with your business?
      `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have to apply customer due diligence measures to that transaction under regulation 27?
      `the body forms a business relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body corporate form a business relationship with your business?
      `there is a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a business relationship between the body corporate and your business (regulation 4)?
      item IS A `reg 43(1) item` @desc Which information are you asking about: name and addresses, board, senior persons, governing law, legal owners, beneficial owners, or articles of association?
      `I have asked the body corporate for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the body corporate to provide you with that information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 43(1), must the UK body corporate provide me with the information` IS
    `reg 43(1) the body corporate must on request provide the item to the relevant person` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person`
        (`reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` `the body is incorporated in the United Kingdom` `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership`)
        `the body is listed on a regulated market` `the body enters into a transaction with me`
        (`reg 43(9) the transaction is a relevant transaction` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27`))
        `the body forms a business relationship with me`
        (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship`)
        item
        `I have asked the body corporate for the information`

@export Under regulation 43(4), by what date must the UK body corporate notify me of a change?
GIVEN `the date the body became aware of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the body corporate become aware of the change in the identity of the individuals or in the information?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 43(4), by what date must the body corporate notify me` IS
    `reg 43(4) the last day for the notification` `the date the body became aware of the change`

-- reg 44(2) and (3): the business meets a trustee.
@export Under regulation 44(2)(a), must a trustee who deals with my business inform me that it is acting as trustee?
GIVEN `the trust is a relevant trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a relevant trust within regulation 42(2)(b)?
      `the trustee is acting as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person dealing with your business doing so in the capacity of trustee?
      `the trustee enters into a transaction with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee enter into a transaction with your business?
      `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have to apply customer due diligence measures to that transaction under regulation 27?
      `the trustee forms a business relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee form a business relationship with your business?
      `there is a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a business relationship between the trustee and your business (regulation 4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(2)(a), must the trustee inform me that it is acting as trustee` IS
    `reg 44(2)(a) the trustee must inform the relevant person that it is acting as trustee` `the case`
    WHERE
        `the case` MEANS
            `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person`
                (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the trust is a relevant trust`)
                `the trustee is acting as trustee` `the trustee enters into a transaction with me`
                (`reg 44(4) the transaction is a relevant transaction` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27`))
                `the trustee forms a business relationship with me`
                (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship`)

@export Under regulation 44(2)(b), must the trustee provide me with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust?
GIVEN `the trust is a relevant trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a relevant trust within regulation 42(2)(b)?
      `the trustee is acting as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person dealing with your business doing so in the capacity of trustee?
      `the trustee enters into a transaction with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee enter into a transaction with your business?
      `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have to apply customer due diligence measures to that transaction under regulation 27?
      `the trustee forms a business relationship with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee form a business relationship with your business?
      `there is a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a business relationship between the trustee and your business (regulation 4)?
      `I have asked for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business requested the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(2)(b), must the trustee provide the information identifying all the beneficial owners` IS
    `reg 44(2)(b) the trustee must provide the relevant person with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust` `the case` `I have asked for the information`
    WHERE
        `the case` MEANS
            `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person`
                (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the trust is a relevant trust`)
                `the trustee is acting as trustee` `the trustee enters into a transaction with me`
                (`reg 44(4) the transaction is a relevant transaction` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `the transaction needs customer due diligence under regulation 27`))
                `the trustee forms a business relationship with me`
                (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship`)

@export Under regulation 44(3), must the trustees notify me of a change?
GIVEN `I was provided with information under regulation 44(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your business provided with information under regulation 44(2)?
      `there is a business relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a business relationship between the trustees and your business (regulation 4)?
      `there is a change in the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a change in the information that was provided to your business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(3), must the trustees notify me of the change` IS
    `reg 44(3) the trustees must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` `I was provided with information under regulation 44(2)` (`mlr2 seat what I say, as a fact` `there is a business relationship`) `there is a change in the information`

@export Under regulation 44(3), by what date must the trustees notify me of a change?
GIVEN `the date any one of the trustees became aware of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date did any one of the trustees become aware of the change?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(3), by what date must the trustees notify me` IS
    `reg 44(3) the last day for the notification` `the date any one of the trustees became aware of the change`

-- reg 44(9): my business as a paid trustee.
@export Under regulation 44(9)(a), must my business, as a paid trustee, retain the records for five years after the final distribution?
GIVEN `my business is being paid to act as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business being paid to act as a trustee of the trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(9)(a), must my business retain the records for five years` IS
    `reg 44(9)(a) the trustees must retain the records for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `my business is being paid to act as trustee`

@export Under regulation 44(9)(a), on what date does that five-year period end?
GIVEN `the date of the final distribution` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the final distribution made?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(9)(a), on what date does the five-year period end` IS
    `reg 44(9)(a) the last day of the period of five years after the final distribution` `the date of the final distribution`

@export Under regulation 44(9)(a), must my business, as a paid trustee, still retain the records on the date I am asking about?
GIVEN `my business is being paid to act as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business being paid to act as a trustee of the trust?
      `the final distribution has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the final distribution of the trust been made?
      `the date of the final distribution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the final distribution made? (any date if it has not been made)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether the records must still be retained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(9)(a), must my business still retain the records on the date` IS
    `reg 44(9)(a) the trustees must still retain the records on the date asked` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `my business is being paid to act as trustee` (`mlr2 seat the day if it has come` `the final distribution has been made` `the date of the final distribution`) `the date I am asking about`

@export Under regulation 44(9)(b), must my business, as a paid trustee, arrange for the records to be deleted at the end of that period?
GIVEN `my business is being paid to act as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business being paid to act as a trustee of the trust?
      `I must retain the records by or under an enactment or for court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business required to retain the records by or under any enactment or for the purpose of court proceedings?
      `a person to whom the information relates consents to its retention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person to whom information in a record relates consent to the retention of that information?
      `I have reasonable grounds to retain it for legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 44(9)(b), must my business arrange for the records to be deleted` IS
    `reg 44(9)(b) the trustees must make arrangements for the records to be deleted at the end of that period` `mlr2 seat the business is a relevant person` `my business is being paid to act as trustee` `I must retain the records by or under an enactment or for court proceedings` `a person to whom the information relates consents to its retention` `I have reasonable grounds to retain it for legal proceedings`

-- reg 45ZB(1) and (4)(a): the business asks the Commissioners for access to the register.
@export Under regulation 45ZB(1), must the Commissioners make the accessible information available to my business?
GIVEN `my business demonstrates a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business demonstrate to the Commissioners a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust?
      `my business so requests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your business made the request?
      `the Commissioners consider the information should be exempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Commissioners consider that the information should be exempt?
      ground IS A `reg 45ZB(5) ground` @desc Which ground do they give: disproportionate risk to the beneficial owner, the beneficial owner is under 18, the beneficial owner lacks capacity or is incapable (England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland), or another ground?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 45ZB(1), must the Commissioners make the accessible information available to my business` IS
    `reg 45ZB(1) the Commissioners must make the accessible information available to the person` `my business demonstrates a legitimate interest in the beneficial ownership of a trust` `my business so requests`
        (`reg 45ZB(5) paragraphs (1) and (3) do not apply to the accessible information` `the Commissioners consider the information should be exempt` ground)

@export Under regulation 45ZB(4)(a), may the Commissioners charge my business this fee?
GIVEN `my request is for accessible information under regulation 45ZB(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request for accessible information under regulation 45ZB(1) or (3)?
      `the fee, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee, in pounds, are they charging?
      `the amount that meets their expenses, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, do the Commissioners consider will enable them to meet any expenses reasonably incurred by them in dealing with such requests, including expenses incurred in maintaining the register?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 45ZB(4)(a), may the Commissioners charge my business the fee` IS
    `reg 45ZB(4)(a) the Commissioners may charge the fee` `my request is for accessible information under regulation 45ZB(1) or (3)` `the fee, in pounds` `the amount that meets their expenses, in pounds`

-- ============================================================
-- mlr3: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer)
-- Regulations 2017 (United Kingdom), regs 45A to 64H -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a business that is a relevant person under the Regulations (a bank, an accountancy or
-- legal firm, an estate agent, a money service business, a cryptoasset business and so on) and
-- its compliance officer.  This layer phrases the rules of the four layer-1 modules imported
-- above as the questions that person would ask about this part of the Regulations: who
-- supervises me and what may they do with what they know about me, must I be on a register, may
-- I trade while my application is waiting, what must I tell the registering authority and by
-- when, what may be done to my registration, who supervises my transfers of funds, and what must
-- travel with a cryptoasset transfer.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from
-- a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person
-- would be asked.  The records and MAYBE inputs the modules expect are built inside each
-- question from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact that another part of the Regulations decides, and that the person may not know
--     (whether a business relationship exists; whether a body is a law enforcement authority;
--     whether an offence is one listed in Schedule 3), is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure";
--     "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A date that may not have happened yet is asked as a yes/no ("has it happened?") and a date.
--   * The dates the Regulations leave out (the full commencement day of reg 56B(2), the days of
--     Good Friday and the bank holidays) are asked for.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulations themselves give;
-- NOTHING means the Regulations do not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result:
-- FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  A provision that addresses only a supervisor or a registering
-- authority is encoded in layer 1 for what it decides, and the person meets it only through the
-- questions below, which ask what it means to a supervised business (regs 46(1) to (4), 46A,
-- 49(1)(a) to (c), 49(2), 49(3), 50(1) and 51 have no question of their own, for example).
-- A question that takes an Authority takes it as a choice from the core's list, never as a role to
-- be played.  The questions are in the text's order and grouped under `§§` headings.

DECLARE `reg 53 my answer` IS ONE OF
    `reg 53 Yes`
    `reg 53 No`
    `reg 53 I am not sure`

DECLARE `reg 52 kind of body I am asking about` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52 another supervisory authority`
    `reg 52 the Treasury`
    `reg 52 a law enforcement authority`
    `reg 52 an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)`
    `reg 52 the Secretary of State, for the functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency`
    `reg 52 the registrar of companies`
    `reg 52 the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`
    `reg 52 none of these`

DECLARE `reg 52A route by which the disclosure is made` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52A(3)(a) in the discharge of its duties under these Regulations`
    `reg 52A(3)(a)(i) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing`
    `reg 52A(3)(a)(ii) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to prudential regulation`
    `reg 52A(3)(a)(iii) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions and cryptoasset businesses`
    `reg 52A(3)(b) in an appeal against a decision of a supervisory authority`
    `reg 52A(3)(c) in court proceedings initiated by a relevant supervisory authority`
    `reg 52A(3)(d) in accordance with sections 17 and 18 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`
    `reg 52A(3)(da) in accordance with sections 348 and 349 of FSMA as modified by paragraph (3A)`
    `reg 52A(3)(e) in accordance with regulation 52`
    `reg 52A(3) none of these routes`

DECLARE `reg 52B what the court's sentence is for` IS ONE OF
    `reg 52B(2)(a) conviction in a magistrates' court or sheriff court (on summary conviction)`
    `reg 52B(2)(b) conviction in the Crown Court or on indictment`

DECLARE `reg 64B the sort of transfer I am asking about` IS ONE OF
    `reg 64B an inter-cryptoasset business transfer`
    `reg 64B an unhosted wallet transfer`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `reg 53 my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `reg 53 Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 53 No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 53 I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A day that may not have happened yet.
GIVEN `it has happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 53 a day if it has happened` MEANS
    IF `it has happened` THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- The supervisors of a relevant person, from the one authority the person names.
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Authority)
`reg 53 the one authority that supervises me` MEANS JUST (LIST authority) -- input mapping

-- The description of a body, from the kind the person names.
GIVEN kind IS A `reg 52 kind of body I am asking about`
      `I know whether it is a law enforcement authority` IS A `reg 53 my answer`
GIVETH A `reg 52(5) description of the body`
`reg 52 the body I am asking about` MEANS
    `reg 52(5) description of the body` OF
        (kind EQUALS `reg 52 another supervisory authority`)
      , (kind EQUALS `reg 52 the Treasury`)
      , (IF kind EQUALS `reg 52 a law enforcement authority` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `I know whether it is a law enforcement authority`)
      , (kind EQUALS `reg 52 an overseas authority within the meaning of regulation 50(4)`)
      , (kind EQUALS `reg 52 the Secretary of State, for the functions under enactments relating to companies, audit and insolvency`)
      , (kind EQUALS `reg 52 the registrar of companies`)
      , (kind EQUALS `reg 52 the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme`)

-- The record of what a disclosure of confidential information relied on, from the route named.
GIVEN route IS A `reg 52A route by which the disclosure is made`
GIVETH A `reg 52A(3) disclosure of confidential information`
`reg 52A the disclosure I am asking about` MEANS
    `reg 52A(3) disclosure of confidential information` OF
        TRUE
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(a) in the discharge of its duties under these Regulations`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(a)(i) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to money laundering, terrorist financing or proliferation financing`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(a)(ii) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to prudential regulation`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(a)(iii) in the discharge of its duties under other legislation relating to the supervision of credit institutions, financial institutions and cryptoasset businesses`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(b) in an appeal against a decision of a supervisory authority`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(c) in court proceedings initiated by a relevant supervisory authority`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(d) in accordance with sections 17 and 18 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(da) in accordance with sections 348 and 349 of FSMA as modified by paragraph (3A)`)
      , (route EQUALS `reg 52A(3)(e) in accordance with regulation 52`)

-- The record of facts about me that regs 54 and 55 sort on.
GIVEN `I am an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have notified the FCA under regulation 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a cryptoasset exchange provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an authorised cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a high value dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a bill payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 54 registrant`
`reg 54 me, as a person to be registered` MEANS
    `reg 54 registrant` OF `I am an authorised person`, `I have notified the FCA under regulation 23`, `I am a cryptoasset exchange provider`, `I am a custodian wallet provider`, `I am an authorised cryptoasset firm`, `I am a specified investment cryptoasset firm`, `I am a high value dealer`, `I am a money service business`, `I am a trust or company service provider`, `I am a bill payment service provider`, `I am a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider`

-- A cryptoasset transfer, from the kind and the sterling value of it and the transfers linked to it.
GIVEN kind IS A `reg 64B the sort of transfer I am asking about`
      value IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cryptoasset transfer`
`reg 64A the transfer I am asking about` MEANS
    `Cryptoasset transfer` OF (IF kind EQUALS `reg 64B an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` THEN `an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` ELSE `an unhosted wallet transfer`), value

-- The three kinds of risk, from a yes for each.
GIVEN `my assessment covered money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my assessment covered terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my assessment covered proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of risk`
`reg 64D the kinds of risk my assessment covered` MEANS
    append (IF `my assessment covered money laundering` THEN LIST `money laundering` ELSE EMPTY)
           (append (IF `my assessment covered terrorist financing` THEN LIST `terrorist financing` ELSE EMPTY)
                   (IF `my assessment covered proliferation financing` THEN LIST `proliferation financing` ELSE EMPTY))


-- Whether the authority that regulation 53 names is a given one.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE Authority
      b IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 53 whether the answer is the authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- input mapping
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (x EQUALS b) -- input mapping

-- A list of days off from the days the person says apply.
GIVEN flag IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`reg 64B the list of one optional day` MEANS
    IF flag THEN LIST day ELSE EMPTY -- input mapping

GIVEN `has the first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first` IS A DATE
      `has the second` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`reg 64B the list of two optional days` MEANS
    append (`reg 64B the list of one optional day` `has the first` `the first`) (`reg 64B the list of one optional day` `has the second` `the second`)

§ `The Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, regs 45A to 64H -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What my supervisory authority must do and may do about me (regs 46 to 52B)`
-- Situation: the business is supervised by the FCA, the Commissioners, the Gambling Commission or a professional body.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 46(5).  A supervisory authority that knows or suspects a relevant person is laundering
-- money or financing terrorism must tell the NCA as soon as practicable.
@export Under regulation 46(5), must the authority that supervises me tell the National Crime Agency if it knows or suspects that I have engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVEN `my supervisory authority knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that I am or have been engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authority that supervises you know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that you are or have been engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 46(5), must my supervisory authority inform the NCA` IS
    `reg 46(5) the authority must inform the NCA` `my supervisory authority knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that I am or have been engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`

@export Under regulation 46(6), is a report to the National Crime Agency under regulation 46(5) about me a breach of any restriction on disclosing information?
GIVEN `the report was made under regulation 46(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the report made by my supervisory authority under regulation 46(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 46(6), is the report not a breach of a restriction` IS
    `reg 46(6) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` `the report was made under regulation 46(5)`

@export Under regulation 46(7), is the authority (or the person who made the report for it) free of civil liability to me for a report made in good faith under regulation 46(5)?
GIVEN `the report was made under regulation 46(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the report made under regulation 46(5)?
      `the report was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 46(7), is there no civil liability for the report` IS
    `reg 46(7) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` `the report was made under regulation 46(5)` `the report was made in good faith`

-- reg 47(1).  Each supervisory authority must make up-to-date information available to the
-- relevant persons it supervises.
@export Under regulation 47(1), must this authority make up-to-date information on money laundering and terrorist financing available to me?
GIVEN `the authority that supervises me` IS AN Authority @desc Which authority supervises your business?
      `the authority I am asking about` IS AN Authority @desc Which authority are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 47(1), must the authority make information available to me` IS
    `reg 47(1) the authority must make up-to-date information available to the relevant person` (`reg 53 the one authority that supervises me` `the authority that supervises me`) `the authority I am asking about`

@export Under regulation 47(2), does the information my supervisory authority has made available to me include the three matters the regulation requires?
GIVEN `it includes the money laundering and terrorist financing practices the authority considers to apply to its own sector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the money laundering and terrorist financing practices the authority considers to apply to its own sector?
      `it includes a description of indications that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in the sector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a description of indications which may suggest that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in your sector?
      `it includes a description of the circumstances in which the authority considers there is a high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a description of the circumstances in which the authority considers that there is a high risk of money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 47(2), does the information include the three matters` IS
    `reg 47(2) the information includes the three matters the paragraph requires` `it includes the money laundering and terrorist financing practices the authority considers to apply to its own sector` `it includes a description of indications that a transfer of criminal funds is taking place in the sector` `it includes a description of the circumstances in which the authority considers there is a high risk`

-- reg 48(1).  The FCA must give guidance on politically exposed persons to the relevant persons
-- subject to its rules.
@export Under regulation 48(1), must the FCA give me guidance on enhanced customer due diligence for politically exposed persons?
GIVEN `I am subject to rules made by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business subject to rules made by the Financial Conduct Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 48(1), must the FCA give me guidance on politically exposed persons` IS
    `reg 48(1) the FCA must give the relevant person guidance on enhanced customer due diligence measures for politically exposed persons` `I am subject to rules made by the FCA`

-- reg 49(1)(d).  A self-regulatory organisation must arrange that a relevant person it
-- supervises that contravenes a relevant requirement is liable to disciplinary measures.
@export Under regulation 49(1)(d), am I liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under my self-regulatory organisation's rules if I contravene a relevant requirement?
GIVEN `my self-regulatory organisation is responsible for supervising me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a self-regulatory organisation (such as a professional body) responsible for supervising your business?
      `I have contravened a relevant requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you contravened a relevant requirement of the Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 49(1)(d), am I liable to disciplinary measures` IS
    `reg 49(1)(d) the relevant person is liable to effective, proportionate and dissuasive disciplinary measures under the organisation's rules` `my self-regulatory organisation is responsible for supervising me` `I have contravened a relevant requirement`

-- reg 50(3).  Co-operation with overseas authorities may include sharing information the
-- authority is not prevented from disclosing, on conditions.
@export Under regulation 50(3), may my supervisory authority share information about me with an overseas authority?
GIVEN `the authority is not prevented from disclosing the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority free of any rule that prevents it from disclosing this information?
      `the information is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information confidential?
      `the other authority will hold it subject to an equivalent obligation of confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the other authority hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to the one in regulation 52A?
      `the information came from a third country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the information come from a competent authority or other institution in a third country?
      `the third-country source has given its express consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that source given its express consent to the disclosure?
      `the disclosure should be confined to the original purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate to confine the disclosure to the purposes for which the information was first provided?
      `the disclosure is for the original purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure for those original purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 50(3), may my supervisory authority share the information` IS
    `reg 50(3) co-operation may include the sharing of the information` `the authority is not prevented from disclosing the information` `the information is confidential` `the other authority will hold it subject to an equivalent obligation of confidentiality` `the information came from a third country` `the third-country source has given its express consent` `the disclosure should be confined to the original purposes` `the disclosure is for the original purposes`

-- reg 52(1).  A supervisory authority may disclose information it holds to a relevant authority
-- for certain purposes.
@export Under regulation 52(1), may my supervisory authority disclose information it holds about me to this body?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `reg 52 kind of body I am asking about` @desc What kind of body would receive the information?
      `I know whether it is a law enforcement authority` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc If the body is a law enforcement authority within the meaning of regulation 44(10), say Yes; if it is not, No; if you are not sure, say so.
      `the information is relevant to the authority's supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information one the authority holds and that is relevant to its supervisory functions?
      `for the body's functions under these Regulations or related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the body's functions under these Regulations, or other functions related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system?
      `for the law enforcement authority's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure for purposes connected with the effective exercise of the functions of a law enforcement authority?
      `for an overseas authority's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the body is an overseas authority: is the disclosure for the functions provided for in the fourth money laundering directive, or equivalent functions?
      `for the complaints investigator's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure for the functions of the investigator appointed under section 84 of the Financial Services Act 2012 in relation to the complaints scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52(1), may my supervisory authority disclose the information to the body` IS
    `reg 52(1) the supervisory authority may disclose the information to the relevant authority` (`reg 52 the body I am asking about` `the kind of body` `I know whether it is a law enforcement authority`) `the information is relevant to the authority's supervisory functions` `for the body's functions under these Regulations or related to money laundering, terrorist financing or the integrity of the international financial system` `for the law enforcement authority's functions` `for an overseas authority's functions` `for the complaints investigator's functions`

@export Under regulation 52(2), may a relevant authority that received information about me under regulation 52(1) or (1A) pass it on?
GIVEN `it was disclosed to the authority under paragraph (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information disclosed to the authority under regulation 52(1) or (1A)?
      `the further disclosure is in accordance with paragraph (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further disclosure in accordance with regulation 52(1) or (1A)?
      `the FCA is passing it to the PRA about a PRA-authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority the FCA, passing it to the PRA, about a PRA-authorised person or someone with a qualifying relationship with one?
      `an overseas authority is passing it on as the disclosing supervisor allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority an overseas authority passing it on in accordance with the conditions the disclosing supervisor imposed?
      `it is for criminal or other enforcement proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further disclosure with a view to the institution of, or otherwise for the purposes of, criminal or other enforcement proceedings?
      `it is otherwise required by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the further disclosure otherwise required by law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52(2), may the relevant authority disclose the information further` IS
    `reg 52(2) the relevant authority may further disclose the information` `it was disclosed to the authority under paragraph (1) or (1A)` `the further disclosure is in accordance with paragraph (1) or (1A)` `the FCA is passing it to the PRA about a PRA-authorised person` `an overseas authority is passing it on as the disclosing supervisor allows` `it is for criminal or other enforcement proceedings` `it is otherwise required by law`

@export Under regulation 52(4), is there no civil liability to me for a disclosure made in good faith under regulation 52(1) or (1A)?
GIVEN `it was made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure made under regulation 52(1)?
      `it was made under paragraph (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disclosure made under regulation 52(1A)?
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52(4), is there no civil liability for the disclosure` IS
    `reg 52(4) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` `it was made under paragraph (1)` `it was made under paragraph (1A)` `it was made in good faith`

-- reg 52A(1).  A person who works or worked for a relevant supervisory authority may not
-- disclose confidential information received in the course of duties, except as the regulation allows.
@export Under regulation 52A(1), may a person who works for my supervisory authority disclose confidential information they received about me?
GIVEN `the person works, or has worked, for a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person work, or did they work, for or on behalf of a relevant supervisory authority?
      `the information is confidential information received in their duties under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it confidential information they received in the course of their duties under these Regulations?
      `the disclosure is in accordance with regulation 52A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure in accordance with regulation 52A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(1), may the person disclose the confidential information` IS
    `reg 52A(1) the person may disclose the confidential information` `the person works, or has worked, for a relevant supervisory authority` `the information is confidential information received in their duties under these Regulations` `the disclosure is in accordance with regulation 52A`

@export Under regulation 52A(1), am I barred from disclosing confidential information I received while working for my supervisory authority?
GIVEN `the person works, or has worked, for a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, or did you work, for or on behalf of a relevant supervisory authority?
      `the information is confidential information received in their duties under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it confidential information you received in the course of your duties under these Regulations?
      `the disclosure is in accordance with regulation 52A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure in accordance with regulation 52A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(1), is the person barred from disclosing the confidential information` IS
    `reg 52A(1) the prohibition on disclosing the confidential information applies` `the person works, or has worked, for a relevant supervisory authority` `the information is confidential information received in their duties under these Regulations` `the disclosure is in accordance with regulation 52A`

@export Under regulation 52A(2), may confidential information about me be disclosed in summary or aggregate form?
GIVEN `it is disclosed in summary or aggregate form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information disclosed in summary or aggregate form?
      `a business is identifiable from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a credit institution, a financial institution or a cryptoasset business be identified from what is disclosed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(2), may the information be disclosed in summary or aggregate form` IS
    `reg 52A(2) the information may be disclosed in summary or aggregate form` `it is disclosed in summary or aggregate form` `a business is identifiable from it`

@export Under regulation 52A(3), may a relevant supervisory authority disclose confidential information it received under the Regulations by this route?
GIVEN route IS A `reg 52A route by which the disclosure is made` @desc By which route is the disclosure made?
      `the authority is a relevant supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authority a supervisory authority responsible for supervising credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses?
      `the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs the supervisory authority?
      `the FCA is the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Financial Conduct Authority the supervisory authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(3), may the relevant supervisory authority disclose the confidential information` IS
    `reg 52A(3) the relevant supervisory authority may disclose the confidential information` (`reg 52A the disclosure I am asking about` route) `the authority is a relevant supervisory authority` `the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` `the FCA is the supervisory authority`

@export Under regulation 52A(4), does regulation 52A prevent the exchange of information between these authorities?
GIVEN `the exchange is between two UK authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the exchange between two UK authorities responsible for supervising credit institutions, financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses?
      `the exchange is between a UK authority and a third-country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it between such a UK authority and a competent authority in a third country supervising credit or financial institutions or cryptoasset businesses?
      `the third-country authority supervises under the fourth money laundering directive or related acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the third-country authority supervise in accordance with the fourth money laundering directive or other legislative acts relating to those businesses?
      `the third-country authority supervises under laws with equivalent effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it supervise in accordance with laws imposing requirements of equivalent effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(4), does the regulation prevent the exchange` IS
    `reg 52A(4) this regulation prevents the exchange of information between the authorities` `the exchange is between two UK authorities` `the exchange is between a UK authority and a third-country competent authority` `the third-country authority supervises under the fourth money laundering directive or related acts` `the third-country authority supervises under laws with equivalent effect`

@export Under regulation 52A(5), may confidential information about me be exchanged under regulation 52A(4)?
GIVEN `it is exchanged under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information exchanged under regulation 52A(4)?
      `the receiving authority agrees to hold it subject to equivalent confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authority receiving it agree to hold it subject to an obligation of confidentiality equivalent to that in regulation 52A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52A(5), may the confidential information be exchanged` IS
    `reg 52A(5) the confidential information may be exchanged under paragraph (4)` `it is exchanged under paragraph (4)` `the receiving authority agrees to hold it subject to equivalent confidentiality`

@export Under regulation 52B(1), is a person who discloses confidential information about me in contravention of regulation 52A guilty of an offence?
GIVEN `the person discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person disclose information in contravention of regulation 52A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52B(1), is the person guilty of an offence` IS
    `reg 52B(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `the person discloses information in contravention of regulation 52A`

@export Under regulation 52B(2), what is the most a person guilty of the offence is liable to, in months of imprisonment?
GIVEN `how the person was convicted` IS A `reg 52B what the court's sentence is for` @desc How was the person convicted?
      `where the offence was tried` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom` @desc In which part of the United Kingdom was the person convicted?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under regulation 52B(2), the most the person is liable to, in months of imprisonment` IS
    (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` (IF `how the person was convicted` EQUALS `reg 52B(2)(a) conviction in a magistrates' court or sheriff court (on summary conviction)` THEN `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` ELSE `reg 52B(2)(b) on conviction on indictment`) `where the offence was tried`)'s `term of imprisonment in months, not exceeding`

@export Under regulation 52B(3), is it a defence for the accused that they did not know the information was confidential and took all reasonable precautions?
GIVEN `the accused proves they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused prove that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential information?
      `the accused proves they took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused prove that they took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid committing the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 52B(3), is it a defence for the accused` IS
    `reg 52B(3) it is a defence for the accused` `the accused proves they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the information was confidential` `the accused proves they took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Which authority registers me, and must I be on a register (regs 53 to 55)`
-- Situation: asked of a business that may have to be on a register kept by the FCA or the Commissioners
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 53 "registering authority" limb 1.  The FCA is the registering authority in relation to the persons regulation 54(1) and (1A) require it to register,
-- and those it decides to register under regulation 55(1).
@export Under regulation 53, is the FCA the registering authority for me?
GIVEN `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)?
      `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)?
      `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)?
      `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 53, is the FCA the registering authority for me` IS
    `reg 53 whether the answer is the authority` (`reg 53 the registering authority for the person` `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)`) `the Financial Conduct Authority`

-- reg 53 "registering authority" limb 2.
@export Under regulation 53, are the Commissioners the registering authority for me?
GIVEN `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)?
      `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)?
      `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)?
      `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 53, are the Commissioners the registering authority for me` IS
    `reg 53 whether the answer is the authority` (`reg 53 the registering authority for the person` `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)`) `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`

-- reg 53 "telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider": an undertaking meeting all three conditions.
@export Under regulation 53, am I a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider?
GIVEN `it is an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions?
      `the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of a telecommunication, digital or IT device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of a telecommunication, digital or IT device?
      `the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 53, am I a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` IS
    `reg 53 the undertaking is a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` `it is an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions` `the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of a telecommunication, digital or IT device` `the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services`

