-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `May I trade before I am registered (regs 56 to 56B)`
-- Situation: asked of a business that must be registered, or a cryptoasset business that must tell the FCA
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 56(1).  JUST FALSE where the prohibition bites; where an exception (paragraph (2), regulation 56A, being on the register) applies the paragraph does not say you may act, so NOTHING.
-- The exceptions are asked as facts: answer the questions on regulation 56(2) and 56A to know whether they apply.
@export Under regulation 56(1), may I act as a business that has to be registered, when I am not on the register?
GIVEN `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person?
      `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `the person is included in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is included in the appropriate register?
      `paragraph (2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (2) applies to the person?
      `regulation 56A applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulation 56A applies to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(1), may I act as a business that has to be registered, when I am not on the register` IS
    `reg 56(1) the person may act as the business` `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` `the person is included in the appropriate register` `paragraph (2) applies to the person` `regulation 56A applies to the person`

-- reg 56(1) in its own polarity: "Unless" is "if not", so the prohibition does not apply (JUST FALSE) to a person on the register or one for whom paragraph (2) or regulation 56A applies.
-- The exceptions are asked as facts: answer the questions on regulation 56(2) and 56A to know whether they apply.
@export Under regulation 56(1), does the prohibition on acting as a business that has to be registered apply to me?
GIVEN `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person?
      `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `the person is included in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is included in the appropriate register?
      `paragraph (2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (2) applies to the person?
      `regulation 56A applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulation 56A applies to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(1), does the prohibition on acting as a business that has to be registered apply to me` IS
    `reg 56(1) the prohibition on acting as the business applies to the person` `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` `the person is included in the appropriate register` `paragraph (2) applies to the person` `regulation 56A applies to the person`

-- reg 56(2): applies to a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider with an application not yet determined,
-- and to a money service business or trust or company service provider that applied before 10th January 2020.
@export Under regulation 56(2), may I carry on while my application for registration is waiting to be decided?
GIVEN `the person is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider?
      `the person is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a money service business or a trust or company service provider?
      `the person has applied for registration in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for registration in the register?
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply for registration?
      `the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application not yet been determined by the registering authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(2), may I carry on while my application for registration is waiting to be decided` IS
    `reg 56(2) paragraph (2) applies to the person` `the person is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` `the person is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` `the person has applied for registration in the register` `the date of the application` `the application has not yet been determined`

-- reg 56(3): a relevant person registered with the Commissioners under the 2007 Regulations is treated as included for the 12 months from commencement (26 June 2017), and after that if it has provided the additional information within those 12 months.
@export Under regulation 56(3), am I treated as included in the appropriate register on this day, because I was registered under the 2007 Regulations?
GIVEN `the person is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the person provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(3), am I treated as included in the appropriate register on this day, because I was registered under the 2007 Regulations` IS
    `reg 56(3) the person is treated as included in the appropriate register on the day` `the person is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` `the day in question` `the person provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came into force`

-- reg 56(4).
@export Under regulation 56(4), am I treated as included in the FCA register of Annex 1 financial institutions, because I was registered under the 2007 Regulations?
GIVEN `the person is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(4), am I treated as included in the FCA register of Annex 1 financial institutions, because I was registered under the 2007 Regulations` IS
    `reg 56(4) the person is treated as included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 55(1)` `the person is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`

-- reg 56(5): a person newly required to register must not carry on for more than 12 months from the date the register is established or the amendment takes effect, unless registered or an application is pending, or an art market participant or letting agent (who are dealt with in 56(6)).
@export Under regulation 56(5), may I carry on my business or profession on this day, when a register has been newly established for it?
GIVEN `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations?
      `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register?
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined?
      `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an art market participant or a letting agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(5), may I carry on my business or profession on this day, when a register has been newly established for it` IS
    `reg 56(5) the relevant person may carry on the business or profession on the day` `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` `the day in question` `the person is included in the register` `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`

-- reg 56(5) in its own polarity: the prohibition applies only after the first 12 months, and only where a register has been established or an amendment takes effect; it does not apply to a person on the register, with an application pending, or an art market participant or letting agent.
@export Under regulation 56(5), does the prohibition on carrying on my business or profession apply to me on this day, when a register has been newly established for it?
GIVEN `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations?
      `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register?
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined?
      `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an art market participant or a letting agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56(5), does the prohibition on carrying on my business or profession apply to me on this day, when a register has been newly established for it` IS
    `reg 56(5) the prohibition on carrying on the business or profession applies to the relevant person on the day` `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` `the day in question` `the person is included in the register` `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`

