      `it was carrying on business as such in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was carrying on business as such in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56A(2), am I an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 56A(2) the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` `it was carrying on business as such in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020`

-- reg 56A(1): regulation 56 does not apply to an existing cryptoasset business until the earliest of (a) the day it is included in the register, (b) the day a decision not to register takes effect, and (c) 10th January 2021 unless the FCA gave notice under 59(3) or the 59(3A) period has not expired.
@export Under regulation 56A(1), does regulation 56 (the duty to be registered) not yet apply to me on this day, as an existing cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `whether this has happened: the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA?
      `the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA
      `whether this has happened: the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)?
      `the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)
      `the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect?
      `whether this has happened: the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it?
      `the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it
      `before 10th January 2021 the FCA gave the person notice under regulation 59(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before 10th January 2021 the FCA gave the person notice under regulation 59(3)?
      `before 10th January 2021 the period specified in regulation 59(3A) expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before 10th January 2021 the period specified in regulation 59(3A) expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56A(1), does regulation 56 (the duty to be registered) not yet apply to me on this day, as an existing cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 56A(1) regulation 56 does not apply to the existing cryptoasset business on the day` `the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` `the day in question` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA` `the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA`) (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)` `the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)`) `the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` `the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it`) `before 10th January 2021 the FCA gave the person notice under regulation 59(3)` `before 10th January 2021 the period specified in regulation 59(3A) expired`

-- reg 56B(1): an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm must, before acting or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA.
@export Under regulation 56B(1), have I told the FCA in time that I am acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your firm an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm?
      `the day the firm began to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the firm begin to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
      `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the firm informed the FCA?
      `the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the firm informed the FCA
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(1), have I told the FCA in time that I am acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 56B(1) the firm has informed the FCA before acting or within 28 days of so doing` `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` `the day the firm began to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA` `the day the firm informed the FCA`) `the day in question`

-- reg 56B(2): paragraph (1) does not apply to a firm that was acting immediately before the full commencement day and continues to, if it informs the FCA within 30 days beginning with that day.
@export Under regulation 56B(2), is the duty in regulation 56B(1) lifted for me, because I was already acting before the full commencement day?
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your firm an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm?
      `immediately before the full commencement day the firm was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that immediately before the full commencement day the firm was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date?
      `the full commencement day` IS A DATE @desc What is the full commencement day (the Regulations do not say, so give the date from the commencement order)?
      `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such?
      `the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(2), is the duty in regulation 56B(1) lifted for me, because I was already acting before the full commencement day` IS
    `reg 56B(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the firm` `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` `immediately before the full commencement day the firm was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date` `the full commencement day` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such` `the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such`) `the day in question`

-- reg 56B(3): within 28 days beginning with the day of ceasing.
@export Under regulation 56B(3), have I told the FCA within 28 days that I have ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your firm an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm?
      `the firm ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the firm ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `the day of ceasing` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the firm cease to act?
      `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the firm informed the FCA?
      `the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the firm informed the FCA
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(3), have I told the FCA within 28 days that I have ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 56B(3) the firm has informed the FCA within 28 days beginning with the day of ceasing` `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` `the firm ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` `the day of ceasing` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the firm informed the FCA` `the day the firm informed the FCA`) `the day in question`

-- reg 56B(4): within 30 days beginning with the day of the material change or of discovering the inaccuracy.
@export Under regulation 56B(4), have I given the FCA details of a change in, or a correction to, what I told it, within 30 days?
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your firm an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm?
      `it has provided the FCA with information under regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has provided the FCA with information under regulation 56B?
      `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the firm that the information contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the firm that the information contains an inaccuracy?
      `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy)
      `whether this has happened: the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction?
      `the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(4), have I given the FCA details of a change in, or a correction to, what I told it, within 30 days` IS
    `reg 56B(4) the firm has provided the FCA with details of the change or a correction within 30 days beginning with the day` `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` `it has provided the FCA with information under regulation 56B` `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the firm that the information contains an inaccuracy` `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction` `the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction`) `the day in question`

-- reg 56B(5).
@export Under regulation 56B(5), is the information I gave the FCA under regulation 56B in the form and verified in the manner the FCA specified?
GIVEN `the information was provided to the FCA under regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information was provided to the FCA under regulation 56B?
      `it is in the form specified by the FCA and verified in the manner the FCA specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is in the form specified by the FCA and verified in the manner the FCA specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(5), is the information I gave the FCA under regulation 56B in the form and verified in the manner the FCA specified` IS
    `reg 56B(5) the information is in the form and verified in the manner the FCA may specify` `the information was provided to the FCA under regulation 56B` `it is in the form specified by the FCA and verified in the manner the FCA specified`

-- reg 56B(6).
@export Under regulation 56B(6), is a requirement imposed on me by regulation 56B treated as a requirement imposed by or under FSMA?
GIVEN `it is a requirement imposed by regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a requirement imposed by regulation 56B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 56B(6), is a requirement imposed on me by regulation 56B treated as a requirement imposed by or under FSMA` IS
    `reg 56B(6) the requirement is to be treated as if it were a requirement imposed by or under FSMA` `it is a requirement imposed by regulation 56B`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Applying to be registered (regs 57 to 59)`
-- Situation: asked of a business applying to the FCA or the Commissioners for registration
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 57(1).
@export Under regulation 57(1), have I made my application for registration in the manner, and with the information, that the registering authority specified?
GIVEN `the person is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55?
      `the applicant made the application in the manner, and provided the information, that the registering authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant made the application in the manner, and provided the information, that the registering authority specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(1), have I made my application for registration in the manner, and with the information, that the registering authority specified` IS
    `reg 57(1) the applicant has made the application in the manner and provided the information the registering authority may specify` `the person is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55` `the applicant made the application in the manner, and provided the information, that the registering authority specified`

-- reg 57(2): what the registering authority may specify includes the listed items (the list is not closed).  "Where" items are JUST FALSE when the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05).
@export Under regulation 57(2), may the registering authority ask me for this item of information?
GIVEN `the item of information` IS A `reg 57(2) item of information` @desc Which item of information are you asking about?
      `the applicant is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant an individual?
      `the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider?
      `the applicant is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a money service business?
      `the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registering authority not your supervisory authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(2), may the registering authority ask me for this item of information` IS
    `reg 57(2) the registering authority may specify the item of information` `the item of information` `the applicant is an individual` `the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` `the applicant is a money service business` `the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant`

-- reg 57(3).
@export Under regulation 57(3), may the registering authority require me to provide further information before it decides my application?
GIVEN `the registering authority has received the application and has not yet determined it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority has received the application and has not yet determined it?
      `the information is what the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is what the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(3), may the registering authority require me to provide further information before it decides my application` IS
    `reg 57(3) the registering authority may require the applicant to provide further information` `the registering authority has received the application and has not yet determined it` `the information is what the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application`

-- reg 57(3): 21 days beginning with the date of issue; the last day is the 21st day counting the date of issue as the first (convention (d)).
@export Under regulation 57(3), have I provided the further information within 21 days beginning with the day the requirement was issued?
GIVEN `the day the requirement is issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the day the requirement is issued)
      `whether this has happened: the day the applicant provided the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the applicant provided the information?
      `the day the applicant provided the information` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the applicant provided the information
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(3), have I provided the further information within 21 days beginning with the day the requirement was issued` IS
    `reg 57(3) the applicant has provided the further information within 21 days beginning with the date on which the requirement is issued` `the day the requirement is issued` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the applicant provided the information` `the day the applicant provided the information`) `the day in question`

-- reg 57(4): within 30 days beginning with the day of the change or the discovery, or within such later time as may be agreed.
@export Under regulation 57(4), have I given the registering authority details of a change in, or a correction to, my application information in time?
GIVEN `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)?
      `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy?
      `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy)
      `whether this has happened: a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: a later time has been agreed with the registering authority?
      `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- a later time has been agreed with the registering authority
      `whether this has happened: the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction?
      `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(4), have I given the registering authority details of a change in, or a correction to, my application information in time` IS
    `reg 57(4) the applicant has provided the registering authority with details of the change or a correction in time` `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)` `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy` `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority`) (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction`) `the day in question`

-- reg 57(6).
@export Under regulation 57(6), is the information I give the registering authority in the form and verified in the manner it specified?
GIVEN `the information is to be provided to the registering authority under regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is to be provided to the registering authority under regulation 57?
      `it is in the form specified by the registering authority and verified in the manner it specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is in the form specified by the registering authority and verified in the manner it specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 57(6), is the information I give the registering authority in the form and verified in the manner it specified` IS
    `reg 57(6) the information is in the form and verified in the manner the registering authority may specify` `the information is to be provided to the registering authority under regulation 57` `it is in the form specified by the registering authority and verified in the manner it specified`

-- reg 58(1): it must refuse if it is satisfied that the applicant, an officer or manager, a beneficial owner or (for a money service business) an agent is not fit and proper.
@export Under regulation 58(1), must the registering authority refuse to register me as a money service business or trust or company service provider?
GIVEN `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider?
      `the applicant is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a money service business?
      `the registering authority is satisfied that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is satisfied that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business?
      `the registering authority is satisfied that an officer or manager of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is satisfied that an officer or manager of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business?
      `the registering authority is satisfied that a beneficial owner of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is satisfied that a beneficial owner of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business?
      `the registering authority is satisfied that an agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business, or an officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent, is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is satisfied that an agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business, or an officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent, is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58(1), must the registering authority refuse to register me as a money service business or trust or company service provider` IS
    `reg 58(1) the registering authority must refuse to register the applicant` `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider` `the applicant is a money service business` `the registering authority is satisfied that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` `the registering authority is satisfied that an officer or manager of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` `the registering authority is satisfied that a beneficial owner of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` `the registering authority is satisfied that an agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business, or an officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent, is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business`

-- reg 58(2): where the FCA has decided to maintain a register of Annex I financial institutions, paragraph (1) applies to such an applicant as to a money service business.
@export Under regulation 58(2), does regulation 58(1) apply to me as an Annex I financial institution?
GIVEN `the FCA has decided to maintain a register of Annex I financial institutions under regulation 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has decided to maintain a register of Annex I financial institutions under regulation 55?
      `the applicant is an Annex I financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is an Annex I financial institution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58(2), does regulation 58(1) apply to me as an Annex I financial institution` IS
    `reg 58(2) paragraph (1) applies to the applicant as it applies to a money service business and a trust or company service provider` `the FCA has decided to maintain a register of Annex I financial institutions under regulation 55` `the applicant is an Annex I financial institution`

-- reg 58(3).  Whether the offence is one that Schedule 3 lists is the Schedule's answer (seam S-5); you say Yes, No or not sure.
@export Under regulation 58(3), am I to be treated as not fit and proper because I have been convicted of a criminal offence listed in Schedule 3?
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has been convicted of a criminal offence?
      `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58(3), am I to be treated as not fit and proper because I have been convicted of a criminal offence listed in Schedule 3` IS
    `reg 58(3) the person is to be treated as not being a fit and proper person to carry on the business` `the person has been convicted of a criminal offence` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence`)

-- reg 58(4): if paragraph (3) does not apply, the registering authority must have regard to three factors.
@export Under regulation 58(4), has the registering authority had regard to the factors it must consider in deciding whether I am fit and proper?
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (3) applies to the person?
      `the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations or of the Money Laundering Regulations 2001, 2003 or 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations or of the Money Laundering Regulations 2001, 2003 or 2007?
      `the registering authority has had regard to the risk that the applicant's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority has had regard to the risk that the applicant's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the applicant, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the applicant, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58(4), has the registering authority had regard to the factors it must consider in deciding whether I am fit and proper` IS
    `reg 58(4) the registering authority has had regard to the factors` `paragraph (3) applies to the person` `the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations or of the Money Laundering Regulations 2001, 2003 or 2007` `the registering authority has had regard to the risk that the applicant's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` `the registering authority has had regard to whether the applicant, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the applicant, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity`

-- reg 58(5): where the applicant is a money service business, the authority may take account of the opinion of the applicant.
@export Under regulation 58(5), may the registering authority take account of my own opinion, as a money service business, on whether I am fit and proper?
GIVEN `the applicant is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a money service business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58(5), may the registering authority take account of my own opinion, as a money service business, on whether I am fit and proper` IS
    `reg 58(5) the registering authority may take account of the opinion of the applicant` `the applicant is a money service business`

-- reg 58A(2): A must be fit and proper, and so must every officer, manager and beneficial owner of A.
@export Under regulation 58A(2), do I meet the fit and proper requirement for a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `A is a fit and proper person to carry on the business of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that A is a fit and proper person to carry on the business of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, as the case may be?
      `every officer, manager and beneficial owner of A is a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that every officer, manager and beneficial owner of A is a fit and proper person to carry on that business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58A(2), do I meet the fit and proper requirement for a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 58A(2) A meets the requirement` `A is a fit and proper person to carry on the business of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, as the case may be` `every officer, manager and beneficial owner of A is a fit and proper person to carry on that business`

-- reg 58A(1): the FCA must refuse if A does not meet the requirement in paragraph (2).  Whether you meet it is the answer to the question on regulation 58A(2).
@export Under regulation 58A(1), must the FCA refuse to register me as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54(1A) as a cryptoasset exchange provider or as a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54(1A) as a cryptoasset exchange provider or as a custodian wallet provider?
      `A meets the requirement in paragraph (2)` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: A meets the requirement in paragraph (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58A(1), must the FCA refuse to register me as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 58A(1) the FCA must refuse to register the applicant` `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54(1A) as a cryptoasset exchange provider or as a custodian wallet provider` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `A meets the requirement in paragraph (2)`)

-- reg 58A(3).
@export Under regulation 58A(3), am I to be treated as not fit and proper because I have been convicted of a Schedule 3 offence, as a cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the person has been convicted of a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has been convicted of a criminal offence?
      `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58A(3), am I to be treated as not fit and proper because I have been convicted of a Schedule 3 offence, as a cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 58A(3) the person is to be treated as not being a fit and proper person` `the person has been convicted of a criminal offence` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence`)

-- reg 58A(4).
@export Under regulation 58A(4), has the FCA had regard to the factors it must consider in deciding whether I am fit and proper?
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (3) applies to the person?
      `the FCA has had regard to whether A has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has had regard to whether A has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations?
      `the FCA has had regard to the risk that A's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has had regard to the risk that A's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `the FCA has had regard to whether A, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of A, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has had regard to whether A, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of A, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 58A(4), has the FCA had regard to the factors it must consider in deciding whether I am fit and proper` IS
    `reg 58A(4) the FCA has had regard to the factors` `paragraph (3) applies to the person` `the FCA has had regard to whether A has consistently failed to comply with the requirements of these Regulations` `the FCA has had regard to the risk that A's business may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` `the FCA has had regard to whether A, and any officer, manager or beneficial owner of A, has adequate skills and experience and has acted and may be expected to act with probity`

-- reg 59(1): it may refuse if any of grounds (a) to (e) is met.
@export Under regulation 59(1), may the registering authority refuse to register me?
GIVEN `any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with?
      `it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular?
      `the applicant has failed to pay a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9, a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11, or a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the applicant has failed to pay a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9, a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11, or a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007?
      `the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority?
      `the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds?
      `the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the applicant, or a person the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers, will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the applicant, or a person the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers, will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(1), may the registering authority refuse to register me` IS
    `reg 59(1) the registering authority may refuse to register the applicant` `any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with` `it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular` `the applicant has failed to pay a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9, a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11, or a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` `the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority` `the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds` `the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the applicant, or a person the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers, will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations`

-- reg 59(2): 45 days beginning with the date they received the application or, if they required further information, the date they received it (fork F7).
@export Under regulation 59(2), have the Commissioners given me notice of their decision on my application within 45 days?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Commissioners the registering authority for your application?
      `the day the Commissioners received the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commissioners receive the application?
      `whether this has happened: the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)?
      `the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)
      `whether this has happened: the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice?
      `the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(2), have the Commissioners given me notice of their decision on my application within 45 days` IS
    `reg 59(2) the Commissioners have given the applicant notice within 45 days` `the Commissioners are the registering authority` `the day the Commissioners received the application` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` `the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)`) (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice` `the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice`) `the day in question`

-- reg 59(2): notice of the decision to register, or of the decision not to register with reasons, the right to a review and the right to appeal.
@export Under regulation 59(2), does the Commissioners' notice to me state what the regulation requires?
GIVEN `the notice states the decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the decision to register the applicant?
      `the notice states the decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for the decision, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for the decision, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(2), does the Commissioners' notice to me state what the regulation requires` IS
    `reg 59(2) the Commissioners' notice states what the paragraph requires` `the notice states the decision to register the applicant` `the notice states the decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for the decision, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99`

-- reg 59(3A): 3 months (cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers) or 45 days, beginning with the day the application, or the further information, was received.
@export Under regulation 59(3A), what is the last day of the period within which the FCA must give me notice?
GIVEN `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `the day the 3 months or 45 days begin` IS A DATE @desc What is the date? (the day the 3 months or 45 days begin)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(3A), what is the last day of the period within which the FCA must give me notice` IS
    `reg 59(3A) the last day of the period specified in this paragraph` `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` `the day the 3 months or 45 days begin`

-- reg 59(3).
@export Under regulation 59(3), has the FCA given me notice of its decision within the period in regulation 59(3A)?
GIVEN `the FCA is the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the FCA the registering authority for your application?
      `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `the day the FCA received the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the FCA receive the application?
      `whether this has happened: the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)?
      `the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)
      `whether this has happened: the day the FCA gave the applicant notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the FCA gave the applicant notice?
      `the day the FCA gave the applicant notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the FCA gave the applicant notice
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(3), has the FCA given me notice of its decision within the period in regulation 59(3A)` IS
    `reg 59(3) the FCA has given the applicant notice within the period specified in paragraph (3A)` `the FCA is the registering authority` `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` `the day the FCA received the application` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` `the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)`) (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the FCA gave the applicant notice` `the day the FCA gave the applicant notice`) `the day in question`

-- reg 59(3): notice of the decision to register, or that it is minded not to register, with reasons and the right to make representations within a period of at least 28 days.
@export Under regulation 59(3), does the FCA's notice to me state what the regulation requires?
GIVEN `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states its decision to register the applicant?
      `the notice states that it is minded not to register the applicant, the reasons for being minded to refuse, and the right to make representations to it within a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states that it is minded not to register the applicant, the reasons for being minded to refuse, and the right to make representations to it within a specified period?
      `the period specified for representations, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the notice give for making representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(3), does the FCA's notice to me state what the regulation requires` IS
    `reg 59(3) the FCA's notice states what the paragraph requires` `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` `the notice states that it is minded not to register the applicant, the reasons for being minded to refuse, and the right to make representations to it within a specified period` `the period specified for representations, in days`

-- reg 59(4).
@export Under regulation 59(4), has the FCA decided my application and given me notice, after the period for representations?
GIVEN `the period for representations has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period for representations has expired?
      `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA decided within a reasonable period?
      `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states its decision to register the applicant?
      `the notice states its decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for its decision, and the right to appeal under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states its decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for its decision, and the right to appeal under regulation 93?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(4), has the FCA decided my application and given me notice, after the period for representations` IS
    `reg 59(4) the FCA has decided and given the applicant notice` `the period for representations has expired` `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` `the notice states its decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for its decision, and the right to appeal under regulation 93`

-- reg 59(5).
@export Under regulation 59(5), has the registering authority included me in the register as soon as practicable after deciding to register me?
GIVEN `the registering authority has decided to register the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority has decided to register the person?
      `it included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(5), has the registering authority included me in the register as soon as practicable after deciding to register me` IS
    `reg 59(5) the registering authority has included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable` `the registering authority has decided to register the person` `it included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable`

-- reg 59(6)(a).
@export Under regulation 59(6)(a), may the registering authority publish information about its decision not to register me?
GIVEN `the registering authority decides not to register an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority decides not to register an applicant?
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(6)(a), may the registering authority publish information about its decision not to register me` IS
    `reg 59(6)(a) the registering authority may publish information about its decision not to register` `the registering authority decides not to register an applicant` `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`

-- reg 59(6)(b).
@export Under regulation 59(6)(b), may the FCA publish information about its decision to object to an acquisition of, or increase in control over, my cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business?
      `the FCA decides to object to the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA decides to object to the acquisition?
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(6)(b), may the FCA publish information about its decision to object to an acquisition of, or increase in control over, my cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 59(6)(b) the FCA may publish information about its decision to object to the acquisition` `the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business` `the FCA decides to object to the acquisition` `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`

-- reg 59(8): a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider included in the FCA register under regulation 54(1A).
@export Under regulation 59(8), am I a registered cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider?
      `it is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 59(8), am I a registered cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 59(8) the person is a registered cryptoasset business` `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` `it is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What may be done to my registration (reg 60)`
-- Situation: asked of a registered business, or one that expects the registering authority to consider suspending or cancelling its registration
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 60(1) and (2): if the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person (or an officer, manager, beneficial owner or agent) is not fit and proper.
@export Under regulation 60(1), may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration as a money service business, trust or company service provider or Annex 1 financial institution?
GIVEN `the registration is of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54, or of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registration is of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54, or of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55?
      `the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to it, is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to it, is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(1), may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration as a money service business, trust or company service provider or Annex 1 financial institution` IS
    `reg 60(1) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` `the registration is of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54, or of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55` `the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to it, is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58`

-- reg 60(2A).
@export Under regulation 60(2A), may the FCA suspend or cancel my registration as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
GIVEN `the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
      `the FCA is satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA is satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(2A), may the FCA suspend or cancel my registration as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS
    `reg 60(2A) the FCA may suspend or cancel the registration` `the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` `the FCA is satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)`

-- reg 60(3).
@export Under regulation 60(3), may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration because a ground for refusing registration appears, or because I failed to comply with a regulation 66 notice?
GIVEN `the registration is in a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registration is in a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55?
      `it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply?
      `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(3), may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration because a ground for refusing registration appears, or because I failed to comply with a regulation 66 notice` IS
    `reg 60(3) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` `the registration is in a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55` `it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply` `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66`

-- reg 60(4).
@export Under regulation 60(4), may the Commissioners suspend or cancel my registration because I did not provide the additional information within 12 months of the commencement of the Regulations?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Commissioners the registering authority for your application?
      `the person was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007?
      `the person has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date these Regulations came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date these Regulations came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(4), may the Commissioners suspend or cancel my registration because I did not provide the additional information within 12 months of the commencement of the Regulations` IS
    `reg 60(4) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` `the Commissioners are the registering authority` `the person was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` `the person has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date these Regulations came into force`

-- reg 60(5).
@export Under regulation 60(5), may the Commissioners suspend or cancel my registration as a money service business that is providing a payment service without being on the FCA payment services register?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Commissioners the registering authority for your application?
      `the registration is of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registration is of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)?
      `the money service business is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the money service business is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so?
      `it is not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `it is a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or a person to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or a person to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(5), may the Commissioners suspend or cancel my registration as a money service business that is providing a payment service without being on the FCA payment services register` IS
    `reg 60(5) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` `the Commissioners are the registering authority` `the registration is of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)` `the money service business is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so` `it is not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` `it is a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or a person to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies`

-- reg 60(1) to (5) taken together (hand-gathered per ruling E1: the text gives five separate powers and no composite).  The power exists if any route gives it; a route outside its scope answers NOTHING.
@export Under regulation 60, may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration by any route in the regulation?
GIVEN `60(1): the registration is of a money service business, trust or company service provider or Annex 1 financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registration that of a money service business or trust or company service provider (regulation 54), or of an Annex 1 financial institution (regulation 55)?
      `60(1): the registering authority is satisfied the registered person is not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registering authority satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1), is not fit and proper?
      `60(2A): the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registration that of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider?
      `60(2A): the FCA is satisfied the registered person does not meet the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the FCA satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)?
      `60(3): the registration is in a register kept by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registration in a register that the registering authority keeps under regulation 54 or 55?
      `60(3): it appears that a ground in regulation 59(1)(a) to (e) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the authority that a ground in regulation 59(1)(a) to (e) applies?
      `60(3): the person has failed to comply with a regulation 66 notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66?
      `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Commissioners the registering authority?
      `60(4): the person was on the Commissioners' register under the 2007 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the 2007 Regulations?
      `60(4): the person has not provided the additional information in 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not provided the additional information required under regulation 57 within the 12 months beginning with the date the Regulations came into force?
      `60(5): the registration is of a money service business under regulation 54(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registration that of a money service business in the Commissioners' register under regulation 54(2)(b)?
      `60(5): it is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money service business providing, or purporting to provide, a payment service in the United Kingdom?
      `60(5): it is not on the FCA payment services register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not included in the FCA register of payment service providers under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `60(5): it is a person excluded by the Payment Services Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or one to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60, may the registering authority suspend or cancel my registration by any route in the regulation` IS
    `reg 60 the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration by any route` (`reg 60(1) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` `60(1): the registration is of a money service business, trust or company service provider or Annex 1 financial institution` `60(1): the registering authority is satisfied the registered person is not fit and proper`) (`reg 60(2A) the FCA may suspend or cancel the registration` `60(2A): the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` `60(2A): the FCA is satisfied the registered person does not meet the requirement`) (`reg 60(3) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` `60(3): the registration is in a register kept by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55` `60(3): it appears that a ground in regulation 59(1)(a) to (e) applies` `60(3): the person has failed to comply with a regulation 66 notice`) (`reg 60(4) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` `the Commissioners are the registering authority` `60(4): the person was on the Commissioners' register under the 2007 Regulations` `60(4): the person has not provided the additional information in 12 months`) (`reg 60(5) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` `the Commissioners are the registering authority` `60(5): the registration is of a money service business under regulation 54(2)(b)` `60(5): it is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom` `60(5): it is not on the FCA payment services register` `60(5): it is a person excluded by the Payment Services Regulations`)

-- reg 60(7): the decision and its date of effect, the period of any suspension, the reasons, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99.
@export Under regulation 60(7), does the Commissioners' notice to me of their decision to suspend or cancel my registration state what the regulation requires?
GIVEN `the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration?
      `the notice states the decision and the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the decision and the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect?
      `a period of suspension is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a period of suspension is appropriate?
      `the notice states the period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the period of the suspension?
      `the notice states the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the reasons for the decision?
      `the notice states the right to a review under regulation 94` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the right to a review under regulation 94?
      `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 99` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 99?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(7), does the Commissioners' notice to me of their decision to suspend or cancel my registration state what the regulation requires` IS
    `reg 60(7) the Commissioners' notice states what the paragraph requires` `the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration` `the notice states the decision and the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect` `a period of suspension is appropriate` `the notice states the period of the suspension` `the notice states the reasons for the decision` `the notice states the right to a review under regulation 94` `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 99`

-- reg 60(8): that it is so minded, the proposed period of any suspension, the reasons, and the right to make representations within a period of at least 28 days.
@export Under regulation 60(8), does the FCA's notice that it is minded to suspend or cancel my registration state what the regulation requires?
GIVEN `the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration?
      `the notice states that it is so minded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states that it is so minded?
      `a period of suspension is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a period of suspension is appropriate?
      `the notice states the proposed period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the proposed period of the suspension?
      `the notice states the reasons for being so minded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the reasons for being so minded?
      `the notice states the right to make representations within the period specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the right to make representations within the period specified in the notice?
      `the period specified for representations, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the notice give for making representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(8), does the FCA's notice that it is minded to suspend or cancel my registration state what the regulation requires` IS
    `reg 60(8) the FCA's notice states what the paragraph requires` `the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration` `the notice states that it is so minded` `a period of suspension is appropriate` `the notice states the proposed period of the suspension` `the notice states the reasons for being so minded` `the notice states the right to make representations within the period specified in the notice` `the period specified for representations, in days`

-- reg 60(9).
@export Under regulation 60(9), has the FCA decided whether to suspend or cancel my registration, and given me notice, after the period for representations?
GIVEN `the FCA has given the notice under paragraph (8) and the period for representations has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA has given the notice under paragraph (8) and the period for representations has expired?
      `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the FCA decided within a reasonable period?
      `the notice states its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration?
      `the notice states its decision to suspend or cancel the registration and the date from which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states its decision to suspend or cancel the registration and the date from which it takes effect?
      `the notice states the period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the period of the suspension?
      `the notice states the reasons for its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the reasons for its decision?
      `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 93?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(9), has the FCA decided whether to suspend or cancel my registration, and given me notice, after the period for representations` IS
    `reg 60(9) the FCA has decided and given the person notice` `the FCA has given the notice under paragraph (8) and the period for representations has expired` `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` `the notice states its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration` `the notice states its decision to suspend or cancel the registration and the date from which it takes effect` `the notice states the period of the suspension` `the notice states the reasons for its decision` `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 93`

-- reg 60(10): if the authority considers that the interests of the public require it and the notice says so with reasons.
@export Under regulation 60(10), does the suspension or cancellation of my registration take effect when the notice is given?
GIVEN `the registering authority considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation to have immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation to have immediate effect?
      `the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(10), does the suspension or cancellation of my registration take effect when the notice is given` IS
    `reg 60(10) the suspension or cancellation takes effect when the notice is given` `the registering authority considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation to have immediate effect` `the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it`

-- reg 60(11).
@export Under regulation 60(11), may the registering authority publish information about its decision to suspend or cancel my registration?
GIVEN `the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person's registration?
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 60(11), may the registering authority publish information about its decision to suspend or cancel my registration` IS
    `reg 60(11) the registering authority may publish information about its decision` `the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person's registration` `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`

