§§ `Who supervises my transfers of funds (regs 61 to 64)`
-- Situation: asked of a payment service provider
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 62(1): the FCA is the authority for authorised persons, authorised and registered small payment institutions (not on the Commissioners' register) and authorised and registered small electronic money institutions.
@export Under regulation 62(1), is the FCA my transfer of funds supervisory authority?
GIVEN `I am a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a payment service provider?
      `I am an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised person under FSMA?
      `I am an authorised payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am a registered small payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)?
      `I am an authorised electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `I am a registered small electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 62(1), is the FCA my transfer of funds supervisory authority` IS
    `reg 62(1) the FCA is the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the payment service provider` (`reg 62 payment service provider` OF `I am a payment service provider`, `I am an authorised person`, `I am an authorised payment institution`, `I am a registered small payment institution`, `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`, `I am an authorised electronic money institution`, `I am a registered small electronic money institution`)

-- reg 62(2): the Commissioners are the authority for payment service providers who do not come within paragraph (1).  Whether you come within paragraph (1) is read from the same facts as the question on regulation 62(1).
@export Under regulation 62(2), are the Commissioners my transfer of funds supervisory authority?
GIVEN `I am a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a payment service provider?
      `I am an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised person under FSMA?
      `I am an authorised payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am a registered small payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)?
      `I am an authorised electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `I am a registered small electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 62(2), are the Commissioners my transfer of funds supervisory authority` IS
    `reg 62(2) the Commissioners are the transfer of funds supervisory authority for the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` (`reg 62 payment service provider` OF `I am a payment service provider`, `I am an authorised person`, `I am an authorised payment institution`, `I am a registered small payment institution`, `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`, `I am an authorised electronic money institution`, `I am a registered small electronic money institution`)

-- reg 61 "transfer of funds supervisory authority" (hand-gathered per ruling E1: the definition names the authority by pointing at regulation 62(1) and (2)).
@export Under regulation 61, is the FCA my transfer of funds supervisory authority?
GIVEN `I am a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a payment service provider?
      `I am an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised person under FSMA?
      `I am an authorised payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am a registered small payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)?
      `I am an authorised electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `I am a registered small electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 61, is the FCA my transfer of funds supervisory authority` IS
    `reg 53 whether the answer is the authority` (`reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` (`reg 62 payment service provider` OF `I am a payment service provider`, `I am an authorised person`, `I am an authorised payment institution`, `I am a registered small payment institution`, `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`, `I am an authorised electronic money institution`, `I am a registered small electronic money institution`)) `the Financial Conduct Authority`

-- reg 61 "transfer of funds supervisory authority" (hand-gathered per ruling E1).
@export Under regulation 61, are the Commissioners my transfer of funds supervisory authority?
GIVEN `I am a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a payment service provider?
      `I am an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised person under FSMA?
      `I am an authorised payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am a registered small payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small payment institution under the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)?
      `I am an authorised electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an authorised electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
      `I am a registered small electronic money institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered small electronic money institution under the Electronic Money Regulations 2011?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 61, are the Commissioners my transfer of funds supervisory authority` IS
    `reg 53 whether the answer is the authority` (`reg 61 the transfer of funds supervisory authority of the provider, read from the provider's own limbs` (`reg 62 payment service provider` OF `I am a payment service provider`, `I am an authorised person`, `I am an authorised payment institution`, `I am a registered small payment institution`, `I am included in the register of the Commissioners under regulation 54(2)`, `I am an authorised electronic money institution`, `I am a registered small electronic money institution`)) `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`

-- reg 63(2): applies to a payment service provider established in the United Kingdom but with its head office elsewhere, or with its head office in the United Kingdom but established elsewhere.
@export Under regulation 63(2), does paragraph (2) of regulation 63 apply to me, because I am established or have my head office in the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom?
      `the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(2), does paragraph (2) of regulation 63 apply to me, because I am established or have my head office in the United Kingdom` IS
    `reg 63(2) paragraph (2) applies to the payment service provider` `the payment service provider is established in the United Kingdom` `the payment service provider has its head office in the United Kingdom`

-- reg 63(3).
@export Under regulation 63(3), may co-operation with other authorities include sharing information about me?
GIVEN `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(3), may co-operation with other authorities include sharing information about me` IS
    `reg 63(3) co-operation may include the sharing of the information` `it is information which the supervisory authority is not prevented from disclosing`

-- reg 63(5).
@export Under regulation 63(5), must my transfer of funds supervisory authority tell the National Crime Agency if it knows or suspects that I have engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVEN `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(5), must my transfer of funds supervisory authority tell the National Crime Agency if it knows or suspects that I have engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS
    `reg 63(5) the authority must inform the NCA` `it knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a payment service provider is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`

-- reg 63(6).
@export Under regulation 63(6), is a disclosure about me made under regulation 63(5) a breach of any restriction on disclosing information?
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(6), is a disclosure about me made under regulation 63(5) a breach of any restriction on disclosing information` IS
    `reg 63(6) the disclosure is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information` `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)`

-- reg 63(7).
@export Under regulation 63(7), is the person who made a good faith disclosure about me under regulation 63(5) free of civil liability?
GIVEN `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)?
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was made in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(7), is the person who made a good faith disclosure about me under regulation 63(5) free of civil liability` IS
    `reg 63(7) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the person who made it` `the disclosure was made under paragraph (5)` `it was made in good faith`

-- reg 63(8).
@export Under regulation 63(8), is the exercise of this function treated as a function of the FCA under FSMA?
GIVEN `it is a function of the FCA under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a function of the FCA under this Part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(8), is the exercise of this function treated as a function of the FCA under FSMA` IS
    `reg 63(8) the function is treated as a function conferred on the FCA under FSMA for the purposes of section 1A of, and Parts 1, 2 and 4 of Schedule 1ZA to, FSMA` `it is a function of the FCA under this Part`

-- reg 63(10): "and" between the limbs read as "or" (fork F2).
@export Under regulation 63(10), is this body an overseas authority for the purposes of regulation 63?
GIVEN `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation?
      `the body is in an EEA state in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is in an EEA state in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office?
      `the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state?
      `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 63(10), is this body an overseas authority for the purposes of regulation 63` IS
    `reg 63(10) the body is an overseas authority` `the body is responsible for any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation` `the body is in an EEA state in which the payment service provider is established or has its head office` `the payment service provider is established or has its head office in another country which is not an EEA state` `the body is in that country and has functions equivalent to any of the functions provided for in the funds transfer regulation`

-- reg 64(3): a financial investigator accredited under section 3 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, a person acting for the Scottish Ministers as an enforcement authority, or a constable or equivalent officer.
