§§ `Cryptoasset transfers: what must travel with them (regs 64A to 64H)`
-- Situation: asked of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider (a cryptoasset business)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- reg 64A(1) with (2) and (3) (hand-gathered per ruling E1: paragraph (1) takes the answers of (2) and (3)).  Part 7A applies to inter-cryptoasset business transfers and unhosted wallet transfers, unless excluded.
@export Under regulation 64A(1), does Part 7A of the Regulations apply to this cryptoasset transfer?
GIVEN `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses?
      `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve making a cryptoasset of an originator available to a beneficiary?
      `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses is carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is at least one of the cryptoasset businesses carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction?
      `it is a transfer from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary?
      `it is a transfer to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary?
      `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary?
      `it is a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation?
      `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each of the originator and the beneficiary a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64A(1), does Part 7A of the Regulations apply to this cryptoasset transfer` IS
    `reg 64A(1) this Part applies in respect of the cryptoasset transfer` (`reg 64B the transaction is a cryptoasset transfer` (`reg 64B the transaction is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses` `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary` `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses is carrying on business in the United Kingdom`) (`reg 64B the transfer is an unhosted wallet transfer` `it is a transfer from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` `it is a transfer to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary` `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary`)) (`reg 64A(2) this Part applies in respect of the transfer` `it is a transfer of funds within the meaning of Article 3.9 of the funds transfer regulation`) (`reg 64A(3) this Part applies to the cryptoasset transfer` `both the originator and the beneficiary is a cryptoasset business acting on its own behalf`)

-- reg 64B "cryptoasset business": a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, am I a cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider?
      `the person is a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a custodian wallet provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, am I a cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 64B the person is a cryptoasset business` `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider` `the person is a custodian wallet provider`

-- reg 64B "originator": a person who owns a cryptoasset and allows a transfer of it (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, am I an originator of this cryptoasset transfer?
GIVEN `the person owns a cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person owns a cryptoasset?
      `the person allows a transfer of that cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person allows a transfer of that cryptoasset?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, am I an originator of this cryptoasset transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the person is an originator` `the person owns a cryptoasset` `the person allows a transfer of that cryptoasset`

-- reg 64B "beneficiary": the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, am I the beneficiary of this cryptoasset transfer?
GIVEN `the person is the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, am I the beneficiary of this cryptoasset transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the person is a beneficiary` `the person is the intended recipient of a cryptoasset from an originator`

-- reg 64B "intermediary cryptoasset business": a cryptoasset business that is not acting for the originator or the beneficiary and that receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, am I an intermediary cryptoasset business in this transfer?
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a cryptoasset business?
      `in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it is acting for the originator or the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it is acting for the originator or the beneficiary?
      `it receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, am I an intermediary cryptoasset business in this transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` `the person is a cryptoasset business` `in the course of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer it is acting for the originator or the beneficiary` `it receives and transmits a cryptoasset on behalf of a cryptoasset business`

-- reg 64B "inter-cryptoasset business transfer": a transaction by two or more cryptoasset businesses making a cryptoasset of an originator available to a beneficiary, provided at least one carries on business in the United Kingdom in respect of it (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, is this an inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
GIVEN `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses?
      `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary?
      `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, is this an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the transaction is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `it is a transaction carried out by two or more cryptoasset businesses` `it involves the making available of a cryptoasset of an originator to a beneficiary` `at least one of the cryptoasset businesses involved is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction`

-- reg 64B "unhosted wallet transfer": a transfer from an unhosted wallet to the beneficiary's cryptoasset business, or from the originator's cryptoasset business to the beneficiary's unhosted wallet, with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, is this an unhosted wallet transfer?
GIVEN `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary?
      `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary?
      `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, is this an unhosted wallet transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the transfer is an unhosted wallet transfer` `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by an originator from an unhosted wallet to the cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` `it is the transfer of a cryptoasset by the cryptoasset business of the originator to the unhosted wallet of a beneficiary` `it is made with a view to making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary`

-- reg 64B "batch file transfer" (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, is this a batch file transfer?
GIVEN `it is a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator?
      `it was put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, is this a batch file transfer` IS
    `reg 64B the transfer is a batch file transfer` `it is a bundle of individual inter-cryptoasset business transfers from a single originator` `it was put together by a cryptoasset business of the originator for transmission to a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary or beneficiaries`

-- reg 64B "unique transaction identifier" (closed).
@export Under regulation 64B, is this combination a unique transaction identifier?
GIVEN `it is a combination of letters, numbers or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a combination of letters, numbers or symbols?
      `it is determined by a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is determined by a cryptoasset business?
      `it permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, is this combination a unique transaction identifier` IS
    `reg 64B the combination is a unique transaction identifier` `it is a combination of letters, numbers or symbols` `it is determined by a cryptoasset business` `it permits the traceability of the transaction from the originator to the beneficiary`

-- reg 64B "working day": not a Saturday, Sunday, Good Friday or bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom (fork F3: defined for Part 7A only).
@export Under regulation 64B, is this day a working day?
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the day is a Good Friday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a Good Friday?
      `the day is a bank holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in any part of the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64B, is this day a working day` IS
    `reg 64B the day is a working day` `day` (`reg 64B the list of one optional day` `the day is a Good Friday` `day`) (`reg 64B the list of one optional day` `the day is a bank holiday` `day`)

-- reg 64C(5): names; the registered or trading name of a firm; account numbers, or the unique transaction identifier where there is no account number.
@export Under regulation 64C(5), does the information that accompanies the transfer meet paragraph (5)?
GIVEN `the names of the originator and the beneficiary are given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the names of the originator and the beneficiary are given?
      `the originator or the beneficiary is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the originator or the beneficiary is a firm?
      `the registered name is given, or if there is no registered name the trading name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the registered name is given, or if there is no registered name the trading name?
      `the account numbers of the originator and the beneficiary are given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the account numbers of the originator and the beneficiary are given?
      `there is no account number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is no account number?
      `the unique transaction identifier is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the unique transaction identifier is given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(5), does the information that accompanies the transfer meet paragraph (5)` IS
    `reg 64C(5) the information specified in this paragraph is provided` `the names of the originator and the beneficiary are given` `the originator or the beneficiary is a firm` `the registered name is given, or if there is no registered name the trading name` `the account numbers of the originator and the beneficiary are given` `there is no account number` `the unique transaction identifier is given`

-- reg 64C(6): for a firm, the customer identification number or the address of its registered office or principal place of business; for an individual, the customer identification number or one of the address, identity document number, or date and place of birth.
@export Under regulation 64C(6), does the information that accompanies the transfer meet paragraph (6)?
GIVEN `the originator is a firm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the originator is a firm?
      `the customer identification number is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the customer identification number is given?
      `the address of the originator's registered office, or if different or if there is none its principal place of business, is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the address of the originator's registered office, or if different or if there is none its principal place of business, is given?
      `the individual's address is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual's address is given?
      `the individual's birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual's birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number is given?
      `the individual's date and place of birth are given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual's date and place of birth are given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(6), does the information that accompanies the transfer meet paragraph (6)` IS
    `reg 64C(6) the information specified in this paragraph is provided` `the originator is a firm` `the customer identification number is given` `the address of the originator's registered office, or if different or if there is none its principal place of business, is given` `the individual's address is given` `the individual's birth certificate number, passport number or national identity card number is given` `the individual's date and place of birth are given`

-- reg 64C(1).  Answer the question on regulation 64C(5) to know whether the information meets paragraph (5).
@export Under regulation 64C(1), have I, as the cryptoasset business of the originator, ensured that the transfer is accompanied by the paragraph (5) information?
GIVEN `the transfer is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `the cryptoasset business is the cryptoasset business of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business is the cryptoasset business of the originator?
      `the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(1), have I, as the cryptoasset business of the originator, ensured that the transfer is accompanied by the paragraph (5) information` IS
    `reg 64C(1) the cryptoasset business of the originator has ensured that the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)` `the transfer is an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `the cryptoasset business is the cryptoasset business of the originator` `the transfer is accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (5)`

-- reg 64C(3): applies where each cryptoasset business executing the transfer, including any intermediary, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom.
@export Under regulation 64C(3), does paragraph (3) of regulation 64C apply to this transfer, because every cryptoasset business executing it carries on business in the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, including any intermediary cryptoasset business, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, including any intermediary cryptoasset business, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(3), does paragraph (3) of regulation 64C apply to this transfer, because every cryptoasset business executing it carries on business in the United Kingdom` IS
    `reg 64C(3) paragraph (3) applies to the transfer` `each of the cryptoasset businesses executing the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, including any intermediary cryptoasset business, is carrying on business in the United Kingdom in respect of the transaction`

-- reg 64C(2): three working days of the request (fork F5: the day of the request is not counted; the third working day after it is the last).  Paragraph (3) must apply (the question on regulation 64C(3)).
@export Under regulation 64C(2), have I provided the paragraph (6) information within three working days of the request?
GIVEN `paragraph (3) applies` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: paragraph (3) applies?
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary made a request for the information specified in paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary made a request for the information specified in paragraph (6)?
      `the day of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary make the request?
      `whether this has happened: the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information?
      `the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (any date if it has not happened) -- the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `a Good Friday falls in or near the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a Good Friday fall in or near the three working days?
      `the date of that Good Friday` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of that Good Friday? (any date if there is none)
      `a first bank holiday falls in or near the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 (in any part of the United Kingdom) fall in or near the three working days?
      `the date of the first bank holiday` IS A DATE @desc What is its date? (any date if there is none)
      `a second bank holiday falls in or near the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a second such bank holiday fall in or near the three working days?
      `the date of the second bank holiday` IS A DATE @desc What is its date? (any date if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(2), have I provided the paragraph (6) information within three working days of the request` IS
    `reg 64C(2) the cryptoasset business of the originator has provided the information specified in paragraph (6) within three working days of the request` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph (3) applies`) `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary made a request for the information specified in paragraph (6)` `the day of the request` (`reg 53 a day if it has happened` `whether this has happened: the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information` `the day the cryptoasset business of the originator provided the information`) `the day in question` (`reg 64B the list of one optional day` `a Good Friday falls in or near the period` `the date of that Good Friday`) (`reg 64B the list of two optional days` `a first bank holiday falls in or near the period` `the date of the first bank holiday` `a second bank holiday falls in or near the period` `the date of the second bank holiday`)

-- reg 64C(4): where paragraph (3) does not apply and the transfer equals or exceeds £800.  Whether paragraph (3) applies is the answer to the question on regulation 64C(3); "not sure" is read as not shown to apply (marginal reading (e)).
@export Under regulation 64C(4), have I ensured that the transfer is also accompanied by the paragraph (6) information?
GIVEN `the kind of transfer` IS A `reg 64B the sort of transfer I am asking about` @desc Is the transfer an inter-cryptoasset business transfer or an unhosted wallet transfer?
      `the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, with linked transfers taken together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, taking together any transfers that appear to be linked?
      `paragraph (3) applies` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: paragraph (3) applies?
      `the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(4), have I ensured that the transfer is also accompanied by the paragraph (6) information` IS
    `reg 64C(4) the cryptoasset business of the originator has ensured that the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)` (`reg 64A the transfer I am asking about` `the kind of transfer` `the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, with linked transfers taken together`) (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph (3) applies`) `the transfer is also accompanied by the information specified in paragraph (6)`

-- reg 64C(7): they do not, provided the beneficiary's cryptoasset business carries on business wholly outside the United Kingdom, the batch carries the information, and each individual transfer carries the originator's account number or unique transaction identifier (a flat negative: JUST FALSE).
@export Under regulation 64C(7), do paragraphs (1) and (4) of regulation 64C apply to each of the individual transfers in my batch file transfer?
GIVEN `the transfer is a batch file transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is a batch file transfer?
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)?
      `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(7), do paragraphs (1) and (4) of regulation 64C apply to each of the individual transfers in my batch file transfer` IS
    `reg 64C(7) paragraphs (1) and (4) apply to each of the individual transfers in the batch` `the transfer is a batch file transfer` `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier`

-- reg 64C(7) in its own polarity: it disapplies them in the case of a batch file transfer whose beneficiary's cryptoasset business carries on business wholly outside the United Kingdom, provided the batch carries the information and each individual transfer carries the originator's account number or unique transaction identifier; an unmet case, "where" or proviso is JUST FALSE.
@export Under regulation 64C(7), does paragraph (7) disapply paragraphs (1) and (4) of regulation 64C for each of the individual transfers in my batch file transfer?
GIVEN `the transfer is a batch file transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer is a batch file transfer?
      `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)?
      `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(7), does paragraph (7) disapply paragraphs (1) and (4) of regulation 64C for each of the individual transfers in my batch file transfer` IS
    `reg 64C(7) paragraph (7) disapplies paragraphs (1) and (4) for each of the individual transfers in the batch` `the transfer is a batch file transfer` `the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary is carrying on business wholly outside the United Kingdom` `the batch is accompanied by the information required by paragraphs (1) and (4)` `each individual transfer within the batch is accompanied by the account number of the originator, or if there is no account number, the unique transaction identifier`

-- reg 64C(8).
@export Under regulation 64C(8), has the information relating to the originator been verified as paragraph (8) requires?
GIVEN `the information relates to the originator and is required under regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information relates to the originator and is required under regulation 64C?
      `it has been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information, in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information, in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(8), has the information relating to the originator been verified as paragraph (8) requires` IS
    `reg 64C(8) the information relating to the originator has been verified` `the information relates to the originator and is required under regulation 64C` `it has been verified by the cryptoasset business of the originator on the basis of documents or information, in either case obtained from a reliable source which is independent of the person whose identity is being verified`

-- reg 64C(9): a cryptoasset business of an originator must not make the transfer before ensuring full compliance; once it has, the paragraph does not say it may, so NOTHING.
@export Under regulation 64C(9), may I, as the cryptoasset business of the originator, make the inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance with regulation 64C?
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a cryptoasset business of an originator?
      `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(9), may I, as the cryptoasset business of the originator, make the inter-cryptoasset business transfer before ensuring full compliance with regulation 64C` IS
    `reg 64C(9) the cryptoasset business of an originator may make the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C`

-- reg 64C(9) as a bar: it is in force until full compliance with regulation 64C is ensured, and then lifts.  The answer never says that you have complied.
@export Under regulation 64C(9), am I barred from making the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, as the cryptoasset business of the originator?
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a cryptoasset business of an originator?
      `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C(9), am I barred from making the inter-cryptoasset business transfer, as the cryptoasset business of the originator` IS
    `reg 64C(9) the prohibition on making the inter-cryptoasset business transfer applies` `it is a cryptoasset business of an originator` `it has ensured full compliance with regulation 64C`

-- reg 64D(1).
@export Under regulation 64D(1), have I, as the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary, made both checks before making the cryptoasset available?
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided?
      `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64D(1), have I, as the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary, made both checks before making the cryptoasset available` IS
    `reg 64D(1) the cryptoasset business has made both checks before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided` `before making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary it checked whether the information relating to the beneficiary corresponds with information verified by it under Part 3`

-- reg 64D(2): request any missing information from the originator's business, and consider enquiries, delay and return of the cryptoasset.
@export Under regulation 64D(2), have I done what the regulation requires on becoming aware of missing or non-corresponding information?
GIVEN `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary?
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3?
      `information required by regulation 64C is missing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that information required by regulation 64C is missing?
      `it has requested the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has requested the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information?
      `it has considered whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has considered whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3?
      `it has considered whether to delay making the cryptoasset available until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has considered whether to delay making the cryptoasset available until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved?
      `it has considered whether, if the information is not received or the discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has considered whether, if the information is not received or the discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64D(2), have I done what the regulation requires on becoming aware of missing or non-corresponding information` IS
    `reg 64D(2) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary has done what the paragraph requires` `it is a cryptoasset business of a beneficiary` `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing or does not correspond with information verified by it under Part 3` `information required by regulation 64C is missing` `it has requested the cryptoasset business of the originator to provide the missing information` `it has considered whether to make enquiries as to any discrepancy between information received and information verified by it under Part 3` `it has considered whether to delay making the cryptoasset available until the information is received or any discrepancy resolved` `it has considered whether, if the information is not received or the discrepancy resolved within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business of the originator`

-- reg 64D(3): the risk assessments under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1), and the level of risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing.
@export Under regulation 64D(3), have I had regard to the matters in regulation 64D(3) in assessing the risk of this transfer?
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)?
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `my assessment covered money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of money laundering?
      `my assessment covered terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of terrorist financing?
      `my assessment covered proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of proliferation financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64D(3), have I had regard to the matters in regulation 64D(3) in assessing the risk of this transfer` IS
    `reg 64D(3) the cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` (`reg 64D the kinds of risk my assessment covered` `my assessment covered money laundering` `my assessment covered terrorist financing` `my assessment covered proliferation financing`)

-- reg 64D(4).  Whether there is a business relationship is regulation 4's answer (seam S-K1); you say Yes, No or not sure.
@export Under regulation 64D(4), have I taken account of the factors in regulation 64D(4) in assessing the level of risk?
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship?
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked?
      `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary?
      `it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64D(4), have I taken account of the factors in regulation 64D(4) in assessing the level of risk` IS
    `reg 64D(4) the cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`) `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of its business relationship with the beneficiary and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the beneficiary via the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary` `it has taken account of the duration of its business relationship with the beneficiary`

-- reg 64D(5).
@export Under regulation 64D(5), have I reported to the FCA a repeated failure to provide the information regulation 64C requires?
GIVEN `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C?
      `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64D(5), have I reported to the FCA a repeated failure to provide the information regulation 64C requires` IS
    `reg 64D(5) the cryptoasset business of the beneficiary has reported the repeated failure to the FCA` `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures`

-- reg 64E(1).
@export Under regulation 64E(1), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, checked the information before further transferring the cryptoasset?
GIVEN `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an intermediary cryptoasset business and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `before further transferring the cryptoasset it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before further transferring the cryptoasset it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64E(1), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, checked the information before further transferring the cryptoasset` IS
    `reg 64E(1) the intermediary cryptoasset business has checked the information before further transferring the cryptoasset` `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business and receives a cryptoasset as part of an inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `before further transferring the cryptoasset it checked whether it has received the information required by regulation 64C to be provided`

-- reg 64E(2).
@export Under regulation 64E(2), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, done what the regulation requires on becoming aware of missing information?
GIVEN `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is an intermediary cryptoasset business?
      `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing?
      `it has requested the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has requested the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information?
      `it has considered whether to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has considered whether to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received?
      `it has considered whether, if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has considered whether, if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64E(2), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, done what the regulation requires on becoming aware of missing information` IS
    `reg 64E(2) the intermediary cryptoasset business has done what the paragraph requires` `it is an intermediary cryptoasset business` `it has become aware that information required by regulation 64C is missing` `it has requested the cryptoasset business from which it received the transfer to provide the missing information` `it has considered whether to delay the onward transfer of the cryptoasset until the information is received` `it has considered whether, if the information is not received within a reasonable time, to return the cryptoasset to the cryptoasset business from which it was received`

-- reg 64E(3).
@export Under regulation 64E(3), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, had regard to the matters in regulation 64E(3) in assessing the risk of this transfer?
GIVEN `the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)?
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `my assessment covered money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of money laundering?
      `my assessment covered terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of terrorist financing?
      `my assessment covered proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of proliferation financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64E(3), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, had regard to the matters in regulation 64E(3) in assessing the risk of this transfer` IS
    `reg 64E(3) the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` `the intermediary cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` (`reg 64D the kinds of risk my assessment covered` `my assessment covered money laundering` `my assessment covered terrorist financing` `my assessment covered proliferation financing`)

-- reg 64E(4).  Whether there is a business relationship is regulation 4's answer (seam S-K1); you say Yes, No or not sure.
@export Under regulation 64E(4), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, taken account of the factors in regulation 64E(4)?
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship?
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer?
      `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64E(4), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, taken account of the factors in regulation 64E(4)` IS
    `reg 64E(4) the intermediary cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`) `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer cryptoasset business, and of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer` `it has taken account of the value of the inter-cryptoasset business transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked`

-- reg 64E(5).
@export Under regulation 64E(5), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, reported to the FCA a repeated failure to provide the information regulation 64C requires?
GIVEN `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C?
      `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64E(5), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, reported to the FCA a repeated failure to provide the information regulation 64C requires` IS
    `reg 64E(5) the intermediary cryptoasset business has reported the repeated failure to the FCA` `there has been repeated failure by a cryptoasset business to provide information required by regulation 64C` `it has reported to the FCA the repeated failure and any steps it has taken in respect of such failures`

-- reg 64F(a).
@export Under regulation 64F(a), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, ensured that all the information also accompanies the onward transfer?
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business?
      `all the information provided in relation to the transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any requested before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all the information provided in relation to the transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any requested before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64F(a), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, ensured that all the information also accompanies the onward transfer` IS
    `reg 64F(a) the intermediary cryptoasset business has ensured that all the information also accompanies the onward transfer` `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` `all the information provided in relation to the transfer pursuant to regulation 64C, including any requested before the transfer is made under regulation 64E(2)(a), also accompanies the onward transfer`

-- reg 64F(b).
@export Under regulation 64F(b), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, sent on as soon as practicable information I received after I had transferred the cryptoasset?
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business?
      `it received information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) after it had transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) after it had transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business?
      `it sent the information on to the relevant cryptoasset business as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it sent the information on to the relevant cryptoasset business as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64F(b), have I, as an intermediary cryptoasset business, sent on as soon as practicable information I received after I had transferred the cryptoasset` IS
    `reg 64F(b) the intermediary cryptoasset business has sent the information on as soon as practicable` `the person is an intermediary cryptoasset business` `it received information requested under regulation 64E(2)(a) after it had transferred the cryptoasset to the relevant cryptoasset business` `it sent the information on to the relevant cryptoasset business as soon as practicable`

-- reg 64G(1): the paragraph (5) information it does not hold, or the paragraph (6) information about the originator where the customer is the beneficiary and the transfer is £800 or more.
@export Under regulation 64G(1), may I request this information from my customer for this unhosted wallet transfer?
GIVEN `the kind of transfer` IS A `reg 64B the sort of transfer I am asking about` @desc Is the transfer an inter-cryptoasset business transfer or an unhosted wallet transfer?
      `the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, with linked transfers taken together` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, taking together any transfers that appear to be linked?
      `the cryptoasset business is involved in the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business is involved in the transfer?
      `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(5) that it does not already hold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(5) that it does not already hold?
      `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator?
      `the customer is the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the customer is the beneficiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64G(1), may I request this information from my customer for this unhosted wallet transfer` IS
    `reg 64G(1) the cryptoasset business may request the information from its customer` (`reg 64A the transfer I am asking about` `the kind of transfer` `the value of the transfer in pounds sterling, with linked transfers taken together`) `the cryptoasset business is involved in the transfer` `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(5) that it does not already hold` `the information requested is information specified in regulation 64C(6) in respect of the originator` `the customer is the beneficiary`

-- reg 64G(2).
@export Under regulation 64G(2), have I had regard to the matters in regulation 64G(2) in assessing the risk of this unhosted wallet transfer?
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)?
      `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the unhosted wallet transfer?
      `my assessment covered money laundering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of money laundering?
      `my assessment covered terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of terrorist financing?
      `my assessment covered proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your assessment cover the risk of proliferation financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64G(2), have I had regard to the matters in regulation 64G(2) in assessing the risk of this unhosted wallet transfer` IS
    `reg 64G(2) the cryptoasset business has had regard to the matters in this paragraph` `the cryptoasset business has had regard to the risk assessments it carried out under regulations 18(1) and 18A(1)` `it has had regard to its assessment of the level of risk arising from the unhosted wallet transfer` (`reg 64D the kinds of risk my assessment covered` `my assessment covered money laundering` `my assessment covered terrorist financing` `my assessment covered proliferation financing`)

-- reg 64G(3).  Whether there is a business relationship is regulation 4's answer (seam S-K1); you say Yes, No or not sure.
@export Under regulation 64G(3), have I taken account of the factors in regulation 64G(3) in assessing the level of risk of this unhosted wallet transfer?
GIVEN `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship?
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the unhosted wallet transfer?
      `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer?
      `it has taken account of the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked?
      `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer via the cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer via the cryptoasset business?
      `it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64G(3), have I taken account of the factors in regulation 64G(3) in assessing the level of risk of this unhosted wallet transfer` IS
    `reg 64G(3) the cryptoasset business has taken account of the factors` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`) `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the unhosted wallet transfer` `it has taken account of the purpose and nature of the business relationship with its customer` `it has taken account of the value of the unhosted wallet transfer and any cryptoasset transfer which appears to be linked` `it has taken account of the frequency of cryptoasset transfers made by or to the customer via the cryptoasset business` `it has taken account of the duration of the business relationship with its customer`

-- reg 64G(4): a cryptoasset business involved in an unhosted wallet transfer that does not receive the information requested must not make the cryptoasset available.
@export Under regulation 64G(4), may I make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary when I have not received the information I requested under regulation 64G(1)?
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer?
      `it requested information under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it requested information under paragraph (1)?
      `it received the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received the information requested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64G(4), may I make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary when I have not received the information I requested under regulation 64G(1)` IS
    `reg 64G(4) the cryptoasset business may make the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary` `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` `it requested information under paragraph (1)` `it received the information requested`

-- reg 64G(4) in its own polarity: "in the event that" counts as "where", so with no request, or with the information received, the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE).
@export Under regulation 64G(4), am I barred from making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary, when I have not received the information I requested under regulation 64G(1)?
GIVEN `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer?
      `it requested information under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it requested information under paragraph (1)?
      `it received the information requested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received the information requested?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64G(4), am I barred from making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary, when I have not received the information I requested under regulation 64G(1)` IS
    `reg 64G(4) the prohibition on making the cryptoasset available to the beneficiary applies` `the cryptoasset business is involved in an unhosted wallet transfer` `it requested information under paragraph (1)` `it received the information requested`

-- seam S-14, answered by Part 7A: whether the relevant person holds information or documents received under regulation 64C, 64D or 64G, which regulation 40 asks.
@export Under regulation 64C, 64D or 64G, do I hold the information or documents I received under that regulation?
GIVEN `it received information or documents under regulation 64C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received information or documents under regulation 64C?
      `it received information or documents under regulation 64D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received information or documents under regulation 64D?
      `it received information or documents under regulation 64G` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it received information or documents under regulation 64G?
      `it holds them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it holds them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64C, 64D or 64G, do I hold the information or documents I received under that regulation` IS
    `reg 64C, 64D or 64G the relevant person holds information or documents received under that regulation` `it received information or documents under regulation 64C` `it received information or documents under regulation 64D` `it received information or documents under regulation 64G` `it holds them`

-- reg 64H.  Whether the body is a law enforcement authority is regulation 44(10)'s answer (seam S-15); you say Yes, No or not sure.
@export Under regulation 64H, have I responded fully and without delay to this written request from a law enforcement authority?
GIVEN `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` IS A `reg 53 my answer` @desc Yes, No or not sure: reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority?
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the request is in writing?
      `the information is held in connection with this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is held in connection with this Part?
      `the authority reasonably requires it in connection with the authority's functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the authority reasonably requires it in connection with the authority's functions?
      `the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 64H, have I responded fully and without delay to this written request from a law enforcement authority` IS
    `reg 64H the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay to the request` (`reg 53 what I say, as a fact` `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`) `the request is in writing` `the information is held in connection with this Part` `the authority reasonably requires it in connection with the authority's functions` `the cryptoasset business has responded fully and without delay`

-- ============================================================
-- mlr4: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Anti-Money Laundering regulations: the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of
-- Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (SI 2017/692), regulations 65 to 110 and
-- Schedules 1, 2, 3 and 3AZA -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- (Text: a converter-script rendering of the Regulations, not the official text.)
--
-- SEAT: a business that is a relevant person under the Regulations (a bank, an accountancy or
-- legal firm, an estate agent, a money service business and so on) and its compliance officer.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions
-- that person would ask about being supervised, inspected, penalised, appealing, disclosing to the
-- NCA, and the lists in the Schedules.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a
-- list -- one for each fact the person can state.  The long modules' records, MAYBE inputs and
-- lists are built inside each question, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then
-- called; no rule is restated here.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure"; "I am not sure"
--     becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A number that a rule treats as possibly unknown is asked with "-1 if you do not know" and
--     becomes NOTHING.
--   * Where the answer of another section is an input to a rule (a seam), the question asks it as
--     "Yes / No / I am not sure"; ask the question for that section first.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulations themselves give;
-- NOTHING means the Regulations do not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result:
-- FALSE and NOTHING (mlr4)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a provision addresses only an official (the supervisory
-- authority, the FCA, the Commissioners, a justice, an officer, the tribunal, the Treasury or the
-- NCA), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below, which ask
-- what it means for the person.
--
-- NAMING.  Every question is named "Under regulation N, ..." (or "Under schedule N, ...") with the
-- Regulations' own numbering, so that no two parts' questions share a name.
-- The helper types and constructors below begin "reg 65-110" (a range, not one provision) because they serve every question in this file, and the merged seat imports every part's seat at once, so a bare `Yes` or `My answer` would be defined twice.

DECLARE `reg 65-110 My answer` IS ONE OF
    `reg 65-110 Yes`
    `reg 65-110 No`
    `reg 65-110 I am not sure`

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `reg 65-110 My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `reg 65-110 Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A number that the person gives as -1 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 65-110 my number if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- Which public authority the person means.  The last choice needs the professional body as well.
DECLARE `reg 65-110 Which authority` IS ONE OF
    `reg 65-110 the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `reg 65-110 the Prudential Regulation Authority`
    `reg 65-110 the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `reg 65-110 the Gambling Commission`
    `reg 65-110 the National Crime Agency`
    `reg 65-110 the Treasury`
    `reg 65-110 the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland`
    `reg 65-110 a local weights and measures authority`
    `reg 65-110 a professional body listed in Schedule 1`

GIVEN who IS A `reg 65-110 Which authority`
      body IS A `Professional body`
GIVETH AN Authority
`reg 65-110 the authority I mean` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Financial Conduct Authority` THEN `the Financial Conduct Authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Prudential Regulation Authority` THEN `the Prudential Regulation Authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Gambling Commission` THEN `the Gambling Commission` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the National Crime Agency` THEN `the National Crime Agency` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Treasury` THEN `the Treasury` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland` THEN `the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 a local weights and measures authority` THEN `a local weights and measures authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `reg 65-110 a professional body listed in Schedule 1` THEN `a professional body listed in Schedule 1` WITH `which body` IS body -- input mapping

§ `The Money Laundering Regulations 2017, regulations 65 to 110 -- my questions`


§§ `Being asked for information, and inspected (regulations 65 to 74)`

@export Under regulation 65(3), am I a connected person of a relevant person?
GIVEN `I am a connected person of the relevant person under Schedule 5` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are you a connected person of the relevant person under Schedule 5? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 65(3), am I a connected person of a relevant person` IS
    `reg 65(3) the person is a connected person` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a connected person of the relevant person under Schedule 5`)

@export Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents?
GIVEN `the body that gave me the notice is a supervisory authority` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the body that gave you the notice a supervisory authority under regulation 7? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `I am a relevant person` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are you a relevant person under regulation 8? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the person is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is a payment service provider?
      `I am a connected person of a relevant person` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are you a connected person of a relevant person? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is in writing?
      `what the notice requires` IS A `reg 66(1) what the notice requires` @desc What does the notice require of you?
      `a time and place are specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a time and place are specified in the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(1), may a supervisory authority require me to provide information or produce documents` IS
    `reg 66(1) the supervisory authority may require P` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the body that gave me the notice is a supervisory authority`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a relevant person`) `the person is a payment service provider` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a connected person of a relevant person`) `the notice is in writing` `what the notice requires` `a time and place are specified in the notice`

@export Under regulation 66(1A), does the power include requiring a copy of a suspicious activity report?
GIVEN `the information required is a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information required is a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(1A), does the power include requiring a copy of a suspicious activity report` IS
    `reg 66(1A) the power in paragraph (1) includes requiring the information` `the information required is a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure made to the NCA`

@export Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time?
GIVEN `the period specified in the notice, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did the notice give you? (-1 if it specified no period or you do not know)
      `the period specified is a reasonable one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the period specified is a reasonable one?
      `the day on which I provided the information or documents, in days after the date of the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you provide them, counted in days after the date of the notice (the date of the notice is day 0)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(2)(a), did I provide the information or documents in time` IS
    `reg 66(2)(a) the information or documents were provided or produced in time` (`reg 65-110 my number if I know it` `the period specified in the notice, in days`) `the period specified is a reasonable one` `the day on which I provided the information or documents, in days after the date of the notice`

@export Under regulation 66(2)(b), did I provide the information or documents at the specified place?
GIVEN `I provided or produced them at the place specified in the notice` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Did you provide or produce them at the place specified in the notice? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(2)(b), did I provide the information or documents at the specified place` IS
    `reg 66(2)(b) the information or documents were provided or produced at the specified place` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I provided or produced them at the place specified in the notice`)

@export Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents?
GIVEN `the officer is an officer within regulation 65(2)` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the person who asked you an officer within regulation 65(2)? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the officer has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so?
      `the powers in regulation 66 may be exercised` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are the information or documents reasonably required by the supervisory authority in connection with the exercise of its supervisory functions (regulation 66(4))? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `what the officer requires` IS A `reg 66(3) what the officer requires` @desc What does the officer require of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(3), may an officer require me to provide information or produce documents` IS
    `reg 66(3) the officer may require P` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the officer is an officer within regulation 65(2)`) `the officer has authorisation in writing from a supervisory authority to do so` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the powers in regulation 66 may be exercised`) `what the officer requires`

@export Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must?
GIVEN `what the notice requires` IS A `reg 66(1) what the notice requires` @desc What does the notice require of you?
      `the notice sets out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice sets out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced?
      `the supervisory authority or the officer is not permitted to disclose this information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the supervisory authority or the officer is not permitted to disclose this information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(5), does the notice I received set out the reasons it must` IS
    `reg 66(5) the notice complies with the requirement to set out the reasons` `what the notice requires` `the notice sets out the reasons why the information is required to be provided or the documents produced` `the supervisory authority or the officer is not permitted to disclose this information`

@export Under regulation 66(7), does producing the document affect a lien on it?
GIVEN `the document is produced under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is produced under this regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(7), does producing the document affect a lien on it` IS
    `reg 66(7) the production of the document affects a lien on it` `the document is produced under this regulation`

@export Under regulation 66(8), may the supervisory authority use the power against a third person who holds my document?
GIVEN `the supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document?
      `it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 66(8), may the supervisory authority use the power against a third person who holds my document` IS
    `reg 66(8) the supervisory authority may exercise the power in relation to the third person` `the supervisory authority has power under this regulation to require a person to produce a document` `it appears that the document is in the possession of a third person`

@export Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises?
GIVEN `the person is a duly authorised officer` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the person who came to your premises a duly authorised officer? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P?
      `I am a relevant person` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are you a relevant person under regulation 8? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `P is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that p is a payment service provider?
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities?
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 69(1), may an officer use the powers of entry on my premises` IS
    `reg 69(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the person is a duly authorised officer`) `the officer is of, or is acting on behalf of, a supervisory authority in relation to P` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a relevant person`) `P is a payment service provider` `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that any premises are being used by P in connection with P's business or professional activities` `the officer has reasonable grounds to believe that P may have contravened the requirements of the funds transfer regulation or of these Regulations`

@export Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there?
GIVEN `paragraph (2) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 69(1) allow this officer to use the powers on your premises? (Ask the regulation 69(1) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the officer produces evidence of the officer's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer produces evidence of the officer's authority?
      `the officer acts at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the officer acts at a reasonable time?
      `the power the officer wants to exercise` IS A `reg 69(2) power` @desc What does the officer want to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 69(2), may an officer enter my premises and exercise a power there` IS
    `reg 69(2) the officer may` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph (2) applies`) `the officer produces evidence of the officer's authority` `the officer acts at a reasonable time` `the power the officer wants to exercise`

@export Under regulation 69(3), may the officer take copies of, or make extracts from, my documents?
GIVEN `paragraph (2) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is it the case that paragraph (2) applies? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the documents were found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the documents were found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 69(3), may the officer take copies of, or make extracts from, my documents` IS
    `reg 69(3) the officer may take copies of, or make extracts from, the documents` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph (2) applies`) `the documents were found as a result of the exercise of the power in paragraph (2)`

@export Under regulation 71(1), may the seized material be retained?
GIVEN `possession of the material was taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that possession of the material was taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70?
      `it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 71(1), may the seized material be retained` IS
    `reg 71(1) the seized material may be retained` `possession of the material was taken in accordance with a requirement under regulation 66 or under a warrant issued under regulation 70` `it is necessary to retain it (rather than copies of it) in connection with the exercise of the functions of the supervisory authority under these Regulations for the purposes of which any requirement was imposed or the warrant was issued`

@export Under regulation 71(3), may I apply for delivery of the material seized from me, and to which court?
GIVEN `the person claims to be the owner of seized material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person claims to be the owner of seized material?
      `where the application is made` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom` @desc In which part of the United Kingdom would you make the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE `reg 71(3) court`
DECIDE `Under regulation 71(3), may I apply for delivery of the material seized from me, and to which court` IS
    `reg 71(3) the person may apply for delivery to` `the person claims to be the owner of seized material` `where the application is made`

@export Under regulation 72(1), may I be required to produce this material or give this information?
GIVEN `the requirement is made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the requirement is made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B?
      `it is to produce excluded material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is to produce excluded material?
      `it is to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which the person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which the person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege?
      `the person is a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is a lawyer?
      `it is to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 72(1), may I be required to produce this material or give this information` IS
    `reg 72(1) the person may be required` `the requirement is made under regulation 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` `it is to produce excluded material` `it is to provide information, produce documents or answer questions which the person would be entitled to refuse to provide, produce or answer on grounds of legal professional privilege` `the person is a lawyer` `it is to provide the full name and address of the lawyer's client`

@export Under regulation 72(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure?
GIVEN `the disclosure is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure is made in good faith?
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure is made in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 72(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure` IS
    `reg 72(3) civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure` `the disclosure is made in good faith` `the disclosure is made in accordance with regulations 66, 69, 70, 74A or 74B`

@export Under regulation 72(5), is the material privileged material?
GIVEN `the person would be entitled to refuse to produce the material on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person would be entitled to refuse to produce the material on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 72(5), is the material privileged material` IS
    `reg 72(5) the material is privileged material` `the person would be entitled to refuse to produce the material on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court`

@export Under regulation 72(7), is the material excluded material?
GIVEN `the material is personal records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the material is personal records?
      `a person has acquired or created them in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a person has acquired or created them in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office?
      `they are held subject to an express or implied undertaking to hold them in confidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that they are held subject to an express or implied undertaking to hold them in confidence?
      `they are held subject to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that they are held subject to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 72(7), is the material excluded material` IS
    `reg 72(7) the material is excluded material` `the material is personal records` `a person has acquired or created them in the course of any trade, business, profession or other occupation or for the purposes of any paid or unpaid office` `they are held subject to an express or implied undertaking to hold them in confidence` `they are held subject to a restriction on disclosure or an obligation of secrecy contained in any enactment, including an enactment contained in, or made under, an Act passed after this Regulation`

@export Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings?
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)?
      `the case` IS A `reg 73(2) case` @desc Which of these describes the criminal proceedings in which the statement is sought to be used?
      `evidence relating to the statement is adduced, or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that evidence relating to the statement is adduced, or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 73, is my statement protected from use in evidence against me in criminal proceedings` IS
    `reg 73 the statement is protected from use in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings` `the statement was made in response to a requirement imposed under regulation 66(1)(c), 69(2)(e), 70(7)(e) or 74B(6)` `the case` `evidence relating to the statement is adduced, or a question relating to it is asked, by the person or on their behalf in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution`

@export Under regulation 74A(1), must my cryptoasset business provide information to the FCA?
GIVEN `the kind of relevant person my business is` IS `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of relevant person is your business? (If it is several kinds, ask once for each)
      `the FCA has directed the business to provide the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the FCA has directed the business to provide the information?
      `the information is about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations?
      `the information is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision)?
      `the information is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74A(1), must my cryptoasset business provide information to the FCA` IS
    `reg 74A(1) the cryptoasset business must provide the information to the FCA` (LIST `the kind of relevant person my business is`) `the FCA has directed the business to provide the information` `the information is about compliance by the cryptoasset business with requirements imposed in or under Parts 2 to 6 and 7A of these Regulations` `the information is required by the FCA for the purpose of calculating charges under regulation 102 (costs of supervision)` `the information is otherwise reasonably required by the FCA in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its supervisory functions`

@export Under regulation 74A(2), did I provide the information as the FCA directed?
GIVEN `I provided it at the times the FCA directed` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Did you provide it at the times the FCA directed? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `I provided it in the form the FCA directed` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Did you provide it in the form the FCA directed? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `I verified it in the manner the FCA directed` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Did you verify it in the manner the FCA directed? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74A(2), did I provide the information as the FCA directed` IS
    `reg 74A(2) the information was provided as the FCA directed` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I provided it at the times the FCA directed`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I provided it in the form the FCA directed`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I verified it in the manner the FCA directed`)

@export Under regulation 74B(1), does the FCA's power to require a skilled person's report apply to my business?
GIVEN `the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA's functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA's functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations?
      `the kind of relevant person my business is` IS `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of relevant person is your business? (If it is several kinds, ask once for each)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74B(1), does the FCA's power to require a skilled person's report apply to my business` IS
    `reg 74B(1) this regulation applies` `the FCA reasonably considers that a report by a skilled person, concerning a matter relating to the exercise of the FCA's functions under these Regulations, is required in connection with the exercise by the FCA of any of its functions under these Regulations` (LIST `the kind of relevant person my business is`)

@export Under regulation 74B(2), may the FCA require me to give it a report by a skilled person?
GIVEN `regulation 74B(1) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 74B(1) apply to your business? (Ask the regulation 74B(1) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the FCA gives notice in writing to the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the FCA gives notice in writing to the relevant person?
      `the step the FCA wants to take` IS A `reg 74B(2) step` @desc What does the FCA want to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74B(2), may the FCA require me to give it a report by a skilled person` IS
    `reg 74B(2) the FCA may take the step` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 74B(1) applies`) `the FCA gives notice in writing to the relevant person` `the step the FCA wants to take`

@export Under regulation 74B(6), did I give the skilled person the assistance required?
GIVEN `the person is the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is the relevant person?
      `I am a connected person of the relevant person` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Are you a connected person of the relevant person? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the person gave the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person gave the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74B(6), did I give the skilled person the assistance required` IS
    `reg 74B(6) the person gave the skilled person the assistance` `the person is the relevant person` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a connected person of the relevant person`) `the person gave the skilled person all such assistance as the skilled person may reasonably require`

@export Under regulation 74C(1), may the FCA impose a direction on my cryptoasset business?
GIVEN `the FCA exercises them in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the FCA exercises them in writing?
      `the FCA exercises them under paragraph (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the FCA exercises them under paragraph (5) or (6)?
      `the kind of relevant person my business is` IS `Kind of relevant person` @desc Which kind of relevant person is your business? (If it is several kinds, ask once for each)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74C(1), may the FCA impose a direction on my cryptoasset business` IS
    `reg 74C(1) the FCA may exercise its powers of direction` `the FCA exercises them in writing` `the FCA exercises them under paragraph (5) or (6)` (LIST `the kind of relevant person my business is`)

@export Under regulation 74C(10), does the FCA notice of a direction contain what it must?
GIVEN `the notice is the notice referred to in paragraph (9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice is the notice referred to in paragraph (9)?
      `it gives details of the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it gives details of the direction?
      `it states the FCA's reasons for imposing or varying the direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states the FCA's reasons for imposing or varying the direction?
      `it informs the cryptoasset business that it may make representations to the FCA within such period as may be specified in the notice (whether or not the cryptoasset business has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it informs the cryptoasset business that it may make representations to the FCA within such period as may be specified in the notice (whether or not the cryptoasset business has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal)?
      `it informs the cryptoasset business of when the direction takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it informs the cryptoasset business of when the direction takes effect?
      `it informs the cryptoasset business of its right to refer the matter to the Upper Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it informs the cryptoasset business of its right to refer the matter to the Upper Tribunal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 74C(10), does the FCA notice of a direction contain what it must` IS
    `reg 74C(10) the notice contains what it must` `the notice is the notice referred to in paragraph (9)` `it gives details of the direction` `it states the FCA's reasons for imposing or varying the direction` `it informs the cryptoasset business that it may make representations to the FCA within such period as may be specified in the notice (whether or not the cryptoasset business has referred the matter to the Upper Tribunal)` `it informs the cryptoasset business of when the direction takes effect` `it informs the cryptoasset business of its right to refer the matter to the Upper Tribunal`


§§ `Penalties, measures, prohibitions and prosecution (regulations 75 to 92)`

@export Under regulation 75, is the requirement I contravened a relevant requirement?
GIVEN `the provision is a relevant requirement under Schedule 6` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the provision you are said to have contravened a relevant requirement under Schedule 6? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 75, is the requirement I contravened a relevant requirement` IS
    `reg 75 the requirement is a relevant requirement` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the provision is a relevant requirement under Schedule 6`)

@export Under regulation 76(1), does a designated supervisory authority have the power in regulation 76(2) over me?
GIVEN `the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the body that is acting a designated supervisory authority under regulation 76(8)(b)? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P?
      `the requirement is a relevant requirement` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the requirement a relevant requirement under regulation 75? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 76(1), does a designated supervisory authority have the power in regulation 76(2) over me` IS
    `reg 76(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the body is a designated supervisory authority`) `the authority is satisfied that P has contravened a requirement imposed on P` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the requirement is a relevant requirement`)

@export Under regulation 76(2), may a designated supervisory authority impose a penalty on me or publish a statement about me?
GIVEN `regulation 76(1) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 76(1) apply? (Ask the regulation 76(1) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the measure the authority wants to take` IS A `reg 76(2) measure` @desc What does the authority want to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 76(2), may a designated supervisory authority impose a penalty on me or publish a statement about me` IS
    `reg 76(2) the designated supervisory authority may` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 76(1) applies`) `the measure the authority wants to take`

@export Under regulation 76(3), may the authority impose a penalty on me as an officer of the business?
GIVEN `the body is a designated supervisory authority` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the body that is acting a designated supervisory authority under regulation 76(8)(b)? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
