§§ `Appeals and review (regulations 93 to 100)`

@export Under regulation 93(1), may I appeal to the Upper Tribunal against the FCA decision?
GIVEN `the decision is made by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is made by the FCA?
      `the decision is a direction under regulation 25(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a direction under regulation 25(2)?
      `the decision refuses to register me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision refuse to register you under regulation 59(1)?
      `the decision suspends or cancels my registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision suspend or cancel your registration under regulation 60?
      `the decision is under regulation 74C(1) to impose a direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 74C(1) to impose a direction?
      `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement?
      `the decision is under regulation 77 to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 77 to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation?
      `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 93(1), may I appeal to the Upper Tribunal against the FCA decision` IS
    `reg 93(1) a person may appeal to the Upper Tribunal` `the decision is made by the FCA` `the decision is a direction under regulation 25(2)` `the decision refuses to register me` `the decision suspends or cancels my registration` `the decision is under regulation 74C(1) to impose a direction` `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` `the decision is under regulation 77 to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation` `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition`

@export Under regulation 94(1), did the Commissioners offer me a review of their decision?
GIVEN `the decision has been notified to P` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision has been notified to P?
      `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision?
      `the Commissioners offered P a review of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners offered P a review of the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 94(1), did the Commissioners offer me a review of their decision` IS
    `reg 94(1) the Commissioners offered P a review` `the decision has been notified to P` `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision` `the Commissioners offered P a review of the decision`

@export Under regulation 95(1), must the Commissioners review the decision because I accepted the offer?
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter?
      `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that p notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer?
      `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which I notified acceptance` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you notify the Commissioners that you accept the offer, counted in days after the date of the notice of the offer (the date of the notice is day 0)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 95(1), must the Commissioners review the decision because I accepted the offer` IS
    `reg 95(1) the duty to review the decision arises` `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which I notified acceptance`

@export Under regulation 95(2), may I notify acceptance of the offer although I have already appealed?
GIVEN `P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that p has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 95(2), may I notify acceptance of the offer although I have already appealed` IS
    `reg 95(2) P may notify acceptance of the offer` `P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100`

@export Under regulation 96(4), on what day does the relevant period end?
GIVEN `the day from which the most recent extension runs` IS A NUMBER @desc From which day does the most recent extension run, in days after the date of the notice of the offer? (-1 if there has been none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under regulation 96(4), on what day does the relevant period end` IS
    `reg 96(4) the relevant period ends on day` (`reg 65-110 my number if I know it` `the day from which the most recent extension runs`)

@export Under regulation 96(1), may the Commissioners extend the relevant period by notice?
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered P a review of a decision under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners have offered P a review of a decision under this Chapter?
      `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which the Commissioners give the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number for: the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which the Commissioners give the notice?
      `the last day of the relevant period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number for: the last day of the relevant period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 96(1), may the Commissioners extend the relevant period by notice` IS
    `reg 96(1) the Commissioners may notify P that the relevant period is extended` `the Commissioners have offered P a review of a decision under this Chapter` `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which the Commissioners give the notice` `the last day of the relevant period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer`

@export Under regulation 97(1), does regulation 97 apply to me because I did not accept the offer of a review in time?
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to P` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to P?
      `P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that p does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 97(1), does regulation 97 apply to me because I did not accept the offer of a review in time` IS
    `reg 97(1) this regulation applies` `the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to P` `P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)`

@export Under regulation 97(2), may the Commissioners review the decision out of time at my request?
GIVEN `regulation 97(1) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 97(1) apply to you? (Ask the regulation 97(1) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time?
      `the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed?
      `the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 97(2), may the Commissioners review the decision out of time at my request` IS
    `reg 97(2) the duty to review the decision out of time arises` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 97(1) applies`) `after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time` `the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed` `the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply`

@export Under regulation 98(1), does regulation 98 apply to my review?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95?
      `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 97` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 97?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 98(1), does regulation 98 apply to my review` IS
    `reg 98(1) this regulation applies` `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95` `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 97`

@export Under regulation 98(6), did the Commissioners give me notice of the conclusions in time?
GIVEN `regulation 98(1) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 98(1) apply to your review? (Ask the regulation 98(1) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the Commissioners gave P notice of the conclusions of the review and their reasoning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners gave P notice of the conclusions of the review and their reasoning?
      `the days after the relevant date on which the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day was the notice of the conclusions given, counted in days after the relevant date (the relevant date is day 0)?
      `the notice was given within such other period as the Commissioners and P agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notice was given within such other period as the Commissioners and P agreed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 98(6), did the Commissioners give me notice of the conclusions in time` IS
    `reg 98(6) the Commissioners gave P notice of the conclusions and reasoning in time` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 98(1) applies`) `the Commissioners gave P notice of the conclusions of the review and their reasoning` `the days after the relevant date on which the notice was given` `the notice was given within such other period as the Commissioners and P agreed`

@export Under regulation 98(8), is the review treated as having concluded that the decision is upheld?
GIVEN `regulation 98(1) applies` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Does regulation 98(1) apply to your review? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the Commissioners gave notice of the conclusions in time` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Did the Commissioners give notice of the conclusions in time under regulation 98(6)? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 98(8), is the review treated as having concluded that the decision is upheld` IS
    `reg 98(8) the review is treated as having concluded that the decision is upheld` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `regulation 98(1) applies`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the Commissioners gave notice of the conclusions in time`)

@export Under regulation 99(1), may I appeal to the tribunal against the Commissioners' decision?
GIVEN `the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners?
      `the decision is a direction under regulation 25(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a direction under regulation 25(2)?
      `the decision is that I am not a fit and proper person, other than one required by regulation 58(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision that you are not a fit and proper person under regulation 58, other than a decision that regulation 58(3) required the Commissioners to make (because you were convicted of a criminal offence listed in Schedule 3)?
      `the decision refuses to register me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision refuse to register you under regulation 59(1)?
      `the decision suspends or cancels my registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision suspend or cancel your registration under regulation 60?
      `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement?
      `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 99(1), may I appeal to the tribunal against the Commissioners' decision` IS
    `reg 99(1) a person may appeal to the tribunal in accordance with regulation 100` `the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners` `the decision is a direction under regulation 25(2)` `the decision is that I am not a fit and proper person, other than one required by regulation 58(3)` `the decision refuses to register me` `the decision suspends or cancels my registration` `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition`

@export Under regulation 99(4)(a), may the tribunal reduce the penalty to this amount?
GIVEN `the penalty the Commissioners imposed, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What penalty, in pounds, did the Commissioners impose?
      `the amount the tribunal thinks appropriate, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, do you ask the tribunal to substitute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 99(4)(a), may the tribunal reduce the penalty to this amount` IS
    `reg 99(4)(a) the tribunal may reduce the penalty to the amount` `the penalty the Commissioners imposed, in pounds` `the amount the tribunal thinks appropriate, in pounds`

@export Under regulation 100(1), did I appeal in time against the Commissioners' decision?
GIVEN `the days after the date of the notice of the decision on which I appealed` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you appeal, counted in days after the date of the notice of the decision (the date of the notice is day 0)?
      `the day on which the relevant period ends` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day does the relevant period end, in days after the date of the notice? (Use the answer to regulation 96(4), or 30 if there was no extension)
      `paragraph (2), (3) or (4) displaces paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case one that paragraph (2), (3) or (4) of regulation 100 covers instead? (a review required, requested, or deemed upheld)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 100(1), did I appeal in time against the Commissioners' decision` IS
    `reg 100(1) the appeal was made in time` `the days after the date of the notice of the decision on which I appealed` `the day on which the relevant period ends` `paragraph (2), (3) or (4) displaces paragraph (1)`

@export Under regulation 100(2), did I appeal in time after a review the Commissioners were required to undertake?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95?
      `the days after the conclusion date on which I appealed` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you appeal, counted in days after the conclusion date (the conclusion date is day 0)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 100(2), did I appeal in time after a review the Commissioners were required to undertake` IS
    `reg 100(2) the appeal was made in time` `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95` `the days after the conclusion date on which I appealed`

@export Under regulation 100(3), did I appeal in time after a review I requested?
GIVEN `the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97?
      `the Commissioners have notified P as to whether or not a review will be undertaken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners have notified P as to whether or not a review will be undertaken?
      `the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken?
      `the days after the conclusion date on which I appealed` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did you appeal, counted in days after the conclusion date (the conclusion date is day 0)?
      `the tribunal gives permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the tribunal gives permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 100(3), did I appeal in time after a review I requested` IS
    `reg 100(3) the appeal was made in time` `the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97` `the Commissioners have notified P as to whether or not a review will be undertaken` `the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken` `the days after the conclusion date on which I appealed` `the tribunal gives permission to appeal`

@export Under regulation 100(4), may I appeal now that the review is deemed to have upheld the decision?
GIVEN `regulation 98(8) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that regulation 98(8) applies?
      `the day I appeal` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day do you appeal, counted in days after the date of the notice of the decision?
      `the day on which the regulation 98(6) period ended` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day did the regulation 98(6) period end, counted in days after the date of the notice of the decision?
      `the conclusion date` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the conclusion date, counted in days after the date of the notice of the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 100(4), may I appeal now that the review is deemed to have upheld the decision` IS
    `reg 100(4) the appeal may be made` `regulation 98(8) applies` `the day I appeal` `the day on which the regulation 98(6) period ended` `the conclusion date`

@export Under regulation 100(5), may I appeal after the end of the period with the tribunal's permission?
GIVEN `the appeal is made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appeal is made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4)?
      `the tribunal gives permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the tribunal gives permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 100(5), may I appeal after the end of the period with the tribunal's permission` IS
    `reg 100(5) the appeal may be made after the end of the period` `the appeal is made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4)` `the tribunal gives permission to appeal`


§§ `Charges, disclosures and the transition from the old regulations (regulations 101 to 110)`

@export Under regulation 101, to whom is a charge or penalty imposed on me a debt due?
GIVEN `the charge or penalty is imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the charge or penalty is imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider?
      `the body that imposed it` IS A `reg 65-110 Which authority` @desc Which body imposed the charge or penalty?
      `the body that imposed it -- which professional body` IS A `Professional body` @desc If you chose a professional body listed in Schedule 1: which one? (If you chose anything else, choose any one; it is ignored.)
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
DECIDE `Under regulation 101, to whom is a charge or penalty imposed on me a debt due` IS
    `reg 101 the charge or penalty is a debt due to` `the charge or penalty is imposed on a relevant person or on a payment service provider` (`reg 65-110 the authority I mean` `the body that imposed it` `the body that imposed it -- which professional body`)

@export Under regulation 102(1), may the FCA or the Commissioners impose a charge on me?
GIVEN `the charge is imposed by the FCA or the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the charge is imposed by the FCA or the Commissioners?
      `the class I am in` IS A `reg 102(1) class` @desc Which of these describes you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 102(1), may the FCA or the Commissioners impose a charge on me` IS
    `reg 102(1) the charge may be imposed on` `the charge is imposed by the FCA or the Commissioners` `the class I am in`

@export Under regulation 102(2), is the charge levied on me permitted?
GIVEN `the charge levied on me, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What charge, in pounds, is levied on you?
      `the amount the authority considers will cover its expenses, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, does the authority consider will cover its expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 102(2), is the charge levied on me permitted` IS
    `reg 102(2) the charge is permitted` `the charge levied on me, in pounds` `the amount the authority considers will cover its expenses, in pounds`

@export Under regulation 102(3), may a charge be levied in respect of each of my premises?
GIVEN `the premises are premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on, or proposes to carry on, business or professional activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the premises are premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on, or proposes to carry on, business or professional activities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 102(3), may a charge be levied in respect of each of my premises` IS
    `reg 102(3) a charge may be levied in respect of each of the premises` `the premises are premises at which the relevant person, the provider or a person connected with the relevant person or the provider carries on, or proposes to carry on, business or professional activities`

@export Under regulation 103(1), is my disclosure to the NCA the disclosure these Regulations require?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `reg 103(1) body` @desc Which of these are you?
      `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `the body or person informed the NCA as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body or person informed the NCA as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 103(1), is my disclosure to the NCA the disclosure these Regulations require` IS
    `reg 103(1) the body or person informed the NCA as required` `who I am` `the body or person knows or suspects, or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` `the body or person informed the NCA as soon as practicable`

@export Under regulation 103(1), must I inform the NCA?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `reg 103(1) body` @desc Which of these are you?
      `I know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 103(1), must I inform the NCA` IS
    `reg 103(1) the duty to inform the NCA arises` `who I am` `I know or suspect, or have reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting, that a person is or has engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing`

@export Under regulation 103(2), does my disclosure to the NCA breach a restriction on the disclosure of information?
GIVEN `the disclosure is made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure is made under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 103(2), does my disclosure to the NCA breach a restriction on the disclosure of information` IS
    `reg 103(2) the disclosure breaches a restriction on the disclosure of information` `the disclosure is made under paragraph (1)`

@export Under regulation 103(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure to the NCA?
GIVEN `the disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 103(3), does civil liability arise because I made the disclosure to the NCA` IS
    `reg 103(3) civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure` `the disclosure under paragraph (1) is made in good faith`

@export Under regulation 106, do these Regulations authorise or require my disclosure?
GIVEN `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation?
      `the disclosure is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 106, do these Regulations authorise or require my disclosure` IS
    `reg 106 these Regulations authorise or require the disclosure` `the disclosure would be in contravention of the data protection legislation` `the disclosure is prohibited by any of Parts 1 to 3 or 5 to 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016`

@export Under regulation 107, is the transfer treated as a transfer of funds within the United Kingdom?
GIVEN `a person's compliance with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation is being determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a person's compliance with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation is being determined?
      `the place at the other end of the transfer` IS A `reg 107 place` @desc Where is the other end of the transfer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 107, is the transfer treated as a transfer of funds within the United Kingdom` IS
    `reg 107 the transfer is treated as a transfer of funds within the United Kingdom` `a person's compliance with a requirement in the funds transfer regulation is being determined` `the place at the other end of the transfer`

@export Under regulation 110(1), is the old instrument revoked?
GIVEN `the instrument is one of the old money laundering regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument one of the old money laundering regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 110(1), is the old instrument revoked` IS
    `reg 110(1) the instrument is revoked` `the instrument is one of the old money laundering regulations`

@export Under regulation 110(2), do the old regulations continue to apply to my past conduct?
GIVEN `the day the conduct constituting the contravention took place` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the conduct take place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 110(2), do the old regulations continue to apply to my past conduct` IS
    `reg 110(2) the old regulations continue to have effect` `the day the conduct constituting the contravention took place`

@export Under regulation 110(3), do a penalty or an offence under these Regulations apply to my past conduct?
GIVEN `the old regulations continue to have effect` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Do the old regulations continue to apply to the conduct? (Ask the regulation 110(2) question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under regulation 110(3), do a penalty or an offence under these Regulations apply to my past conduct` IS
    `reg 110(3) a penalty or an offence under the relevant Part of these Regulations has effect` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the old regulations continue to have effect`)

@export Under regulation 110(4), on what day is a continuing contravention taken to have begun?
GIVEN `the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during such a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during such a period?
      `the earliest of those days` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest day on which the conduct took place?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under regulation 110(4), on what day is a continuing contravention taken to have begun` IS
    `reg 110(4) the conduct is taken to have begun on` `the conduct is found to have been committed over a period of two or more days, or at some point during such a period` `the earliest of those days`


§§ `The Schedules (schedules 1, 2, 3 and 3AZA)`

@export Under schedule 1, is my professional body one that is listed?
GIVEN `the body` IS A `reg 65-110 Which authority` @desc Which body is it?
      `the body -- which professional body` IS A `Professional body` @desc If you chose a professional body listed in Schedule 1: which one? (If you chose anything else, choose any one; it is ignored.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1, is my professional body one that is listed` IS
    `sch 1 the body is a professional body listed in Schedule 1` (`reg 65-110 the authority I mean` `the body` `the body -- which professional body`)

@export Under schedule 2, is my business's activity a listed activity?
GIVEN `my activity` IS A `Listed activity` @desc Which of the listed activities is your business's activity closest to?
      `my activity is on the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business's activity one of the activities on the Schedule 2 list?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2, is my business's activity a listed activity` IS
    `sch 2 the activity is a listed activity` (IF `my activity is on the list` THEN JUST `my activity` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 1, is my kind of credit within lending?
GIVEN `the credit is consumer credit, a credit agreement relating to immovable property, factoring with or without recourse, or the financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the credit is consumer credit, a credit agreement relating to immovable property, factoring with or without recourse, or the financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 1, is my kind of credit within lending` IS
    `sch 2 item 1 the kind of credit is within lending` `the credit is consumer credit, a credit agreement relating to immovable property, factoring with or without recourse, or the financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting)`

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 3, is my service within payment services?
GIVEN `the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017?
      `the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 3, is my service within payment services` IS
    `sch 2 item 3 the service is within payment services` `the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` `the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)`

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 6, is my trading within the item?
GIVEN `the trading is for own account or for the account of customers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the trading is for own account or for the account of customers?
      `the instrument I trade in` IS A `sch 2 item 6 instrument` @desc Which instrument do you trade in?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 6, is my trading within the item` IS
    `sch 2 item 6 the trading is within the item` `the trading is for own account or for the account of customers` `the instrument I trade in`

@export Under schedule 3 paragraph 36, is the act done abroad a relevant offence?
GIVEN `the act constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the act constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country?
      `the paragraph of Schedule 3 under which it would be an offence, from 1 to 36` IS A NUMBER @desc Under which paragraph of Schedule 3 (1 to 36) would the act be an offence?
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom?
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done by a person linked to a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done by a person linked to a part of the United Kingdom?
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done as regards the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done as regards the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 paragraph 36, is the act done abroad a relevant offence` IS
    `sch 3 para 36 the act is a relevant offence` `the act constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country` `the paragraph of Schedule 3 under which it would be an offence, from 1 to 36` `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom` `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done by a person linked to a part of the United Kingdom` `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done as regards the United Kingdom`

@export Under schedule 3, is the offence a relevant offence?
GIVEN `the paragraph of Schedule 3 the offence falls within` IS A `sch 3 paragraph` @desc Which paragraph of Schedule 3 does the offence fall within?
      `the act done abroad is a relevant offence under paragraph 36` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc If the offence was committed abroad: is it a relevant offence under paragraph 36? (Ask the paragraph 36 question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3, is the offence a relevant offence` IS
    `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` `the paragraph of Schedule 3 the offence falls within` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `the act done abroad is a relevant offence under paragraph 36`)

@export Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 1, may a material discrepancy arise in relation to this information?
GIVEN `I am a beneficial owner of a body corporate within regulations 5 and 6` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the individual a beneficial owner of a body corporate within regulations 5 and 6? (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `the information is about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006?
      `the information is about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 1, may a material discrepancy arise in relation to this information` IS
    `sch 3AZA para 1 a material discrepancy may arise in relation to the information` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `I am a beneficial owner of a body corporate within regulations 5 and 6`) `the information is about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` `the information is about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022`

@export Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 2, does the discrepancy satisfy the condition?
GIVEN `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing?
      `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 2, does the discrepancy satisfy the condition` IS
    `sch 3AZA para 2 the discrepancy satisfies the condition` `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing` `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer`

@export Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 3, is the discrepancy in a form listed in paragraph 3?
GIVEN `the form of the discrepancy` IS A `sch 3AZA para 3 form` @desc Which of these forms is the discrepancy in?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3AZA paragraph 3, is the discrepancy in a form listed in paragraph 3` IS
    `sch 3AZA para 3 the discrepancy is in a form listed in paragraph 3` `the form of the discrepancy`

@export Under schedule 3AZA, is the discrepancy a material discrepancy?
GIVEN `paragraph 1 is met` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is paragraph 1 met? (Ask the paragraph 1 question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `paragraph 2 is met` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is paragraph 2 met? (Ask the paragraph 2 question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
      `paragraph 3 is met` IS A `reg 65-110 My answer` @desc Is the discrepancy in a form listed in paragraph 3? (Ask the paragraph 3 question first) (Yes, No or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3AZA, is the discrepancy a material discrepancy` IS
    `sch 3AZA the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph 1 is met`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph 2 is met`) (`reg 65-110 what I say, as a fact` `paragraph 3 is met`)

-- ============================================================
-- mlr5: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom -- Schedules 3A to 7
-- (lines 3055-3808 of the plain-text rendering, which is not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a business that is a relevant person (a bank, an accountancy or legal firm, an estate agent, a money service business, a cryptoasset exchange provider ...) and its
-- compliance officer.  This layer phrases the rules of the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs: yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list, one for each fact the person can state, each with a @desc worded as the person
-- would be asked.  A fact the person may not know is asked as "yes / no / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
-- Percentages are 0 to 100.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the text itself gives; NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Never read NOTHING as no.  A question that begins "Under schedule N paragraph M," says the scope its answer claims.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Schedule 4 (what a supervisory authority reports), Schedule 6A (the NCA's duties) and the regulative parts of Schedule 6B are addressed to officials; the
-- rule is in layer 1, and the questions below are only what each means to the business.  Schedule 3ZA is blank in the text, and the explanatory note is not operative.

DECLARE `mlr5 my answer` IS ONE OF
    `mlr5 yes`
    `mlr5 no`
    `mlr5 I am not sure`

-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.

-- An answer of yes, no or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `mlr5 my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`mlr5 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `mlr5 yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `mlr5 no` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `mlr5 I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A holding of shares or voting power, before and after, from two percentages.
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER
      after IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 6B holding`
`mlr5 a holding from` MEANS
    `sch 6B holding` WITH
        `the percentage before the step` IS before
        `the percentage after the step` IS after

§ `Schedules 3A to 7 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2017 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 3A -- is the trust an excluded trust? (lines 3082-3205)`
-- Situation: regulations 42 (line 1331), 45(10A) (line 1463) and 45ZA(2) (lines 1509-1510) reach only a trust that is "not a trust listed in Schedule 3A", so a relevant person
-- asks whether a trust is listed whenever it has to decide whether one of them reaches it.  The first question tries every paragraph at once (the layer-1 module gathers them by hand for regulations 42, 45 and 45ZA, SEAM S-18),
-- and then there is one question for each paragraph, in the order of the Schedule.  A paragraph that states a condition the trust does not meet ("where", a period, "only") answers No.  A paragraph whose description simply does not fit the
-- trust usually answers NOTHING, not No: the Schedule lists kinds of excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside them is not excluded.  The first question answers No for a trust that fits no paragraph, because it reads the Schedule as the list the
-- term "a trust listed in Schedule 3A" is handed to (assumed, not ruled: FORK S3A-F8), unless an answer still unknown (whether the creator, or a participant, is a relevant supervised person) could make paragraph 12 or 13 apply.
-- A number printed with +k (paragraph 7+1) is the k-th bare paragraph printed after paragraph 7 in the rendering of the text, which prints no number for it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 3A, every paragraph at once (SEAM S-18).  A fact the trust does not turn on can be answered No, 0 or any date.
@export Under schedule 3A, is the trust an excluded trust, that is a trust listed in Schedule 3A (any of its paragraphs)?
GIVEN `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust one that an enactment imposes or requires?
      `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 of Schedule 3A (a trust imposed or required by an enactment)?
      `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the trust been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925?
      `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason paragraph 1 stopped applying that one of the trustees died?
      `the date of the death of that trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that trustee die?
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether the trust is an excluded trust? (the day to count two years from a death up to)
      `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal?
      `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold sums or assets of a pension scheme?
      `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that pension scheme a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004?
      `the trust is of a life policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of a life policy?
      `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the life policy pay out in any case other than (a) the death, terminal or critical illness, or permanent or temporary disablement of the person assured, or (b) meeting the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured?
      `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of an insurance policy?
      `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insurance policy pay out on the temporary disablement of the person assured?
      `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the insurance policy applied for at the same time as a life policy of the kind in paragraph 4(1)?
      `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the insurance policy pay out in any case other than (a) the temporary disablement of the person assured or (b) meeting the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured?
      `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy?
      `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for charitable purposes?
      `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom` @desc In which part of the United Kingdom is the trust?
      `the trust is registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust registered as a charity?
      `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011?
      `the value of the property the trust holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in pounds sterling, of the property the trust holds?
      `the date the trust was created` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the trust created?
      `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date does regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations come into force? (the rendering of the text does not give it)
      `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created as a requirement of opening an account of the kind described in paragraph 6A(2)?
      `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the account consist only of a sum of money?
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who holds the account an authorised person (within the meaning of FSMA)?
      `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person have a Part 4A permission, within the meaning of section 55A(5) of FSMA, to carry on the activity of accepting deposits?
      `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person carry on the activity of accepting deposits by way of business?
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18?
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005?
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000?
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986?
      `the trust was effected by will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust effected by will?
      `the person was beneficially entitled to all the property the trust holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died beneficially entitled to all the property that the trust holds (so that it is all part of the person's estate on death)?
      `the date of the death of the person` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person (whose estate it is, or who was assured, or whose estate P is) die?
      `the trust holds only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy of the kinds in paragraph 4?
      `the trust was created under a deed or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created under a deed or instrument?
      `the deed or instrument varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deed or instrument vary any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person (P)?
      `the deed or instrument was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deed or instrument made by the persons, or any of the persons, who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions?
      `the trust is of jointly held property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of jointly held property?
      `the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the trustees and the beneficiaries the same persons?
      `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9 of Schedule 3A (a co-ownership trust)?
      `the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason paragraph 9 stopped applying that one of the trustees died?
      `the deed or instrument revokes a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deed or instrument revoke a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland?
      `the deed or instrument provides that from the date of execution the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the deed or instrument provide that from the date of execution the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees?
      `the trust was created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or of the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under such arrangements or rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under them?
      `the trust relates to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust relate to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities (within the meaning of regulation 3(1) of the Uncertificated Securities Regulations 2001)?
      `the entity is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity that created the trust, or for which it was created, an authorised person?
      `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty?
      `the entity is a participant in a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity a participant in a designated system?
      `the entity is a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity a designated system?
      `the entity is a recognised body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that entity a recognised body?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to that entity's clients?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients or to keep separate client records and accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to that entity's clients, or to keep separate client records and accounts?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums or assets belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums or assets belonging to a person other than the trustee?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of documents belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of documents belonging to a person other than the trustee?
      `the trustee is carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 40 (safeguarding and administering investments) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee carrying on by way of business the activity of safeguarding and administering investments (article 40 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001)?
      `the trustee is acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme (within section 237 of FSMA)?
      `the trustee is acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition agreed between two or more other persons, including the person for whom they are held?
      `the creator is a relevant supervised person` IS A `mlr5 my answer` @desc Is the person who created the trust a relevant supervised person (a relevant person, or a person subject to and supervised under equivalent requirements)? Yes, no or not sure.
      `the trust was created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets?
      `the trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust incidental to the carrying on of business by that relevant supervised person?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2 to these Regulations? (the rendering of Schedule 2 prints no point numbers)
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity?
      `one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person` IS A `mlr5 my answer` @desc Is one or more of the participants in that activity a relevant supervised person? Yes, no or not sure.
      `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use of the trust incidental to the principal purpose of that activity?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons?
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction?
      `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use of the trust incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction?
      `the trust was created on the transfer or disposal of an asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created on the transfer or disposal of an asset?
      `the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the trust to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made, until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed?
      `the trust holds property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies?
      `the trust is of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect?
      `the trust is of funds derived from a payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a trust of funds derived from a payment?
      `the payment was made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person?
      `the payment was disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987?
      `the trust holds tenants' contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold tenants' contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987?
      `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust the plan trust of a share incentive plan?
      `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share incentive plan meet the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003?
      `the trust was created under a share option scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created under a share option scheme?
      `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share option scheme meet the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003?
      `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government?
      `the purpose is to carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the trust to enable or assist that body to carry out its functions, including any functions as a court or tribunal and, in the case of the Bank of England, any of its functions as a monetary authority within the meaning of section 244(2)(c) of the Banking Act 2009?
      `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold any interest in land in the United Kingdom?
      `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value, in pounds sterling, of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds? (they include works of art, antiques, collectibles, jewellery and other non-financial assets capable of increasing in value over time)
      `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the cumulative total value, in pounds sterling, of the property the trust has held since it was created?
      `the income of the trust per annum` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the income of the trust per annum, in pounds sterling?
      `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a UK trust which is an express trust?
      `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the settlor, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts?
      `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is or was one of those other trusts an excluded trust under paragraph 23A of Schedule 3A (the general exclusion)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A, is the trust an excluded trust, that is a trust listed in Schedule 3A (any of its paragraphs)` IS
    `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`
        (`sch 3A facts about the trust` WITH
            `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment`
            `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1`
            `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925`
            `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`
            `the date of the death of that trustee` IS `the date of the death of that trustee`
            `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS `the date for which the trust is being tested`
            `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal`
            `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme`
            `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004`
            `the trust is of a life policy` IS `the trust is of a life policy`
            `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)`
            `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS `the trust is of an insurance policy`
            `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured`
            `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)`
            `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)`
            `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy`
            `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS `the trust is for charitable purposes`
