      `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share incentive plan meet the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 16+4 (the fourth unnumbered paragraph after paragraph 16), is the trust an excluded trust because it is the plan trust of a qualifying share incentive plan` IS
    `sch 3A para 16+4 the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` WITH `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` IS `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan`, `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`

-- sch 3A para 16+5 (lines 3183-3183).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 16+5 (the fifth unnumbered paragraph after paragraph 16), is the trust an excluded trust because it was created under a qualifying share option scheme?
GIVEN `the trust was created under a share option scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created under a share option scheme?
      `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share option scheme meet the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 16+5 (the fifth unnumbered paragraph after paragraph 16), is the trust an excluded trust because it was created under a qualifying share option scheme` IS
    `sch 3A para 16+5 the trust is created under a share option scheme` WITH `the trust was created under a share option scheme` IS `the trust was created under a share option scheme`, `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`

-- sch 3A para 16+6 (lines 3184-3184).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 16+6 (the sixth unnumbered paragraph after paragraph 16), is the trust an excluded trust because it holds property for a disabled person?
GIVEN `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 16+6 (the sixth unnumbered paragraph after paragraph 16), is the trust an excluded trust because it holds property for a disabled person` IS
    `sch 3A para 16+6 the trust holds property for a disabled beneficiary` WITH `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005` IS `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005`

-- sch 3A para 23 (lines 3185-3191).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 23, is the trust an excluded trust because it was created to enable or assist a public authority to carry out its functions?
GIVEN `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency?
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government?
      `the purpose is to carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the trust to enable or assist that body to carry out its functions, including any functions as a court or tribunal and, in the case of the Bank of England, any of its functions as a monetary authority within the meaning of section 244(2)(c) of the Banking Act 2009?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 23, is the trust an excluded trust because it was created to enable or assist a public authority to carry out its functions` IS
    `sch 3A para 23 the trust is a public authorities trust` WITH `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act` IS `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act`, `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002` IS `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002`, `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency` IS `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency`, `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government` IS `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government`, `the purpose is to carry out its functions` IS `the purpose is to carry out its functions`

-- sch 3A para 23A(3) (lines 3201-3201).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 23A(3), is the kind of asset an asset of appreciable worth?
GIVEN `the kind of asset` IS A `sch 3A kind of asset` @desc What kind of asset is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 23A(3), is the kind of asset an asset of appreciable worth` IS
    `sch 3A para 23A(3) the asset is an asset of appreciable worth` WITH `the kind of asset` IS `the kind of asset`

-- sch 3A para 23A (lines 3192-3200).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 23A, is the trust an excluded trust under the general exclusion?
GIVEN `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trust hold any interest in land in the United Kingdom?
      `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value, in pounds sterling, of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds? (they include works of art, antiques, collectibles, jewellery and other non-financial assets capable of increasing in value over time)
      `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the cumulative total value, in pounds sterling, of the property the trust has held since it was created?
      `the income of the trust per annum` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the income of the trust per annum, in pounds sterling?
      `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a UK trust which is an express trust?
      `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the settlor, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts?
      `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is or was one of those other trusts an excluded trust under paragraph 23A of Schedule 3A (the general exclusion)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 23A, is the trust an excluded trust under the general exclusion` IS
    `sch 3A para 23A the trust is within the general exclusion` WITH `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom`, `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` IS `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds`, `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` IS `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created`, `the income of the trust per annum` IS `the income of the trust per annum`, `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust` IS `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust`, `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts` IS `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts`, `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A` IS `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A`

-- sch 3A para 24 (lines 3202-3205).
@export Under schedule 3A paragraph 24, is the person a relevant supervised person?
GIVEN `the person is a relevant person` IS A `mlr5 my answer` @desc Is the person a relevant person under these Regulations? Yes, no or not sure.
      `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive)?
      `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3A paragraph 24, is the person a relevant supervised person` IS
    `sch 3A para 24 the person is a relevant supervised person` WITH `the person is a relevant person` IS (`mlr5 what I say, as a fact` `the person is a relevant person`), `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity` IS `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity`, `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 4 -- the information my supervisory authority is asked for (lines 3206-3241)`
-- Situation: a business that is supervised (by the FCA, HMRC, the Gambling Commission or a professional body) asks what information its supervisor collects under regulation 51 (line 1715)
-- about its supervision, and whether it is counted.  The Schedule lists the information to collect; it imposes nothing on the business.  The items are unnumbered in the text:
-- `item N` is the N-th printed item.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 4 item 1 (line 3207): "(“supervised persons”)".
@export Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts?
GIVEN `I am subject to the supervision of my supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to the supervision of your supervisory authority?
      `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your supervisory authority a self-regulatory organisation (a professional body that supervises its own members)?
      `I am a member of that self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation, are you one of its members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 item 1, am I a supervised person whom my supervisory authority counts` IS
    `sch 4 item 1 the person is a supervised person` `I am subject to the supervision of my supervisory authority` `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` `I am a member of that self-regulatory organisation`

-- Schedule 4, the items together (lines 3207-3241).
@export Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information?
GIVEN `the position of the item in the printed order` IS A NUMBER @desc Which item of Schedule 4 do you mean, counting the printed items from 1 (the text prints no numbers)?
      `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your supervisory authority a self-regulatory organisation (a professional body that supervises its own members)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4, is my supervisory authority asked for an item of the supervisory information` IS
    `sch 4 the item is asked of the supervisory authority` `the position of the item in the printed order` `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation`

-- Schedule 4 item 17 (line 3235): "A copy of any suspicious activity disclosure ... the supervisory authority or any of its supervised persons has made to the NCA."
@export Under schedule 4 item 17, is my supervisory authority asked for a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure that I have made to the NCA?
GIVEN `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your supervisory authority a self-regulatory organisation (a professional body that supervises its own members)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 item 17, is my supervisory authority asked for a copy of a suspicious activity disclosure that I have made to the NCA` IS
    `sch 4 the item is asked of the supervisory authority` 17 `my supervisory authority is a self-regulatory organisation`

-- Schedule 4 item 6 (lines 3215-3219).
@export Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk?
GIVEN `the level of risk at which the authority rates the firm` IS A `sch 4 risk rating` @desc At which level of risk does your supervisory authority rate the firm?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under schedule 4 item 6, under which limb is a firm counted that my supervisory authority considers to be at a given level of risk` IS
    `sch 4 item 6 the limb that counts firms of that rating` `the level of risk at which the authority rates the firm`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 5 -- who is a connected person of my business (lines 3242-3255)`
-- Situation: a relevant person (or a payment service provider) asks whether someone is a "connected person" of it, that is whether its supervisory authority may require
-- that person to give information (regulation 66(1), line 2217) and whether that person must help a skilled person (line 2401).  The roles are facts about the person; "officer" is not a defined term in this
-- Schedule (regulation 3(1), line 88: "officer", except in Part 8 and Schedule 5), so each role is answered as it is ordinarily understood.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 5, paragraphs 1 to 4 together (SEAM S-16, answering).
@export Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business?
GIVEN `the legal form of my business` IS A `Form of customer` @desc What is the legal form of your business?
      `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: an officer of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: a manager of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: an officer of a parent undertaking of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: a manager of a parent undertaking of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: an employee of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: an agent of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: an agent of a parent undertaking of my business?
      `the person is, or has been, a member of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person described in this way: a member of my business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5, is this person a connected person of my business` IS
    `sch 5 the person is a connected person of the relevant person` `the legal form of my business` (`sch 5 roles of the person` WITH `officer of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, an officer of my business`, `manager of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, a manager of my business`, `officer of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, an officer of a parent undertaking of my business`, `manager of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, a manager of a parent undertaking of my business`, `employee of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, an employee of my business`, `agent of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, an agent of my business`, `agent of a parent undertaking of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, an agent of a parent undertaking of my business`, `member of the subject` IS `the person is, or has been, a member of my business`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 6 -- is a requirement a relevant requirement (lines 3256-3348)`
-- Situation: a business asks whether a requirement that binds it is one of the "relevant requirements" for which a penalty or censure can follow if it is contravened
-- (regulation 76(1), line 2454, and the offence in regulation 86(1), line 2644).  The Schedule lists them by instrument, Article or regulation, and paragraph of it; the rendering prints no paragraph numbers after the lead-in.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 6, the chapeau and limbs (a) to (c) together (SEAM S-17, answering).
@export Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement?
GIVEN `the instrument the requirement is in` IS A `sch 6 instrument` @desc In which instrument is the requirement: the funds transfer regulation, these Regulations, the UK auctioning regulations, or another?
      `the number of the Article or regulation as printed` IS A STRING @desc What is the number of the Article or regulation, as printed (for example 28, 45ZA)?
      `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole` IS A STRING @desc Which paragraph of it do you mean, written without brackets (for example 11)? Leave empty if you mean the Article or regulation as a whole.
      `on whom the requirement is imposed` IS A `sch 6 bearer` @desc On whom is the requirement imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6, is this requirement a relevant requirement` IS
    `sch 6 the provision is a relevant requirement` (`sch 6 requirement` WITH `instrument` IS `the instrument the requirement is in`, `number` IS `the number of the Article or regulation as printed`, `paragraph` IS `the paragraph of it as printed, or empty if you mean the whole`, `bearer` IS `on whom the requirement is imposed`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 6A -- the NCA and the financial intelligence unit (lines 3349-3390)`
-- Situation: a relevant person asks what the National Crime Agency, as the UK's financial intelligence unit, may do about information it holds.  Every duty in the
-- Schedule is the NCA's (or a UK competent authority's); there is no question for an official.  What it means to a relevant person is that the NCA may ask it for
-- information to answer a foreign unit's request (paragraph 5(a)), and that a request about it, if its head office is in another EEA state, goes to that state's unit
-- (paragraphs 13 to 15).  The paragraph numbers 5, 14 and 15 are derived from the Schedule's cross-references (the rendering prints 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 13 and 16 only).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 6A paragraph 5(a) (lines 3366-3367).
@export Under schedule 6A paragraph 5(a), may the NCA use its powers to seek an order from me for information?
GIVEN `a foreign financial intelligence unit has made a request to the NCA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the NCA received an external request for information from a foreign financial intelligence unit?
      `the NCA has no information that it considers relevant to the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the NCA hold no information that it considers relevant to that request?
      `the NCA suspects that I hold such information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the NCA suspect that your business holds information relevant to that request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6A paragraph 5(a), may the NCA use its powers to seek an order from me for information` IS
    `sch 6A para 5(a) the NCA may exercise its powers to seek an order for information from the relevant person` WITH `an external request is received` IS `a foreign financial intelligence unit has made a request to the NCA`, `the NCA does not possess information which it considers relevant to the external request` IS `the NCA has no information that it considers relevant to the request`, `the NCA suspects that a relevant person possesses such information` IS `the NCA suspects that I hold such information`

-- Schedule 6A paragraph 14 (line 3384), read with paragraph 13 (line 3383).
@export Under schedule 6A paragraph 14, must the NCA address a request for information about me to the foreign financial intelligence unit of the state of my head office?
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information about my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the NCA wish to obtain information concerning your business?
      `my business has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6A paragraph 14, must the NCA address a request for information about me to the foreign financial intelligence unit of the state of my head office` IS
    `sch 6A para 14 the NCA must address the request to the foreign FIU in the state of the head office` WITH `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS `the NCA wishes to obtain information about my business`, `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS `my business has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom`

-- Schedule 6A paragraph 15 (line 3385), read with paragraph 13.
@export Under schedule 6A paragraph 15, must the NCA's request to a foreign financial intelligence unit about me contain the facts, the reasons and the proposed use?
GIVEN `the NCA wishes to obtain information about my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the NCA wish to obtain information concerning your business?
      `my business has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your business have its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom?
      `the NCA makes a request to a foreign financial intelligence unit for information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the NCA made a request to a foreign financial intelligence unit for information about your business?
      `the NCA considers the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the NCA consider the information may be relevant for its performance of its financial intelligence unit functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6A paragraph 15, must the NCA's request to a foreign financial intelligence unit about me contain the facts, the reasons and the proposed use` IS
    `sch 6A para 15 the request must contain the relevant facts, the reasons and the proposed use` WITH `the NCA wishes to obtain information concerning a relevant person` IS `the NCA wishes to obtain information about my business`, `the relevant person has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom` IS `my business has its head office in an EEA state other than the United Kingdom`, `the NCA makes a request to a foreign FIU for information` IS `the NCA makes a request to a foreign financial intelligence unit for information`, `the NCA considers that the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions` IS `the NCA considers the information may be relevant for its performance of FIU functions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 6B -- changes in control of a registered cryptoasset business (lines 3391-3543)`
-- Situation: a cryptoasset exchange provider that is on the FCA's register (regulation 54(1A)), and its compliance officer, asking whether Part 12 of FSMA (control over
-- authorised persons) applies to it, which of two sets of changes to Part 12 applies, whether a person is acquiring, increasing or reducing control over it, and what the penalties
-- and the defence are.  Which set of changes applies depends on the day the business was entered on the register: before 25 October 2027 (paragraphs 1 and 2) or on or after it
-- (paragraphs 3 and 4).  The unamended Part 12 is not among the sources, so a section that the Schedule does not mention is reported as "not mentioned".
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 6B paragraph 1 (line 3393).
@export Under schedule 6B paragraph 1, does Part 12 of FSMA apply to my business with the modifications in paragraph 2?
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)?
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business included in the register the FCA maintains under regulation 54(1A)?
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your business included in that register?
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Part 12 of FSMA apply to your business anyway, without this Schedule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6B paragraph 1, does Part 12 of FSMA apply to my business with the modifications in paragraph 2` IS
    `sch 6B para 1 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 2` WITH `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)`, `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`, `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS `the date on which the business was included in the register`, `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`

-- Schedule 6B paragraph 3 (line 3494).
@export Under schedule 6B paragraph 3, does Part 12 of FSMA apply to my business with the modifications in paragraph 4?
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)?
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business included in the register the FCA maintains under regulation 54(1A)?
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your business included in that register?
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Part 12 of FSMA apply to your business anyway, without this Schedule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6B paragraph 3, does Part 12 of FSMA apply to my business with the modifications in paragraph 4` IS
    `sch 6B para 3 Part 12 of FSMA applies to the business with the modifications specified in paragraph 4` WITH `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)`, `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`, `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS `the date on which the business was included in the register`, `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`

-- Schedule 6B paragraphs 1 and 3 together (gathered by hand).
@export Under schedule 6B paragraphs 1 and 3, which set of changes to Part 12 of FSMA applies to my business?
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)?
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business included in the register the FCA maintains under regulation 54(1A)?
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your business included in that register?
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Part 12 of FSMA apply to your business anyway, without this Schedule?
GIVETH A `sch 6B the set of modifications`
DECIDE `Under schedule 6B paragraphs 1 and 3, which set of changes to Part 12 of FSMA applies to my business` IS
    `sch 6B paras 1 and 3 which set of modifications applies` WITH `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)`, `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`, `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS `the date on which the business was included in the register`, `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business`

-- Schedule 6B paragraphs 2 and 4 (lines 3394-3537): the tables of modifications.
@export Under schedule 6B paragraphs 2 and 4, how does the Schedule treat a section of Part 12 of FSMA for my business?
GIVEN `the business is a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business a cryptoasset exchange provider within the meaning of regulation 14A(1)?
      `the business is included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your business included in the register the FCA maintains under regulation 54(1A)?
      `the date on which the business was included in the register` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your business included in that register?
      `Part 12 of FSMA would otherwise apply to the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Part 12 of FSMA apply to your business anyway, without this Schedule?
      `the section of Part 12 of FSMA` IS A STRING @desc Which section of Part 12 of FSMA do you mean (for example 190A)?
GIVETH A `sch 6B treatment of a section`
