-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Schedule 7 -- rules inserted into other instruments (lines 3544-3794)`
-- Situation: most of Schedule 7 changes words in other Acts and orders, and is inert.  Three paragraphs insert rules that stand alone and touch a business or its customer:
-- the right of a person wrongly identified as a politically exposed person to complain to the ombudsman (paragraph 3(2)), the estate agent that cannot complete customer due
-- diligence (paragraph 12), and bearer shares in an open-ended investment company (paragraph 18).  The host provisions are not among the sources, so a case outside the inserted words answers NOTHING.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Schedule 7 paragraph 3(2): section 226(7A) to (7C) of FSMA as inserted (lines 3555-3563).
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain?
GIVEN `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business identify the person as a politically exposed person?
      `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business identify the person as a family member of a politically exposed person?
      `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your business identify the person as a known close associate of a politically exposed person?
      `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person complain that the person was incorrectly identified in that way?
      `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person complain about something your business did or failed to do because of that identification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3(2), must the ombudsman rules make a person we identified as politically exposed eligible to complain` IS
    `sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person`) (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)`)

